\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 South Carolina Supreme Court Upholds Six-Week  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban; Newly constituted all-male court reverses itself from a ruling earlier this year\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 733 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 August 2023\par 18:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 South Carolina's highest court upheld a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after about six weeks of pregnancy, a long-awaited victory for Republicans who faced repeated hurdles in their efforts to further restrict the procedure since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2  in June 2022.\par \par \uc2 The 4-to-1 decision effectively reverses a ruling from earlier this year, in which the court had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/south-carolinas-6-week-abortion-ban-ruled-unconstitutional-11672940087"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down a so-called fetal heartbeat law  }}}\uc2  banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the early weeks of pregnancy on the basis that it violated a privacy guarantee in the state constitution. The decision significantly reduces \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in South Carolina, one of a few Southern states that had\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 maintained robust \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Justice John Kittredge, writing for the majority, said that while the six-week ban "infringes on a woman's right of privacy and bodily autonomy," it was the role of the state legislature to make policy decisions. Lawmakers determined that a woman's right "does not outweigh the interest of the unborn child to live" after a certain point in pregnancy, he said.\par \par \uc2 "Through the legal and judicial lens under which we must operate, while mindful of the difficult and emotional issue before us, we cannot say as a matter of law that the 2023 Act is unreasonable and thus violates the state constitution," Kittredge wrote.\par \par \uc2 After the South Carolina Supreme Court struck down a prior six-week ban in January, the female justice who authored that opinion retired. That cleared the way for the state legislature to appoint a replacement, giving South Carolina the only all-male state supreme court in the country.\par \par \uc2 The legislature then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-restrictions-pass-across-u-s-as-republicans-overcome-divisions-331d7d31?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a new six-week ban  }}}\uc2 , over the objections of some female Republican legislators, sending the issue quickly back up to the high court.\par \par \uc2 South Carolina Gov. \uc2 Henry McMaster\uc2  , a Republican, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/henrymcmaster/status/1694348395962360169"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called the decision  }}}\uc2  Wednesday a "historic moment" for the state and a result years in the making.\par \par \uc2 The law will limit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access not just for South Carolinians but those across the region who have traveled to the state over the last year as bans took effect elsewhere, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights leaders said Wednesday. The law will force many residents to "remain pregnant against their will," said Jenny Black, president and chief executive of Planned Parenthood South Atlantic, one of the plaintiffs that challenged the law.\par \par \uc2 The events in South Carolina underscore how volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights could remain for years to come. Unlike \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  justices, state supreme court justices are often elected and typically don't have lifetime tenure. That potentially tees up repeated legal battles when the composition of the courts changes. In Iowa the legislature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/iowa-lawmakers-pass-six-week-abortion-ban-14a937df"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a six-week ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 this summer, just weeks after the state's highest court deadlocked on whether to revive a 2018 law, leaving a permanent block in place.\par \par \uc2 Thomas Hydrick, an attorney for South Carolina, had argued in a hearing in late June that the prior decision hadn't been binding on future legislation. He argued that Justice John Cannon Few, who was one of the votes in the majority, had left open the door for the legislature to ban the procedure after six weeks if it adequately considered whether that gives women sufficient time to end a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Few, the justice, voted to uphold the law in the state Supreme Court's decision Wednesday. He wrote in his concurrence that lawmakers had made "a sincere attempt to comply with the narrowest reading of this Court's ruling."\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice Donald Beatty, who dissented, said the 2023 law "effectively reinstated" the struck-down law and failed to clarify when the ban applies during pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 "The majority has abandoned the precedent established just months earlier by this Court and, despite its insistence otherwise, has turned a blind eye to the obvious fact that the 2021 Act and the 2023 Act are the same," Beatty wrote. "The result will essentially force an untold number of affected women to give birth without their consent. I am hard-pressed to think of a greater governmental intrusion by a political body."\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at \par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230823ej8n00439\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
