\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 GOP Voters Urge 2024 Candidates to Hold Firm on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Limits; Republican hopefuls have to contend with a party base that is more conservative on the issue than many Americans\b0\par\par\uc2 By Catherine Lucey and Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 890 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 August 2023\par 14:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CAMBRIDGE, Iowa\u8212\'20\'14Iowa Republicans, who will cast the first ballots in the 2024 presidential primary, are pressing candidates to hold firm on their antiabortion stands, despite {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/ohio-vote-is-another-warning-to-gop-on-abortion-89ffe3a8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent election losses }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Laura Carlson, 60, of Story City, Iowa, said "no abortions would be preferable for me."\par \par \uc2 "I'm OK with a six-week or heartbeat ban," said Carlson, who serves for the Iowa Federation of Republican Women and volunteers for a support group for women with unplanned pregnancies. "No weakening, no."\par \par \uc2 The GOP presidential candidates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-other-gop-2024-hopefuls-struggle-to-define-abortion-message-71fed983"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have taken differing approaches on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  as they contend with a party base that is more conservative on the issue than many Americans. Some have backed a 15-week national ban, others have said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be left to the states. Florida Gov. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis }}}\uc2  and former President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  have avoided committing to a national ban, and Trump has warned that extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions could hinder Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Sheryl Soden, a retiree in her 70s from Ames, Iowa, said she understood the former president's caution. "I think he's walking a fine line," she said. "There are a lot of people out there that are against the six-week ban. I know he's pro-life, but he's trying to reach as many people as he can."\par \par \uc2 Democrats see \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights as a potent issue in the 2024 election that could boost them in swing states like Michigan, Wisconsin and Pennsylvania. Recent polling indicates most Americans favor some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/506759/broader-support-abortion-rights-continues-post-dobbs.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May Gallup poll }}}\uc2 showed that 34% say it should be legal under any circumstances, 51% say it should be legal under "certain circumstances" and 13% say it should be illegal in all circumstances.\par \par \uc2 The divide between the political parties was clear in the survey. Among Republicans, 66% thought {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-dobbs-year-after-roe-support-politics-d1ef5a5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Dobbs decision overturning Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 , which granted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, was a good thing, compared with 33% of Independents and 12% of Democrats.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups have won on six ballot measures since the overturning of Roe and are looking to put the issue on the ballot in more states next year. Democrats also scored some victories in the 2022 midterm elections in races that focused on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the re-election of Michigan Gov. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 . Earlier this month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/ohio-election-abortion-issue-one-vote-d7df6402"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio voters rejected a ballot measure }}}\uc2  that would have made it harder to add \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/election-day-ballots-ohio-abortion-maine-texas-colorado-d9922480"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to the state's constitution }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The issue doesn't always cut the Democrats' way. Several GOP governors handily won re-election last year after backing strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limits, including Govs. \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  of Georgia and Greg Abbott of Texas. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-restrictions-pass-across-u-s-as-republicans-overcome-divisions-331d7d31"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican-led states continue to pass new \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  restrictions }}}\uc2 , like bans on the procedure after six weeks of pregnancy. Iowa Republicans passed a six-week ban last month, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/iowas-six-week-abortion-ban-halted-by-court-4eed4e92"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a state judge has blocked it }}}\uc2 , opening up a legal battle that will likely be settled at the state's Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Dannenfelser, president of Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America, a politically powerful antiabortion group, said Republicans and business groups failed to deliver on a promised advertising and get-out-the-vote effort in Ohio and that she doesn't see the result as a reflection on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics more broadly or a warning about 2024 races.\par \par \uc2 "There should be no pro-life defeat takeaway message" from the Ohio ballot loss, she said.\par \par \uc2 Dannenfelser also said it is critical to get Republican presidential candidates talking about the issue in a forceful way or it will signal the party is in retreat on the issue, which could hurt the antiabortion side in coming ballot fights in Ohio, Arizona and other states.\par \par \uc2 "What happens on that debate stage will affect state ballot initiatives. A head in the sand will communicate expectant losses and that is not to be abided," she said, referring to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/business/media/fox-news-republican-gop-debate-donald-trump-9177b7dd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the first GOP primary debate }}}\uc2  next week in Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How should the Republican Party approach \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  going forward? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 In interviews, Iowa Republicans largely didn't call for a specific standard, but stressed that they wanted strong antiabortion candidates. Some, including Carlson, said they would prefer that the issue remains at the state level. "It's not a federal issue, it's a state issue," said Ginny Mitchell, from Boone, Iowa. "There shouldn't be a national ban."\par \par \uc2 Other Iowa voters stressed that while \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a priority, the candidates should focus on a broad array of issues. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is very important, but there are other issues that are going to carry the Republicans," said Barb Corson, a 64-year-old retiree from Waverly, Iowa, citing jobs and border security.\par \par \uc2 Lynn Paris, 66, a retiree from Muscatine, Iowa, and a registered Republican, said he supports Trump and that he wasn't concerned that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be a turnoff for voters in the general election.\par \par \uc2 Paris called Trump a fighter: "I think he'll keep the issues in the forefront that are important to voters, like the economy, and on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he'll stick to his guns."\par \par \uc2 Write to Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230819ej8j000p2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
