\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Appeals Panel Rules \uc2 FDA\uc2  Improperly Expanded Access to  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Pill; Ruling sets stage for potential review by the Supreme Court, which has allowed broad access to mifepristone while litigation continues\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 754 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 August 2023\par 22:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A federal appeals panel ruled that the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  improperly expanded access to the widely used \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone over the last seven years but left in place the drug's original approval, teeing up the issue for review by the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 The ruling by a three-judge panel of the New Orleans-based Fifth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals is the latest twist in a case that has at times {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-pill-ruling-ignites-new-national-battle-a9c03329"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened to pull the pill }}}\uc2  from the market nationwide.\par \par \uc2 The appeals panel said pill opponents who sued the \uc2 FDA\uc2  had likely waited too long to challenge the drug's original approval in 2000, and it also left in place the agency's 2019 approval of the generic version of the pill. But the court said the \uc2 FDA\uc2  failed to properly scrutinize changes that eased access to mifepristone in recent years, such as allowing the drug to be administered without an in-person visit with a medical provider.\par \par \uc2 In expanding access to the drug, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  inadequately weighed whether the changes would make taking the drug riskier and neglected to follow up by collecting detailed data on the prevalence of serious complications, the judges said.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 FDA\uc2  failed to account for the fact that it was about to significantly loosen mifepristone's conditions for use. At no point during the decision did the agency acknowledge that the 2016 Amendments might alter the risk profile," wrote Judge Jennifer Walker Elrod, an appointee of \uc2 George W. Bush\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 All three judges on the panel were appointed by Republican presidents. One, Judge James Ho, a Trump appointee, issued a partial dissent saying he would have gone further and set aside the drug's original approval. He said the agency violated its own rules by using an approval process designed for medications used to treat serious or life-threatening illness. Pregnancy, he said, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-battle-returns-to-the-courtroom-b163f075"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is not an illness }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The appeals court decision doesn't have immediate practical consequences because the Supreme Court in April issued an order allowing current broad levels of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-faces-fresh-deadline-in-abortion-pill-case-6d7b9049"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 access to mifepristone }}}\uc2  while litigation proceeds. That is likely to ensure availability for months.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit, brought by antiabortion medical associations and individual doctors represented by the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , has drawn national attention because it has the potential to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access even in states with strong protections for the procedure. The challengers sued the \uc2 FDA\uc2  late last year, arguing the agency improperly approved the pill and inadequately considered potential safety concerns about the drug.\par \par \uc2 "It puts the \uc2 FDA\uc2  on notice and may give women a reason to think twice about taking mifepristone unsupervised," Erin Hawley, an attorney with the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , said of the Wednesday decision.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department, defending the \uc2 FDA\uc2 , said the pill's approval\u8212\'20\'14and subsequent government expansion of its availability\u8212\'20\'14was supported by decades of research about the pill's safety and efficacy.\par \par \uc2 The department said it strongly disagreed with the decision and would appeal to the Supreme Court, adding that it was committed to "protecting Americans' access to safe and effective reproductive care."\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has faced a series of case setbacks in front of conservative lower courts.\par \par \uc2 U.S. District Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk, a Trump appointee in Amarillo, Texas, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-approval-suspended-by-u-s-judge-3c5c88cf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 initially issued a sweeping ruling in April }}}\uc2  suspending approval of the pill, though it never took effect.\par \par \uc2 Previously, a different Fifth Circuit three-judge panel issued an interim order that narrowed Kacsmaryk's ruling somewhat, while still returning restrictions on the drug to what they were before 2016. Back then, the pill could be used only through about seven weeks of pregnancy, required three in-person doctor visits and couldn't be sent to patients through the mail. Wednesday's ruling puts in place a similar set of restrictions.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -pill supporters said Wednesday's ruling underscores the precariousness of the pill's future. The case could present the first big test for the Supreme Court on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it overruled Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  and withdrew constitutional protection for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 "The 5th Circuit's opinion makes it clear that mifepristone's approval is very much still at risk, as is the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's independence," said \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , president of \uc2 Planned Parenthood Federation of America\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Liz Essley Whyte contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230816ej8g005sd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
