\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Rights Supporters Score Win as Ohio Voters Defeat Issue 1; Measure would have made it harder to pass amendments to state constitution, including one on November ballot guaranteeing  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kris Maher \par \uc2 965 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 August 2023\par 15:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters were gathering signatures this spring for a constitutional amendment to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in Ohio's constitution. An earlier version of this article incorrectly said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents were gathering the signatures. (Corrected on Aug. 8)\par \par \uc2 Voters in Ohio defeated a measure that would have made it harder to change the state constitution, according to the Associated Press, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/election-day-ballots-ohio-abortion-maine-texas-colorado-d9922480"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a win for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -rights supporters }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The defeat of the measure known as Issue 1 means a proposed constitutional amendment on the November ballot enshrining {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access }}}\uc2  faces a lower bar for passage. Issue 1 would have made all future constitutional amendments receive at least 60% support to be adopted, instead of the current rule requiring a simple majority.\par \par \uc2 With nearly all ballots counted, 57% voted against Issue 1 and 43% in favor, according to the AP.\par \par \uc2 The contest, which featured millions of dollars of advertisements for both sides, was the latest fight over state-level \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  overturned Roe v. Wade last year, ending the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ohio is one of several Republican-dominated states to vote with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -rights supporters }}}\uc2 , following Kansas and Kentucky last year.\par \par \uc2 The state's Republican-controlled legislature voted this spring to put Issue 1 on the ballot in an August special election. At the time, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters were gathering signatures for their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/ohio-abortion-rights-coalition-begins-push-for-constitutional-amendment-9ab5d752"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 constitutional amendment }}}\uc2 , which last month was approved for the November ballot by the secretary of state.\par \par \uc2 The 60% threshold for constitutional amendments set by Issue 1 could have proven decisive for November's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ballot measure. A July poll by the USA Today Network and \uc2 Suffolk University\uc2  found that 58% of likely voters in Ohio supported it.\par \par \uc2 Voters in different parts of the state said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was top of mind as they voted on Issue 1.\par \par \uc2 Karen Kopack, a 56-year-old Democrat in Mason, Ohio, and mother of three, said she voted against the measure because she views it as government overreach aimed at limiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 "It's going to effectively end any citizen-led initiative in the state," Kopack said.\par \par \uc2 Ruth Edmonds, 59, a Republican who works for the Center for Christian Virtue, a faith-based, public-policy organization, said she voted for Issue 1 because she doesn't want special-interest groups funding campaigns to bypass the legislature and change the state constitution on issues like \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. "I think the issue of life is superior to all other issues," she said.\par \par \uc2 Issue 1, which needed a simple majority to pass, also would have required citizens who want to put an amendment on the ballot to get signatures from each of the state's 88 counties\u8212\'20\'14instead of 44 currently\u8212\'20\'14and eliminated a 10-day period in which signatures deemed faulty can be replaced.\par \par \uc2 Dennis Willard, a spokesman for One Person One Vote, the primary group advocating against Issue 1, said in a statement, "The majority still rules in Ohio, and the people's power has been preserved."\par \par \uc2 Protect Our Constitution, a leading proponent, issued a statement that said in part, "Though these are not the results we hoped for, our coalition looks forward to working with the General Assembly on policy for the betterment of all Ohioans, in a manner that honors and respects the legislative process\u8212\'20\'14not circumvents it."\par \par \uc2 Voters have favored \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in referendums in half a dozen states since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  overturned Roe v. Wade in June 2022.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, a coalition of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups in Arizona submitted language to the secretary of state to amend that state's constitution to protect the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until a doctor has determined fetal viability, which typically occurs around 22 to 24 weeks. Abortions would be allowed after that cutoff if a healthcare provider determines the procedure is necessary to protect the life or health of the mother.\par \par \uc2 Supporters will need to gather 383,923 signatures to put that amendment on the ballot next year. Arizona law currently bans most abortions after 15 weeks.\par \par \uc2 In Ohio, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now legal up to 22 weeks of pregnancy. Last year, after the Supreme Court decision, a 2019 law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at six weeks took effect in Ohio. In September, a state judge issued an injunction blocking it while litigation proceeds.\par \par \uc2 Supporters said Issue 1 was needed to keep out-of-state special interest groups from bypassing the legislature on a range of issues, such as redistricting or raising the minimum wage. Opponents said it was primarily aimed at keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights amendment from passing.\par \par \uc2 The state GOP, antiabortion advocates and business groups that supported Issue 1 faced off against state Democrats, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups and labor groups.\par \par \uc2 One Person One Vote has raised $14.8 million, according to the latest available campaign-finance records. Protect Our Constitution and another group that supported Issue 1, Protect Women Ohio, have raised a combined $14.5 million.\par \par \uc2 Nearly 700,000 people voted early or by mail in Tuesday's special election, according to Ohio's secretary of state, far outpacing earlier August elections. Last year, about 150,000 people voted early in an August primary.\par \par \uc2 November's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measure states that every individual "has a right to make and carry out one's own reproductive decisions." It also states that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be prohibited after fetal viability, except when a physician deems it necessary to protect a patient's life or health.\par \par \uc2 Eliza Collins and Laura Kusisto contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Kris Maher at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Kris.Maher@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kris.Maher@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230808ej8800231\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
