\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 House Passes Defense Bill With  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 , Transgender Provisions; Democrats drop support for NDAA after GOP added 'culture war' amendments\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lindsay Wise, Isaac Yu and Simon J. Levien \par \uc2 1,363 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2023\par 20:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14The Republican-controlled House narrowly passed a $886 billion defense-policy bill loaded with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/house-gop-threatens-to-derail-defense-bill-over-abortion-transgender-care-1c7dfe7a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 measures restricting \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access, transgender healthcare and diversity }}}\uc2  efforts in the military, as House Speaker Kevin McCarthy kept his party largely united amid strong Democratic opposition.\par \par \uc2 The vote was 219-210, with just four Republicans and four Democrats crossing party lines. The Senate is working to pass its own version, and then lawmakers will work behind closed doors to come up with a compromise that must clear both chambers before heading to President Biden's desk for his signature.\par \par \uc2 The National Defense Authorization Act for fiscal year 2024 would authorize a 5.2% pay raise for troops and funding for new barracks, combat ships and drones, create a Space National Guard, and establish a new Special Inspector General for Ukraine Security Assistance to oversee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/u-s-watchdogs-want-to-deploy-staff-to-ukraine-war-zone-to-track-arms-aid-up-close-c61b09b3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 audits of all U.S. aid provided to Ukraine }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It also would authorize $300 million in security assistance for Ukraine and $600 million more than the Biden administration had requested to respond to security threats in the Indo-Pacific region.\par \par \uc2 The vote marked a victory for the hard-line House Freedom Caucus, whose members hailed it as their latest success in shifting the House rightward. The passage also notched a win for McCarthy, who held his rowdy conference together by appeasing conservatives and striking side deals with individual lawmakers, an approach that will be tested again later this year when the NDAA is finalized.\par \par \uc2 Republican leaders said the adoption of the GOP amendments on polarizing issues, many of them championed by members of the Freedom Caucus, would keep the military focused on protecting the country rather than what they see as progressive social-policy distractions.\par \par \uc2 "We don't want Disneyland training our military," McCarthy, a California Republican, said of the social-policy amendments. Majority Whip Rep. \uc2 Tom Emmer\uc2  (R., Minn) said the GOP was delivering on its promise to cut out the "woke garbage" from the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 Infuriated Democrats said Republicans had hitched their own divisive agenda to what is typically a bipartisan bill, and warned that Republicans in competitive districts could pay a price in the 2024 elections. Only a handful of Democrats sided with Republicans on the series of amendments ahead of the final vote.\par \par \uc2 "Extreme MAGA Republicans have hijacked a bipartisan bill that is essential to our national security\u8230\'20\'26and weaponized it to jam their extreme right wing ideology down the throats of the American people," said House Minority Leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  (D., N.Y.), proceeding to tick off names of Republicans in competitive districts who voted in favor of the contentious amendments.\par \par \uc2 The vote again showed the unstable and unpredictable nature of the House, in which McCarthy can lose no more than four Republicans without Democratic support. Ahead of the vote, Rep. Scott Perry (R., Pa.), the chair of the Freedom Caucus, said the group wasn't taking an official position on the bill, even after the House adopted some amendments it championed. Walking onto the floor, many Republicans said they were uncertain how the vote was going to turn out.\par \par \uc2 "We're going to have some fun today," quipped Emmer, the chief vote counter, when asked if Republicans had enough support. "Are you optimistic now?" joked Rep. \uc2 Garret Graves\uc2  (R., La.) to reporters, minutes ahead of the final vote.\par \par \uc2 In the end, most of the Freedom Caucus's roughly three dozen members backed the bill. Only four Republicans voted no: Freedom Caucus members Andy Biggs of Arizona, \uc2 Ken Buck\uc2  of Colorado and Eli Crane of Arizona, as well as \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2  of Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 On the other side, four Democrats from competitive swing districts voted to support the bill: Reps. Don Davis of North Carolina, Jared Golden of Maine, Marie Gluesenkamp Perez of Washington and Gabe Vasquez of New Mexico.\par \par \uc2 Typically centrists from both parties come together to ensure the NDAA passes by large margins. With the amendments turning off Democrats, McCarthy needed to keep almost every Republican on board to win a majority. For some conservatives, it was the first time in their careers that they had voted to pass a defense-policy bill.\par \par \uc2 With this NDAA, "we have crushed this social experiment that they have been conducting," said Rep. \uc2 Matt Rosendale\uc2  (R., Mont.), who backed the defense-policy bill after voting against it last year. "This is how Congress is supposed to work."\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What do you think of the provisions included in the defense-policy bill? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Jennifer McClellan (D., Va), a member of the \uc2 House Armed Services Committee\uc2 , said the bill would have detrimental impacts on hundreds of thousands of servicemembers and their families. "Extreme MAGA Republicans have turned the NDAA into yet another vehicle to wage their culture wars," she said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  amendment, which passed largely along party lines, would bar the Secretary of Defense "from paying for or reimbursing expenses relating to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services."\par \par \uc2 The Pentagon currently grants troops leave and travel funds for reproductive healthcare outside the states where they are stationed, including for abortions or fertility treatment. Among the states with the most-restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies that are also home to major military installations are Texas, Louisiana and Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 Ronny Jackson\uc2  (R., Texas), a House Freedom Caucus member and retired Navy rear admiral who sponsored the amendment, said taxpayer money should be spent on national security, "not to promote and support the Biden administration's radical immoral pro \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  agenda."\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 Chrissy Houlahan\uc2  (D., Pa.), an Air Force veteran, said Democrats will keep fighting to protect service members' right to access abortions. "As someone who has worn the uniform, and has a uterus\u8212\'20\'14unlike many opining on this subject\u8212\'20\'14I'm furious," she said. [\par \par \uc2 Another amendment that also passed on a near party-line vote would prohibit the Defense Department or TRICARE, the military's healthcare program, from providing gender-related surgeries and hormone treatments for transgender people.\par \par \uc2 Transgender troops have been able to serve openly in the military since 2021, and advocacy groups say there are roughly 15,000 transgender service members.\par \par \uc2 Other amendments would eliminate all the offices and personnel dedicated to diversity in the Armed Forces and prohibit government properties from hoisting up unauthorized flags, taking aim at government sites that flew LGBTQ pride flags.\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 Tom Cole\uc2  (R., Okla.), the chairman of the \uc2 House Rules Committee\uc2 , argued that the hot-button amendments wouldn't have any effect on about 95% of the defense-policy bill, which runs more than 1,200 pages and deals with everything from military recruitment to nuclear weapons. Cole said the reality is that the final product will be bipartisan, and hinted that the most divisive provisions likely will be dropped.\par \par \uc2 "There is no way a Republican House and Democratic Senate and a Democratic president are going to do anything on any issue that's not essentially bipartisan," Cole said.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy and his leadership team won over on-the-fence Republicans by making promises addressing some of their concerns. He gave Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  (R., Ga.) a spot on a conference committee charged with ironing out differences between House and Senate versions of the NDAA.\par \par \uc2 Greene expressed unhappiness with the failure of amendments that would have stripped Ukraine aid out of the NDAA, but voted for the bill anyway, with the caveat that she would continue to push for a final version of the defense-policy bill to include such a provision.\par \par \uc2 "I let him know it would be my red line," she said she told McCarthy.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy also suggested that he agreed to a September vote related to the 2001 authorization-for-use of military force, in a nod to the GOP lawmakers who were unhappy that GOP leaders blocked an amendment vote on repealing the 2001 use-of-force measure.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14Siobhan Hughes contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Lindsay Wise at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:lindsay.wise@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lindsay.wise@wsj.com }}}\uc2 , Isaac Yu at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:isaac.yu@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 isaac.yu@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Simon J. Levien at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:simon.levien@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 simon.levien@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230714ej7e002bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
