\par \par \uc2 Iowa Gov. \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2  said she would sign a bill banning most abortions after about six weeks of pregnancy. PHOTO: KC McGinnis for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers filed a challenge to a newly passed Iowa bill that would ban the procedure after about six weeks of pregnancy, setting up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-state-guide-laws-bf5072da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new legal battle }}}\uc2  just weeks after the state's highest court stalemated over a similar law.\par \par \uc2 The providers' lawsuit filed on Wednesday said the new bill, passed in a special session a day earlier, is virtually identical to a 2018 state law that had been permanently blocked by a lower court, a decision that the Iowa Supreme Court in June allowed to remain in place after the justices deadlocked on whether to revive that law.\par \par \uc2 The justices said, however, they could reconsider the issue if the legislature enacted a new law in the wake of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-dobbs-year-after-roe-support-politics-d1ef5a5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the U.S. Supreme Court decision }}}\uc2  a year ago eliminating a federal constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Following the decision, Iowa Gov. \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2 , a Republican, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://governor.iowa.gov/press-release/2023-07-05/gov-reynolds-calls-special-session-enact-pro-life-legislation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called a special session }}}\uc2  to enact a new ban. The governor said she would sign the bill Friday.\par \par \uc2 "The Iowa Supreme Court questioned whether this legislature would pass the same law they did in 2018, and today they have a clear answer," Reynolds said in a statement Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The bill, which is set to take effect immediately after the governor signs it, would sharply curtail \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state. It makes exceptions for rape if reported to a law enforcement agency or certain medical personnel within 45 days, incest, medical emergencies, and fatal fetal abnormalities.\par \par \uc2 Iowa joins some 14 other states that have banned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many or most abortions }}}\uc2  since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  last June. Nearby states including Missouri and South Dakota have banned the procedure. Kansas, where voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-abortion-vote-results-11659440554"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected a proposal }}}\uc2  to end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections in a statewide referendum last year, saw a steep increase in abortions from out-of-state patients between 2021 and 2022, state data show.\par \par \uc2 Following the loss of a federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , advocates have turned to state supreme courts seeking protections for the procedure. They have had some wins in places such as South Carolina and Oklahoma. But it is unclear how lasting those decisions will be from state supreme courts, which are made up of justices who generally serve set terms and are often elected. All seven of the justices on the Iowa Supreme Court were appointed by Republican governors.\par \par \uc2 In South Carolina, state Republicans this spring {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/judge-blocks-south-carolina-six-week-abortion-ban-3a31e2f3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a six-week ban }}}\uc2  following a decision by their state's highest court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/south-carolinas-6-week-abortion-ban-ruled-unconstitutional-11672940087?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 striking down a nearly identical law }}}\uc2 . The justice who wrote the opinion subsequently retired and Republicans are hopeful that the newly constituted court could reverse itself and uphold the new law.\par \par \uc2 In their lawsuit on Wednesday, Iowa providers are seeking a broader ruling from the high court than the largely procedural one it issued last month. They argue that the ban imposes an undue burden by banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before many women know they are pregnant and have time to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and violates an inalienable rights provision in the Iowa constitution providing protections for equality, life, liberty, safety and happiness.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Shannon Najmabadi at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:shannon.najmabadi@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shannon.najmabadi@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230712ej7c001xh\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
