\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Dannenfelser, president of Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America. PHOTO: Stephen Voss for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Republicans and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents are divided about whether to double down on their commitment to tight \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions or instead respond to public pushback by offering modest compromises.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma so far has decided not to budge, despite Lauinger's warning.\par \par \uc2 In the spring of 2022, a time of increasing expectation that Roe would be overturned, the state legislature passed three separate bills banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  through most or all of pregnancy. Republican state Sen. Julie Daniels co-authored two of them. Now she wants to add language to state law to ensure women can obtain abortions if their physical health, not just their life, is in danger, and to allow doctors to be able to provide abortions without criminal penalties to victims of rape and incest that have been reported to law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 Daniels said she is worried that unless her side compromises, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates could succeed with a potential ballot initiative that would undo her work. She pointed to a poll requested by Oklahomans for Life that showed just 4% of state voters supported a total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with only exceptions for the life of the mother, but that more than 70% support a ban with more exceptions.\par \par \uc2 "I have to act to try and shore up the protections that we have," she said.\par \par \uc2 Kristan Hawkins\uc2 , president of the national antiabortion group Students for Life of America, said her side shouldn't retreat. "We can't play a shell game with public opinion," Hawkins said. "We're going to have to make our case."\par \par \uc2 The effort to add exceptions in Oklahoma failed this legislative session. Then, in May, the state's Supreme Court struck down the two laws Daniels had co-written, saying they didn't comply with a right in the state constitution for women to obtain abortions in life-threatening situations.\par \par \uc2 Nationally, former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the front-runner for the GOP presidential nomination in 2024, has made some overtures to antiabortion groups but in other settings has said the Republican Party has suffered politically by taking extreme positions.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion leaders have praised Florida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  after he helped push behind the scenes for the state's recently adopted six-week ban. But DeSantis, often an unabashed culture warrior, for months didn't say much publicly about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In May he gave a 40-minute keynote address at an event hosted by a prominent state antiabortion group in which he didn't use the word \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A DeSantis spokesman pointed to a recent interview in which the governor said he was proud "to stand for a culture of life."\par \par \uc2 Legal victories for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups at the state level might prove more fragile than Roe was. That is because state supreme court justices generally serve a set term and must be re-elected or reappointed, opening the door for a shift in a court's political makeup.\par \par \uc2 Campaigns are under way in Florida and Ohio to gather enough signatures to place on the ballot constitutional amendments protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. In both states, proponents of the measures say they are outpacing their initial signature-gathering goals.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates also are considering putting the issue to voters in Missouri and Oklahoma, two of the states with the most robust history of restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. They say last year's successful campaign in Kansas taught them how to talk to voters in more conservative states, including by leaning heavily on messages about freedom from government interference. The antiabortion ballot measure there {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-vote-signals-abortion-could-emerge-as-top-political-issue-in-november-11659555741"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ultimately failed by 18 percentage points in a state Trump carried by nearly 15 points in 2020  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Clinics are struggling to devise sustainable business models. Providers have faced opposition in conservative pockets of states with otherwise liberal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/new-mexico-abortion-clinics-demand-1a888fa7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 such as New Mexico  }}}\uc2 . Some say it can be difficult to recruit and retain employees in Republican-led states, where job security can be affected by the shifting legal landscape. Clinics in places such as Florida are bracing to have their number of patients cut in half if new restrictions take effect.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
