\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Senate Confirms  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Rights Lawyer to U.S. Appeals Court; Biden nominee Julie Rikelman argued in Supreme Court case that overruled Roe v. Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 714 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 June 2023\par 23:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  on Tuesday confirmed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights lawyer Julie Rikelman to a U.S. appeals court, resolving a high-profile nomination by President Biden that had been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-nominates-lawyer-who-argued-supreme-court-abortion-case-to-judgeship-11659122157"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pending nearly a year }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Rikelman, 51 years old, will join the Boston-based First U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals, which has jurisdiction over four northeastern states, plus Puerto Rico. She has worked as an advocate for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights for more than a decade, most recently leading U.S. litigation for the \uc2 Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Representing a Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic at the Supreme Court, she was on the losing end of last year's ruling in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization }}}\uc2  that overruled Roe v. Wade and ended nearly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 50 years of constitutional protections }}}\uc2  for women seeking the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The Senate confirmed her on a 51-43 vote.\par \par \uc2 Rikelman is one of several {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-to-renominate-his-picks-for-judicial-and-diplomatic-posts-11672718861"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden judicial nominees }}}\uc2  who have been confirmed recently after languishing for many months. The Senate last week confirmed Dale Ho, an outspoken voting-rights attorney at \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2 , to the U.S. District Court for the Southern District of New York.\par \par \uc2 These nominees "were seen as really breaking the mold," said Marin K. Levy, a professor at Duke Law School. "Time passed and there's been a real interest in whether they would ultimately get to the bench."\par \par \uc2 Biden has made filling judicial vacancies a priority of his administration, aided by his party's retention of Senate control in the November midterms. Democrats have faced complications in recent months, however, as California Sen. \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2 , a Democrat who sits on the \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2 , was absent for health reasons.\par \par \uc2 The president has vowed to nominate candidates who would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/bidens-supreme-court-pledge-reflects-push-across-federal-judiciary-11643891401"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 diversify the federal judiciary }}}\uc2 , both in terms of demographics and professional experience. Of the more than 130 Biden judicial nominees confirmed so far, two-thirds are women and nearly 70% are people of color. He also has sought nominees who have done work in areas such as criminal defense and civil rights.\par \par \uc2 Biden remains on pace to make more judicial appointments during his first term than many of his predecessors but faces an uphill battle matching former President Trump's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-appointees-poised-to-influence-legal-outcomes-for-decades-to-come-11612112401"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record of appointments }}}\uc2  to the federal bench.\par \par \uc2 When Rikelman appeared before the \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2 , Republicans asked about her prior statements on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, including a report by the \uc2 Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  to which she contributed that called the Dobbs decision "callous" and "egregiously wrong."\par \par \uc2 Rikelman said her past statements were made in her role as an advocate, adding that she was committed to following Supreme Court precedent. "As a judge I will have a very different role. I understand that role because I always wanted to appear in front of fair and open minded judges who would follow the law," she said.\par \par \uc2 Rikelman was born in Ukraine to parents who immigrated to the U.S. after they experienced antisemitism in the former Soviet Union. She said in her confirmation hearing that her family's experience helped shape her views of the legal system.\par \par \uc2 "My family came to this country because of the rule of law. I understand what it's like based on that experience to not have faith in a government institution," she said.\par \par \uc2 Ho, who was nominated in September 2021, was one of the president's longest languishing judicial nominees. He was a prominent legal opponent of the Trump administration who argued high-profile cases on issues such as voter identification laws and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-dismisses-challenge-to-trump-plan-to-exclude-illegal-immigrants-from-congressional-reapportionment-11608305125"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 excluding unauthorized immigrants }}}\uc2  from the U.S. census.\par \par \uc2 At his confirmation hearing, Republicans questioned Ho on whether he could be a fair and impartial judge, pointing to statements he had made describing himself as a "wild-eyed sort of leftist" who "is accused sometimes of seeing racial discrimination everywhere I look."\par \par \uc2 Ho said he was referring to a caricature of how others might describe him and acknowledged that he had sometimes taken an overly combative tone on social media.\par \par \uc2 "I know that I've pushed the envelope," he said. "I do regret it."\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230620ej6k005v5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
