\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  Launches 2024 GOP Presidential Campaign, Questions Trump's Conservatism; North Dakota Gov. \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  also joins Republican field\b0\par\par\uc2 By John McCormick and Catherine Lucey \par \uc2 1,242 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 June 2023\par 19:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Former Vice President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/mike-pence?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Pence }}}\uc2  joined the 2024 Republican presidential nomination race Wednesday and immediately questioned the conservatism and leadership of his ex-boss, former President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2 . "When \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ran for president in 2016 he promised to govern as a conservative, and together we did just that," Pence said in his announcement speech. "But today, he makes no such promise." Pence challenged Trump's commitment to secure further \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions and suggested the former president was "retreating" on the issue, one central to many GOP primary voters.\par \par \uc2 "The sanctity of life has been our party's calling for half a century, long before \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was a part of it," he said. "Now, he treats it as an inconvenience, even blaming our election losses in 2022 on overturning Roe v. Wade." The former president nominated three justices to the Supreme Court, creating a conservative majority that overturned the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-other-gop-2024-hopefuls-struggle-to-define-abortion-message-71fed983"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More recently }}}\uc2 , he has expressed skepticism about any national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, as some Republicans have called for.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for Trump's campaign didn't immediately respond to an email seeking comment on Pence's criticisms.\par \par \uc2 Karoline Leavitt, spokeswoman for a super PAC backing Trump, said in a statement that "the question most GOP voters are asking themselves about Pence's candidacy is 'Why?'" Pence's entry {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/miami-mayor-francis-suarez-joins-2024-gop-presidential-nomination-race-1a28e7a1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 into the race }}}\uc2  came the same day as that of North Dakota Gov. \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 . After a flurry of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/chris-christie-to-enter-gop-presidential-race-as-chief-trump-antagonist-8d3a44a3?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 candidate announcements }}}\uc2  in May and early June, including one Tuesday by former New Jersey Gov. \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/whos-running-for-president-in-2024-adb754e2?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 GOP field appears to be mostly set }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former vice president launched his bid from Iowa, the state that starts the nomination process early next year. He plans to focus heavily on the state, where he has long been popular among the social conservatives and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gop-presidential-hopefuls-aim-to-gain-on-trump-by-wooing-evangelicals-2ea3187d?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 evangelical Christians }}}\uc2  who dominate its GOP caucuses.\par \par \uc2 "We can defend our liberties and give America a new beginning for life," Pence said. "But it will require new leadership\u8212\'20\'14in the White House and the Republican Party."\par \par \uc2 Trump leads national polls of Republicans, but nomination races have been known to deliver unexpected results, and GOP activists in states that host the first contests have expressed an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/iowa-republicans-are-open-to-names-other-than-donald-trump-or-ron-desantis-370c5fbd?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 openness to candidates }}}\uc2  other than Trump. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.realclearpolitics.com/epolls/2024/president/us/2024_republican_presidential_nomination-7548.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Surveys of the 2024 GOP }}}\uc2  primary field have shown Pence in the low single digits.\par \par \uc2 The latest entries add to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/first-republican-gop-debate-who-7f128142"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an already crowded field }}}\uc2  that also includes Florida Gov. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis }}}\uc2 , Sen. Tim Scott of South Carolina, former Arkansas Gov. \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2 , multimillionaire biotech company founder {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biotech-founder-vivek-ramaswamy-enters-gop-presidential-race-92accc7f?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy }}}\uc2  and Nikki Haley, a former South Carolina governor and United Nations ambassador.Pence, who turns 64 years old on the day of his announcement, cast himself as a conservative on economic, security and social issues. He has hawkish foreign-policy views that are at odds with some segments of the GOP, including advocating for strong {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/future-u-s-aid-to-ukraine-turns-on-kyivs-success-on-the-battlefield-1d4bac4e?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 U.S. support for Ukraine }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He has said he would support a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  at six weeks of pregnancy. And he has differed from some fellow Republicans by calling for changes to Medicare and Social Security to shore up their solvency.\par \par \uc2 Through nearly all of his four years serving as vice president, Pence was a loyal sidekick, standing by Trump during the investigations into Russian interference in the 2016 election, the impeachment of the president by the House and the tumultuous response to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-trump-sowed-covid-supply-chaos-try-getting-it-yourselves-11598893051?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 coronavirus pandemic }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He publicly broke with the former president, however, after the Capitol riot on Jan. 6, 2021. Pence {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/cheney-kinzinger-face-rnc-censure-vote-as-trump-rift-widens-11643993140?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to go along }}}\uc2  with Trump's effort to overturn the 2020 election, prompting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/jan-6-hearing-today-trump/card/trump-s-tweet-about-pence-seen-as-critical-moment-during-riot-fmPxoFkeoTKxi0NqPLCL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump to tweet }}}\uc2  that Pence "didn't have the courage to do what should have been done," and leading some Capitol rioters to call for his hanging. He was at the Capitol that day to certify {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden }}}\uc2 's victory and was rushed out as the mob {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-protesters-are-in-the-building-inside-the-capitol-stormed-by-a-pro-trump-mob-11609984654?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 swarmed the building }}}\uc2 . "On that fateful day, President Trump's words were reckless and he endangered my family and everyone at the Capitol," Pence said Wednesday in his speech. "On that day, President Trump also demanded that I choose between him and the Constitution. Now voters will be faced with the same choice. I chose the constitution and I always will."\par \par \uc2 While Pence wants to make a forward-looking pitch as a candidate, he continues to grapple with the riot's aftermath. In April, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/mike-pence-testifies-before-jan-6-grand-jury-investigating-donald-trump-6318d359?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he testified }}}\uc2  before a grand jury investigating Trump's efforts to remain in power after the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Arguing the country is ready for a fresh start, Pence is hoping to remind people of Trump-era policies, which he dubs "Trump-Pence," while offering a contrast with the former president's steady boil of controversy and election denialism.\par \par \uc2 Trump tapped Pence as his vice presidential pick in July 2016, hoping the then Indiana governor and former congressman and conservative radio talk-show host would appeal to Midwestern voters and traditional conservatives, in particular the religious right wing of the party.\par \par \uc2 Burgum, 66 years old, was first elected in 2016. He isn't well-known nationally and will face a challenge building name recognition in a field with much better-known candidates.\par \par \uc2 But he could use his fortune to help boost his prospects. Burgum built \uc2 Great Plains Software\uc2  from a small startup into a company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/SB986423710522507997"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 acquired by Microsoft }}}\uc2  for $1.1 billion in 2001.\par \par \uc2 Two people familiar with his planning told The Wall Street Journal late last month that he has always invested in his companies and campaigns and would do the same if he runs.\par \par \uc2 In an announcement speech Wednesday in front of several hundred in Fargo, N.D., Burgum stressed small-town values, his experience as a business executive and innovator, and familiarity with working-class jobs.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How do you expect \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 's presidential campaign will play out? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 "We need a leader who understands the real work that Americans do everyday, someone who has worked alongside our farmers, our ranchers and our small-business owners," he said. "Someone who has held jobs where you shower at the end of the day, not the beginning."\par \par \uc2 Known for a casual style and noninflammatory rhetoric, Burgum would stand in contrast to Trump and called for greater civility in politics.\par \par \uc2 "In a country built on neighbors helping neighbors, we've become a country of neighbors fighting neighbors," he said. "We should all be fighting to unite the country against our common enemies like China, Russia, Iran, North Korea and the drug cartels."\par \par \uc2 In April, Burgum signed into law a near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that permits the procedure in cases of rape and incest only in the first six weeks of pregnancy. The law also makes an exception in the case of a serious physical health risk to a mother.\par \par \uc2 He also signed legislation this year that prohibits public schools and government entities from requiring teachers and employees to refer to transgender people by the pronouns they use. The law also requires teachers to tell a parent or legal guardian if the student identifies as transgender, and prohibits transgender students from using the bathroom of their choice without prior approval from a parent or guardian.\par \par \uc2 Write to John McCormick at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:mccormick.john@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mccormick.john@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230607ej670015p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
