\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Where  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Is Legal and Where It Loses Protections Without Roe v. Wade;  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  access across the U.S. now depends on state laws after Supreme Court overturned 1973 decision that established constitutional right to an  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kara Dapena and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 1,334 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 May 2023\par 20:09 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court in June 2022 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124?"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 , the landmark 1973 decision that established the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The majority opinion in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s.wsj.net/public/resources/documents/dobbs-v-jackson-womens-health-organization-6-24-2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization }}}\uc2  upended nearly five decades of precedent and allowed stronger state restrictions to take effect\u8212\'20\'14including total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Lawmakers on both sides of the aisle had been preparing for the shift for years, bringing laws forward that further restrict or assert protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Now, because of a patchwork of state laws,\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/fall-of-roe-v-wade-upends-abortion-landscape-for-american-women-11656081225"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access varies widely }}}\uc2  depending on where someone lives.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/indiana-legislature-is-first-to-approve-abortion-bans-since-supreme-court-overturned-roe-v-wade-11659755538"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Indiana }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/west-virginia-passes-near-total-abortion-ban-11663107167"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 West Virginia }}}\uc2  were the first state legislatures to pass new bans on most abortions following the high court's decision. North Dakota lawmakers passed a new ban in April 2023. About a dozen states are currently enforcing laws that ban nearly all abortions. Seventeen states and Washington, D.C., have approved protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Some states have overlapping policies.\par \par \uc2 Where things stand as of May 31:\par \par \uc2 ________________________________\par \par \uc2 Trigger bans\par \par \uc2 Thirteen states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/states-prepare-to-quickly-implement-abortion-trigger-laws-11655385028"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have so-called trigger laws }}}\uc2 , which ban nearly all abortions and were designed to take effect in the event the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 The laws in three of those states\u8212\'20\'14Kentucky, Louisiana and South Dakota\u8212\'20\'14took effect immediately after the court's June 24, 2022, decision, while laws in Idaho, Tennessee and Texas were designed to take effect weeks later. Trigger laws elsewhere required certification from attorneys general, governors or other state officials to take effect. Penalties for providers who violate the laws also differ.\par \par \uc2 Shortly after the Supreme Court's ruling, Missouri Attorney General Eric Schmitt said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AGEricSchmitt/status/1540338042413944832?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he certified the court's decision }}}\uc2 , allowing the state's trigger law to take effect. Trigger laws in Arkansas and Utah also went into effect later in the day after action from state officials. Mississippi's ban took effect July 7, 2022.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights litigants quickly turned to state courts. Trigger laws in several states have gone into and out of effect following Dobbs, as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers challenge the law.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma in May 2022 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-governor-signs-abortion-ban-11653529937"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned nearly all abortions }}}\uc2  throughout pregnancy before the Supreme Court's decision. The law uses a novel strategy, first employed by Texas lawmakers, that deputizes citizens to enforce it. The 2021 Texas law bars \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedures after about six weeks of pregnancy. Court challenges {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rejects-emergency-request-to-block-texas-six-week-abortion-ban-11630556283"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have failed to block it }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ________________________________\par \par \uc2 Pre-Roe bans\par \par \uc2 Before the Supreme Court's 2022 decision, nine states had bans on the books that predated Roe v. Wade. They were unenforceable for nearly five decades, but, without Roe, some states have argued they could revive them.\par \par \uc2 In Arizona, a state court judge in September 2022 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/arizona-can-enforce-near-total-abortion-ban-blocked-for-50-years-judge-rules-11663976573"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lifted a 50-year-old block }}}\uc2 on a mid-19th-century law banning nearly all abortions in the state. A state appeals court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/arizona-appeals-court-blocks-territorial-era-abortion-law-11665194904"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporarily halted enforcement }}}\uc2  of the law two weeks later.\par \par \uc2 A judge in Michigan blocked the state from enforcing its dormant 91-year-old law banning most abortions, following lawsuits from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups and Democratic Gov. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 . Michigan voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-supporters-prevail-in-midterm-ballot-measures-11667986139"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved a constitutional amendment }}}\uc2  enshrining protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights on Nov. 8, nullifying the pre-Roe ban. The state repealed its pre-Roe ban in 2023.\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin Gov. Tony Evers, a Democrat, has repeatedly called on lawmakers to repeal the state's 1849 ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The law was still on the books in 2023.\par \par \uc2 ________________________________\par \par \uc2 Near-total bans\par \par \uc2 Five states passed near-total bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Supreme Court established constitutional protections. Those laws were previously blocked by court order. While lawmakers in the states are now able to resurrect the bans, that might not be necessary to achieve a similar effect. Arkansas, Louisiana, Oklahoma and Utah all have trigger laws on the books, and Alabama, Arkansas and Oklahoma have pre-Roe bans.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/alabama-governor-signs-abortion-ban-into-law-11557962972"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2019 Alabama law }}}\uc2  making it a felony for doctors to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any point during pregnancy\u8212\'20\'14with exceptions in cases when a mother has a serious health risk\u8212\'20\'14went into effect June 24, 2022, after a federal judge agreed to lift a previous injunction.\par \par \uc2 Indiana's legislature became the first state to pass a near-total ban on abortions following the Supreme Court's Dobbs decision. The law, signed by Republican Gov. Eric Holcomb on Aug. 5, 2022, shortly after lawmakers approved it, was temporarily blocked by an Indiana judge on Sept. 22\u8212\'20\'14about a week after it went into effect.\par \par \uc2 West Virginia lawmakers passed a ban on nearly all abortions in the state on Sept. 13, 2022. North Dakota Gov. Doug Burgum signed a similar law in April 2023.\par \par \uc2 ________________________________\par \par \uc2 Six- and eight-week bans\par \par \uc2 In the years leading up to the latest Supreme Court decision, several states tried to set narrow limits on when abortions could be performed during pregnancy. The majority of the efforts were blocked in court but now could be revived. Missouri in 2019 passed a bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/missouri-house-passes-bill-banning-abortion-at-8-weeks-11558122597"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning abortions after eight weeks }}}\uc2 , but a federal judge later {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/missouri-judge-temporarily-blocks-eight-week-abortion-ban-11566927945"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked it }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A dozen states passed bans on abortions after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-legislature-passes-six-week-abortion-ban-bill-11651190141"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six weeks of pregnancy }}}\uc2 . Most were blocked in court as well, with two exceptions, Texas and Oklahoma. Oklahoma lawmakers in 2022 passed several bills restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including a ban after about six weeks of pregnancy and a ban on abortions at any stage of pregnancy\u8212\'20\'14which both leave enforcement to individuals through civil lawsuits\u8212\'20\'14and another ban that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-legislature-passes-near-total-ban-on-abortion-11649192968"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 includes criminal penalties }}}\uc2  against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers.\par \par \uc2 Six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgia-six-week-abortion-ban-goes-into-effect-11658352186"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia }}}\uc2 , Ohio, South Carolina and Tennessee were all implemented in the hours and days after the high court's decision, following court orders. The South Carolina Supreme Court permanently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked enforcement }}}\uc2  of the state's 2021 law in January 2023, and an Ohio judge temporarily blocked a six-week ban in September 2022.\par \par \uc2 South Carolina's legislature passed a new six-week ban in 2023, which went into effect on May 25 after the governor signed it into law. A circuit court judge temporarily {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/judge-blocks-south-carolina-six-week-abortion-ban-3a31e2f3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked the law }}}\uc2  a day later.\par \par \uc2 Georgia's ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgias-six-week-abortion-ban-reinstated-by-state-supreme-court-11669224954"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was reinstated }}}\uc2  in November 2022 by the state Supreme Court, about a week after a lower court had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgias-abortion-ban-after-six-weeks-is-blocked-11668540794"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 permanently blocked enforcement }}}\uc2 of the 2019 law.\par \par \uc2 In Florida, which has been a major provider of abortions in the South, Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  signed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gov-ron-desantis-signs-florida-six-week-abortion-ban-b18029cc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban }}}\uc2  into law on April 13, 2023. The law won't take effect immediately.\par \par \uc2 ________________________________\par \par \uc2 State constitution bars protection\par \par \uc2 Before the Dobbs decision, voters had approved constitutional amendments in Alabama, Louisiana, Tennessee and West Virginia that assert their state constitutions don't secure the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Voters in Kansas and Kentucky rejected {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-abortion-vote-results-11659440554"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 similar proposed amendments }}}\uc2  in August and November 2022.\par \par \uc2 ________________________________\par \par \uc2 Protect access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 More than a dozen states and Washington, D.C., established protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in state law. Four states and the District of Columbia protect the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout pregnancy, while about a dozen others do so before viability, the point at which the fetus can live outside of the womb (around week 24 of pregnancy). The vast majority of states with these protections enacted them before Dobbs; Minnesota was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/minnesota-with-new-democratic-control-enacts-state-abortion-rights-11675190873"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the first to do so }}}\uc2  in the months that followed.\par \par \uc2 Voters in California, Michigan and Vermont {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-supporters-prevail-in-midterm-ballot-measures-11667986139"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved constitutional amendments }}}\uc2  enshrining protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  in November, becoming the first states to do so.\par \par \uc2 Following the Dobbs decision, Democratic leaders in states including New Mexico, Massachusetts, Maine and Colorado signed executive orders aimed at protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-health\b0 \highlight\uc2  services.\par \par \uc2 ________________________________\par \par \uc2 Methodology\par \par \uc2 Reproductive-age women are those 15 to 44 years old, according to the Census Bureau's American Community Survey five-year estimates for 2020, and calculated as a share of the total number of women in the age group in the 50 states plus Washington, D.C.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230525ej5p003s5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
