\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Judge Blocks South Carolina Six-Week  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban; Decision sets up battle over new law that is poised to go to state's highest court\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 507 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 May 2023\par 17:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A South Carolina judge on Friday blocked a newly enacted law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after about six weeks of pregnancy, the first salvo in a legal battle that is expected to make its way up to the state's highest court.\par \par \uc2 Gov. \uc2 Henry McMaster\uc2 , a Republican, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-restrictions-pass-across-u-s-as-republicans-overcome-divisions-331d7d31"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed the new six-week ban }}}\uc2  into law on Thursday and it took effect immediately. Local \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers quickly filed a lawsuit in state court, seeking to block its enforcement.\par \par \uc2 In January, the South Carolina Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/south-carolinas-6-week-abortion-ban-ruled-unconstitutional-11672940087"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 permanently blocked }}}\uc2  the state's 2021 law banning most abortions after six weeks of pregnancy, saying in a 3-2 decision that it violated the right to privacy in the state constitution. The decision was a key legal victory for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters, making South Carolina {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of the few states in the South }}}\uc2  to have fairly robust access.\par \par \uc2 Friday's decision by Circuit Court Judge Clifton Newman isn't expected to be the final word on the matter. The crucial test for the new law will come when it returns to the state's highest court. A justice who was key to the decision in January recently retired, giving the court a new makeup.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers said in the lawsuit that the new law "flies in the face of the South Carolina Supreme Court's ruling." They also said that by constraining women's ability to make deeply personal decisions the law violates guarantees in the state constitution to privacy, equality, life and liberty.\par \par \uc2 Attorney General Alan Wilson, a Republican, said on Friday, "We've defended the right to life in court before, and we're prepared to do it again."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state will for now remain legal up until about 22 weeks of pregnancy, as it has been for most of the time since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  ended federal constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  last June. Since then any efforts to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state have largely been blocked by the courts.\par \par \uc2 The GOP-controlled state legislature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-restrictions-pass-across-u-s-as-republicans-overcome-divisions-331d7d31"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed the six-week ban this month }}}\uc2  after several previous unsuccessful attempts to push through new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions over the past year. Its passage ended months of debates among Republicans over how far to push restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state. Five female senators, including three Republicans, successfully filibustered a near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April.\par \par \uc2 South Carolina is one of four states to set new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limits this year. Florida lawmakers passed a ban after around six weeks of pregnancy. That bill is currently in legal limbo, pending a decision by the state supreme court on a challenge to the current 15-week ban. Legislatures in North Carolina and Nebraska also banned most abortions after 12 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230526ej5q004s9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
