\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Restrictions Pass Across U.S. as Republicans Overcome Divisions; South Carolina's six-week ban caps first major legislative session since fall of Roe V. Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 1,200 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 May 2023\par 17:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 As state legislatures wrap up their first full sessions since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overruled Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 , Republican-led bodies that aimed to pass new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions found the votes to do so, but not without considerable political turbulence along the way.\par \par \uc2 The last expected major legislative battle of the season on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended Tuesday evening, with the passage of a bill banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after about six weeks of pregnancy in South Carolina, where Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-abortion-ruling-puts-states-in-spotlight-11656082938"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have for months been at odds }}}\uc2  with each other over how far to push.\par \par \uc2 The GOP-controlled state legislature had made several previous unsuccessful attempts to pass an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill since the Supreme Court ended federal constitutional protections for the procedure last June. Legislators finally overcame dissent within their party, passing the strict new abortions limits Tuesday by a vote of 27 to 19 in the state Senate, with a handful of Republicans voting against it.\par \par \uc2 The bill earlier passed the House overwhelmingly, after some of the most conservative lawmakers in that chamber, who initially opposed a six-week limit as too lenient, agreed to support it.\par \par \uc2 The bill now heads to the desk of the state's Republican Gov. \uc2 Henry McMaster\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/henrymcmaster/status/1661152551734243328?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1661152551734243328%7Ctwgr%5E7370a672e5958b3a057310bfc232f402550714f8%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thestate.com%2Fnews%2Fpolitics-government%2Farticle275697956.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who tweeted after the vote }}}\uc2  that he looked forward to signing it into law as soon as possible. The legislation is expected to face a difficult legal fight. The state's highest court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/south-carolinas-6-week-abortion-ban-ruled-unconstitutional-11672940087"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down a similar 2021 law }}}\uc2 less than six months ago but one justice who was central to that ruling has since retired.\par \par \uc2 Four states passed broad new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limits after recent legislative deliberations, but they varied in their time limits on the procedure. Florida joined South Carolina in landing on a ban after about six weeks of pregnancy, while North Carolina and Nebraska opted to set the limit at 12 weeks after some lawmakers noted that women don't always know they are pregnant by six weeks. A key conservative senator in Nebraska blocked a vote on a six-week bill there.\par \par \uc2 The North Carolina legislature overcame a veto by the state's Democratic governor. The state GOP essentially couldn't afford to lose a single vote, and the final bill reflected some compromises from within the Republican legislative supermajority.\par \par \uc2 Collectively, the bills are expected to further restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, requiring women in the South and Midwest to travel increasingly long distances if they want to obtain the procedure, while also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/women-encounter-abortion-delays-as-clinics-draw-patients-from-out-of-state-f40e318b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dealing with weekslong waits }}}\uc2  for appointments.\par \par \uc2 Other Republican-led states passed new limits this session on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills and on travel, including in Idaho, where the legislature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/idaho-legislature-votes-to-restrict-abortion-travel-by-minors-c8911e43"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made it a crime }}}\uc2  to assist a minor in traveling for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Legislators in Tennessee and North Dakota, facing criticism that previously enacted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans were too severe, added exceptions this legislative session for medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 The passage of a flurry of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions this year follows a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related electoral setbacks for Republicans since the end of Roe. Proposed constitutional amendments by antiabortion groups in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-abortion-vote-results-11659440554"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/abortion-rights-supporters-prevail-in-midterm-ballot-measures-Tfw0WrHeOVu4J8kI2Xit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kentucky }}}\uc2 both failed, while an amendment to add protections for the procedure to the Michigan constitution passed easily. Voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-shows-abortion-continues-to-sway-voters-4e47297c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also elected a justice }}}\uc2  who supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to the Wisconsin Supreme Court and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-supporters-prevail-in-midterm-ballot-measures-11667986139"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 handed Republicans weaker-than-expected results }}}\uc2  in the November midterms.\par \par \uc2 Political scientists said the dynamics in state legislatures are different than in statewide referendums and political races, due in part to gerrymandering that has created many safe districts.\par \par \uc2 "The way politics is, especially these days in this country, it doesn't matter what's popular with the general public. You are running for what's popular with the primary voter in your state, even in your district," said Steven Greene, a political-science professor at \uc2 North Carolina State University\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Leading up to its votes, Florida was in the political spotlight, with Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  seeking to position himself to run for the 2024 GOP presidential nomination. State Republicans had been quiet about plans to pass any new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions. This included the governor, who said little about the issue for months despite taking vocal positions on other contentious cultural issues.\par \par \uc2 But a bill banning abortions after six weeks of pregnancy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gov-ron-desantis-signs-florida-six-week-abortion-ban-b18029cc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed quickly in April }}}\uc2 after DeSantis put his support behind it. A small number of Republicans in more vulnerable districts in both the House and Senate voted against the bill, which remains in legal limbo, subject to a case challenging the state's current 15-week ban.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups have faced their own internal disagreements over how to push measures with conservative lawmakers, but some leaders say they have accomplished most of their key legislative goals this year. "It shows real momentum at the state level," said Caitlin Connors, southern regional director for Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America, an antiabortion group.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, antiabortion groups have yet to meet broad expectations that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-abortion-ruling-puts-states-in-spotlight-11656082938"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about half of states would impose strict bans on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  after Roe fell. That number today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stands closer to 15.  }}}\par \par \uc2 Virginia, where Republicans control the governor's mansion and the state House, was one place where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents had hoped to pass new restrictions this year and failed. A proposed 15-week ban died before reaching a vote in the state's Democratic-led Senate.\par \par \uc2 South Carolina's journey to Tuesday's six-week ban was filled with drama. Five female senators, including three Republicans, successfully filibustered a near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month, saying the bill was extreme and would push women to obtain dangerous illegal abortions.\par \par \uc2 GOP leaders then coalesced around the six-week approach, though several Republican senators joined an effort Tuesday to try to stymie the bill by pushing an amendment that would have allowed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until 12 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 "Shame on you. You should be here for the people you serve now, especially for the women," Sen. Katrina Shealy, a Republican who supported the 12-week amendment, told her colleagues.\par \par \uc2 Other Republicans said the bill didn't go far enough but that it was better than the state's current law, which allows \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to about 22 weeks of pregnancy. "I'd be the first to say it's a terribly flawed bill," said GOP Sen. Richard Cash. "It fails to protect human life from the beginning."\par \par \uc2 It is unclear if the bill will pass muster with the South Carolina Supreme Court, which ruled 3-2 in January to strike down the prior six-week ban. The female justice who wrote that decision retired recently and the legislature in February appointed a male replacement.\par \par \uc2 Some legislators expressed concern about the dynamic they were creating. "I don't want to have the constitutionality of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill decided because a man replaced a woman on the state Supreme Court. I think that would be a horrible look for this state," said Sen. \uc2 Tom Davis\uc2 , a Republican who voted in favor of the bill.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230524ej5o002p9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
