\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 A 19th-Century Law Could Help Influence the  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Pill's Future; Republicans see long-neglected Comstock Act as still-valid ban on shipping  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  drugs in the U.S.\b0\par\par\uc2 By Liz Essley Whyte and Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 841 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 May 2023\par 14:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents have mapped out a multipronged legal strategy for combating use of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-battle-returns-to-the-courtroom-b163f075"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill mifepristone  }}}\uc2  by invoking an obscure 1873 law called the Comstock Act that made it illegal to send "obscene" or "immoral" materials through the mail.\par \par \uc2 The act outlawed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-access-case-texas-judge-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shipping \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  drugs  }}}\uc2  across state lines, punishable by a fine or up to five years in prison. Local leaders in New Mexico have relied on the law in passing ordinances heavily restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and Republican elected officials have warned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/walgreens-abortion-pill-furor-highlights-complexity-of-access-in-post-roe-world-6ed0086c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pharmacies and drug distributors  }}}\uc2  that they could one day be prosecuted under the act.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion doctors and medical groups are also citing the law as part of their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-faces-fresh-deadline-in-abortion-pill-case-6d7b9049"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fast-moving legal challenge  }}}\uc2  to the \uc2 U.S. Food and Drug Administration\uc2  's approval of mifepristone two decades ago and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/story/states-are-next-battlegrounds-for-abortion-pill-access-8abde763"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expansion of pill access  }}}\uc2  in more recent years. The Fifth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals heard arguments in that case last week, though Comstock wasn't a central topic in the proceedings.\par \par \uc2 The law was named for 19th-century anti-vice crusader Anthony Comstock. Appalled by pornography and prostitution in New York City, he drafted the law and lobbied Congress to pass it, then later enforced it in his role as a special agent of the \uc2 U.S. Postal Service\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 By the 1940s there was a widespread consensus among judges that the Comstock Act could only be enforced if the seller intended the materials to be used for an illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to legal academics. In 1973 the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2  recognized a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , leading to widespread legalization of the procedure, and Comstock fell further out of use.\par \par \uc2 "I teach \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  and I always teach Comstock early in the course as this historical thing that nobody knows about and to not forget about, but not that I thought it was going to be relevant again," said Joanna Grossman, a visiting law professor at \uc2 Stanford University\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Since the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended federal constitutional protections  }}}\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly a year ago, Comstock has become grist for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents.\par \par \uc2 In New Mexico, a handful of cities and counties have passed ordinances imposing civil penalties for mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills or other implements into their jurisdictions, citing the Comstock Act. This has set up a legal battle with the state attorney general, who has asked New Mexico's highest court to invalidate the ordinances because they conflict with state law, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which allows \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . The court has temporarily blocked enforcement of the local laws.\par \par \uc2 Attorney General Ra\u250\'00\'FAl Torrez, a Democrat, in an interview said the antiabortion movement is using the act "as a way to implement their goal to institute a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban."\par \par \uc2 The municipalities have responded that New Mexico law doesn't trump a federal law, which they say bans mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. "This Court does not have the authority to rewrite federal law," attorneys for Roosevelt County, which passed one of the ordinances, wrote in a legal brief.\par \par \uc2 Federal courts recently have issued conflicting rulings on the relevance of Comstock today.\par \par \uc2 This month, a federal judge in West Virginia rejected arguments that the Comstock Act's restrictions apply to legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in a case involving GenBioPro, which makes the generic version of mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 But a federal district judge in Amarillo, Texas, adopted a contrary holding in April, saying the act was unambiguous and still in effect. "The Comstock Act plainly forecloses mail-order \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the present," wrote Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Should sales of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill be protected or be prosecuted under the 1873 Comstock Act? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Twenty Republican state attorneys general, nine U.S. senators and 38 congressmen in recent months sent letters to pharmacies warning them that they could face liability under the Comstock Act\u8212\'20\'14either from a future Republican administration or state attorneys general under racketeering law\u8212\'20\'14for shipping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs.\par \par \uc2 Even if people are unfamiliar with the statute, "the text could not be clearer," the attorneys general said in one letter.\par \par \uc2 Democratic senators, in turn, wrote to the same companies, urging them to do everything they can to widen access for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department's position is that the act doesn't prohibit the shipping of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  materials if the sender doesn't intend for them to be used illegally. Some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters worry, however, that the department's interpretation is tenuous and think Congress should change the law.\par \par \uc2 "The cleanest remedy is to repeal the Comstock Act," said Larry Gostin, a Georgetown Law professor and director of the O'Neill Institute for National and Global Health Law. "It doesn't represent the values of Americans today."\par \par \uc2 Write to Liz Essley Whyte at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:liz.whyte@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 liz.whyte@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Laura Kusisto at \par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230522ej5m001uq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
