\par\par \uc2 Main Street\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Who's Extreme on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 ? Republicans need to make the point that Democrats favor no restrictions whatever.\b0\par\par\uc2 By William McGurn \par \uc2 901 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 May 2023\par 21:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 In the months since the Supreme Court returned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the democratic process, politics has broken out across America. That was as the Supreme Court expected. Most interesting is the clash over the issue between the two Floridians who are the leading contenders to head the 2024 Republican ticket\u8212\'20\'14former \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump, who likes to tout himself as "the most pro-life president in American history," recently attacked Mr. DeSantis for signing a heartbeat bill that bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Florida after six weeks (with exceptions for rape, incest, etc.). Mr. Trump claimed that "many people within the pro-life movement feel that that was too harsh," though he neither named those alleged pro-lifers nor spelled out his preferred alternative.\par \par \uc2 The governor fired back. "The legislature put it in, I signed the bill, I was proud to do it. He [Trump] won't answer whether he would sign it or not."\par \par \uc2 It's not Mr. Trump's first go-round with pro-lifers. Last month he was rebuked by \uc2 Susan B. Anthony\uc2  Pro-Life America for taking the line that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is solely a state issue. Before that, he blamed pro-lifers for the GOP's disappointing results in November's midterms\u8212\'20\'14in answer to those who said it was his fault for backing candidates who could win Republican primaries but not general elections.\par \par \uc2 But as a candidate for the 2024 Republican nomination, Mr. Trump goes into the race with two signal pro-life achievements. The first is that the three justices he appointed to the Supreme Court provided the majority in the landmark Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization decision, which found no constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The second came in the final presidential debate of 2016. When asked how far she'd take \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  defended her vote against a ban on partial-birth \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by arguing that the government should have no say on the "most personal" of decisions. When asked to respond, Mr. Trump violated every liberal convention about how \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be discussed in polite society.\par \par \uc2 "Well, I think it's terrible," he said. "If you go with what Hillary is saying, in the ninth month, you can take the baby and rip the baby out of the womb of the mother just prior to the birth of the baby." In so speaking, Mr. Trump turned the tables on Mrs. Clinton, making the case that she was way out of sync with the American people.\par \par \uc2 For 2024, it's no secret that Democrats plan to use \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to paint Republicans as extremists. According to the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , the Democratic Party commissioned several surveys post-Dobbs in search of the best messaging on the issue. It found the answer: avoid all details, and characterize Republicans as supporting a national ban.\par \par \uc2 "Debating weeks is not where we want to be," Celinda Lake, a Democratic pollster who conducted some of these surveys, told the Times. "People are terrible at math and terrible at biology."\par \par \uc2 The Trump-DeSantis spat over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  must be viewed in this light. If Mr. Trump wins the nomination partly by maintaining that Mr. DeSantis is too extreme on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pro-lifers may not be as keen to come out for him\u8212\'20\'14especially with Roe v. Wade now overturned. Whatever restrictions Mr. Trump does ends up supporting, moreover, will also be attacked as extreme by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's campaign.\par \par \uc2 If, by contrast, Mr. DeSantis wins the nomination, Mr. Trump just handed the Biden campaign an attack ad: "Even \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  agrees that \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is too extreme on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Now, Mr. DeSantis wouldn't have signed the law unless he believed he could defend it publicly. That doesn't mean he will advocate making it national. He is likelier to say: I am a pro-lifer who believes we should be ambitious, but a 12-week ban is where the American people are.\par \par \uc2 That would help put the focus on Democrat extremism. Democrats argue that the Republican targeting of late-term abortions is misleading, because only 1% of abortions occur in the third trimester.\par \par \uc2 So why not flip the script and ask Mr. Biden why he can't agree to a restriction that leaves 99% of abortions untouched? The answer is because no Democratic Party leader can name any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  he would restrict.\par \par \uc2 There are other things pro-lifers can do. A friend of mine with a child who has Down syndrome suggests a pro-life ad featuring families like his and asking why their children's lives should be treated as having no worth. It's an uncomfortable question to ask\u8212\'20\'14and impossible to imagine the press ever asking it of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14but putting it out there would be clarifying.\par \par \uc2 For the moment, the clash between Mr. DeSantis and Mr. Trump has been reduced to the precise number of weeks \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be allowed. But the Republican challenge in 2024 is much larger.\par \par \uc2 Constantly we are told\u8212\'20\'14rightly\u8212\'20\'14that Americans want to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal but also support limits. Mr. Biden is not for any limits. For Republicans to prevail, they need to break through the protective media barrier and drive that home to the American people.\par \par \uc2 Write to mcgurn@wsj.com.\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230522ej5m003xp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
