\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Nebraska Passes Restrictions on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 , Gender-Affirming Care for Minors; Vote marks cumulation of tense and historic legislative session\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 1,119 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 May 2023\par 22:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Nebraska Legislature passed a bill restricting access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gender-affirming care, sending two of the most contentious issues of the legislative session to the Republican governor's desk after months of impassioned debate.\par \par \uc2 The vote marks the culmination of a historic legislative session in Nebraska, where heated and personal debates have deeply divided the nonpartisan legislature. Sen. Machaela Cavanaugh led an effort to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/nebraskas-legislative-session-is-tangled-up-in-transgender-rights-fight-8f455ea3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filibuster nearly every bill up for debate }}}\uc2  to protest the proposed restrictions on gender-affirming care for Nebraskans under age 19. The filibuster slowed the passage of bills by adding hours of debate to each piece of legislation.\par \par \uc2 The unicameral Legislature on Tuesday amended its bill restricting gender-affirming care for youth to include a ban on most abortions after 12 weeks of pregnancy. A separate bill banning most abortions after six weeks of pregnancy failed to advance in April. The legislative maneuvering combined the two issues under one bill in the final weeks of the session.\par \par \uc2 The hours of debate on the floor this week were tense and emotional. Protesters chanted and booed in opposition throughout the debate Friday. The legislature's speaker ordered officers to clear the chamber's balcony after protesters interrupted debate.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers passed the bill in a 33 to 15 vote Friday afternoon. Nebraska Gov. \uc2 Jim Pillen\uc2 , a Republican, said Tuesday he would sign the bill upon its final passage.\par \par \uc2 "All children deserve a chance to grow and live happy, fruitful lives. This includes pre-born boys and girls, and it includes children struggling with their gender identity," Pillen said in a statement shortly after the bill's passage Friday. "These kids deserve the opportunity to grow and explore who they are and want to be, and they can do so without making irreversible decisions that should be made when they are fully grown."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban will take effect after the governor signs the bill. The gender-affirming-care restrictions will be enforced beginning Oct. 1.\par \par \uc2 Tensions and debates over social issues, including transgender rights and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, have ricocheted through state legislatures this year. Republican-led legislatures passed bills barring certain gender-based therapies and surgeries for youth in states including Georgia, Tennessee and South Dakota. Texas lawmakers recently joined more than a dozen other states in passing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-lawmakers-pass-measure-preventing-treatment-for-transgender-youth-a0d2f12f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new restrictions on care for transgender youth }}}\uc2  this year. Courts have temporarily blocked similar laws passed in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/arkansas-bans-gender-transition-treatment-for-trans-minors-11617744915?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arkansas }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/alabama-argues-for-transgender-medication-ban-citing-supreme-court-abortion-ruling-11656698904?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alabama }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers supporting such restrictions say they are concerned about what they believe can be harmful long-term impacts of treatments on transgender youth. Those opposing bans on gender-affirming care say eliminating access to treatments and therapies can be dangerous and traumatizing for transgender children and teens. Medical groups including the \uc2 American Medical Association\uc2  and the \uc2 American Academy of Pediatrics\uc2  strongly oppose limiting access to gender-affirming care.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Republican-led legislatures in states including Florida and North Carolina {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-abortion-ban-law-28c65d8c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed new \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  restrictions this year }}}\uc2 , emboldened by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court's decision overturning Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  in June. South Carolina lawmakers are currently weighing a ban on most abortions after six weeks of pregnancy in a special session.\par \par \uc2 During debate in Nebraska on Friday, conservative lawmakers who supported the measure called the final version of the bill a compromise and an effort to protect children. They also sought to defend their legislation from those who called it dangerous and hateful to transgender children.\par \par \uc2 "The adults in the room are trying very hard to come up with legislation that will provide guidelines for kids who are dealing with gender dysphoria," Sen. Kathleen Kauth, the bill's sponsor, said on the floor Friday. "It does not mean by any stretch of the imagination that we hate them." \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich427\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6405
