\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 North Carolina Lawmakers Vote to Override Veto of 12-Week  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban; New restrictions could further unsettle  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  landscape in the South\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 819 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 May 2023\par 01:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 North Carolina's Republican-led legislature on Tuesday overrode the governor's veto of a bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/north-carolina-passes-12-week-abortion-ban-39b06537"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning most abortions after 12 weeks of pregnancy  }}}\uc2 , a sign of the GOP's willingness to adopt tougher \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions in swing states where it has political power.\par \par \uc2 Once it takes effect in the coming months, the law promises to further unsettle the national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  landscape. Since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2  in June, North Carolina has seen one of the largest influxes of out-of-state patients, many from Southern states that have\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enacted strict limits  }}}\uc2  on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Democratic Gov. \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2  and others in his party lobbied several moderate Republican state lawmakers to vote against overriding the governor's veto, which he issued on Saturday. They pointed to statements a handful of Republicans made in the lead-up to the 2022 election indicating support for the current state law, which allows \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the middle of the second trimester. Republicans recently gained a narrow legislative supermajority, giving them the ability to override the governor, but they essentially couldn't afford to lose a single vote.\par \par \uc2 The Senate on Tuesday voted 30 to 20, along party lines, to override the veto. The House voted 72 to 48, also along party lines.\par \par \uc2 State Rep. Tricia Cotham {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/north-carolina-democrat-changes-parties-upending-state-politics-e8651a8e?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 switched parties in April  }}}\uc2  after she was elected as a Democrat in November, giving the GOP its supermajority. Last year, the lawmaker said she would fight to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in North Carolina, following the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-has-yet-to-identify-who-leaked-draft-opinion-in-abortion-case-11674157126"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leak of a draft Supreme Court ruling  }}}\uc2  that eliminated a federal constitutional right to the procedure. The high court issued its ruling in June. Ms. Cotham voted for the 12-week ban earlier this month and again on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 After the legislature passed the 12-week ban, Mr. Cooper vetoed the bill at an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights rally and has held roundtables in recent days with doctors, patients and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates. "How about we leave medicine to the doctors and the decisions to the women," the governor said at the rally.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have called the legislation a compromise. North Carolina House Speaker Tim Moore, a Republican, said over the weekend that the governor's veto would quickly be overridden. The bill, he said, would "save unborn lives, protect women and support families."\par \par \uc2 GOP lawmakers bypassed the usual committee and amendment process in crafting the legislation, an approach their Democratic colleagues called undemocratic.\par \par \uc2 Sen. Sydney Batch, a Democrat, said Republicans struggled for months with internal dissent about the bill from members in more vulnerable districts who didn't want to be forced to vote on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation. "They know that when they talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  they lose," she said in an interview.\par \par \uc2 Sen. Michael Lee was among the Republicans the governor said had campaigned on promises to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Mr. Lee wrote an op-ed last year opposing bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first trimester of pregnancy. His vote in favor of the 12-week ban was consistent with that position, he said on the floor Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "My wife and I personally believe life begins at conception," Mr. Lee said. "But from a policy perspective, I think this is something that we should be doing."\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups, meanwhile, said the governor's lobbying efforts against the bill were out of step with North Carolina voters. "During his tour targeting legislators to uphold his veto, the governor made it abundantly clear who he was representing by holding a panel with the chief medical officer of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  and the owner of another \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  facility," said Caitlin Connors, southern regional director for SBA Pro-Life America.\par \par \uc2 The legislation bans nearly all abortions after 12 weeks of pregnancy and allows limited exceptions for rape, incest and serious fetal anomalies. There is no gestational limit on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 Eighty-eight percent of abortions in North Carolina in 2020 occurred at or before 12 weeks of pregnancy, according to data from the \uc2 North Carolina Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 In neighboring South Carolina, legislators are expected to meet this week in a special session to debate a bill to ban most abortions after about six weeks of pregnancy. The state's Republican-led legislature had previously failed to pass a near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of opposition from some lawmakers, including Republicans, but it appears the party might have enough support for the six-week bill.\par \par \uc2 If the bill passes, it will set up a legal battle in the state, whose highest court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/south-carolinas-6-week-abortion-ban-ruled-unconstitutional-11672940087"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier this year ruled  }}}\uc2  that the South Carolina Constitution contains a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at \par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230516ej5g003jt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
