\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  Dominates Florida Legislative Session Ahead of Expected Presidential Run; Conservative wins may help against Trump, but  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 , guns stances could hurt in general election\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alex Leary \par \uc2 1,079 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 May 2023\par 18:18 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 What \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  wanted, he got.\par \par \uc2 The Florida governor dominated the 60-day legislative session in Tallahassee that ended Friday, racking up conservative policy victories that will serve as the backbone of his soon-expected entry into {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/down-in-polls-and-taking-flak-from-donald-trump-ron-desantis-looks-to-rebound-9bf13a27"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 2024 presidential race }}}\uc2 . Those wins could boost him in the GOP primary contest\u8212\'20\'14even as some allies are concerned about how far to the right he pushed, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-other-gop-2024-hopefuls-struggle-to-define-abortion-message-71fed983"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 particularly on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We're really delivering a big agenda," Mr. DeSantis said this week while signing a trio of crime bills, a "very bold agenda that's really setting the terms of the debate for the country."\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeSantis aims to attract Republican voters on the basis of effective governing, part of a contrast he is trying to make with former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/donald-trump-tops-ron-desantis-in-test-of-gop-presidential-field-wsj-poll-finds-88c84663"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has grown his lead }}}\uc2  in the GOP primary. Mr. DeSantis is expected to announce in May or June, and next week he will make another visit to Iowa.\par \par \uc2 "What happens in the future, look, we'll get on that relatively soon," Mr. DeSantis said Friday as the session adjourned. "You've either got to put up or shut up."\par \par \uc2 Over the course of the legislative session, Mr. DeSantis marshaled a Republican supermajority to pass bills allowing people to carry concealed weapons without permits; cracking down on illegal immigration; banning Chinese citizens from buying land in the state and prohibiting state and local governments from considering environmental, social justice and governance factors, or ESG, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/floridas-desantis-takes-aim-at-woke-capital-11659043495"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in investment decisions }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He secured restrictions on drag shows and on colleges' spending on diversity programs while limiting the use of preferred pronouns in K-12 schools and banning gender-affirming care for transgender minors. He backed a major school-voucher expansion, made it easier to impose the death penalty, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-gov-ron-desantis-sets-stage-for-legislative-action-against-disney-d96b2e33"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broadened his legal battle }}}\uc2  with \uc2 Walt Disney Co\uc2 . and signed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gov-ron-desantis-signs-florida-six-week-abortion-ban-b18029cc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeSantis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gov-ron-desantis-signs-florida-six-week-abortion-ban-b18029cc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  legislation }}}\uc2  late at night and has talked about it little since then. A Wall Street Journal poll conducted in April showed that 68% of Republican primary voters nationally favored a six-week ban, but 53% of voters overall opposed it.\par \par \uc2 "He clearly is trying to run to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's right on that issue since Trump antagonized pro-life forces by blaming them for the 2020 Republican losses," said GOP pollster \uc2 Whit Ayres\uc2 . "I presume he is thinking you can't face the challenge of a general election if you don't win a primary."\par \par \uc2 Along with the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue, allowing people to carry a concealed handgun without a permit could also prove challenging in a general election. The Journal poll showed 56% of GOP primary voters supported that right, while 65% of overall voters were in opposition.\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeSantis has portrayed himself as unbowed by criticism as he pursues a largely conservative agenda. He has sought to contrast his putting "points on the board" with Mr. Trump's polarizing and sometimes chaotic tenure and has pointed to Republican losses in the last three major election cycles.\par \par \uc2 "We believe in just leading. And we don't think you've got to put a finger in the wind, we don't worry about the media," Mr. DeSantis said at an event Thursday. "On issue after issue, I think we've delivered, and delivered in a really, really big way."\par \par \uc2 Privately, some GOP lawmakers grumbled about Mr. DeSantis's dominance and what they see as his "my way or the highway" approach.\par \par \uc2 Former Republican state Sen. \uc2 Jeff Brandes\uc2  said Mr. DeSantis's agenda has taken attention from some pressing state issues, including affordability questions over housing and insurance and a stressed state prison system. "When the major issues you are discussing are things that help you get on Fox News, it means not focusing on meat and potato issues," he said.\par \par \uc2 Still, Florida legislators handed Mr. DeSantis gifts to ease a White House bid: changing state law so he won't have to resign to run for president and shielding his past and future travel records from public disclosure, making it hard for political opponents and reporters to scrutinize his movements and use of taxpayer money.\par \par \uc2 His strength in Tallahassee, coming off a landslide re-election win in November, may not necessarily travel with him to early primary states.\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeSantis, 44, has at times struggled on the national level, both with policy and his personal style, and he has faced unrelenting attacks from Mr. Trump. Some prominent donors have signaled concerns over his mixed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gop-2024-rivals-pounce-on-ron-desantis-over-ukraine-aid-fe80821d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comments about Ukraine }}}\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill. A number of Republicans, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/disney-ron-desantis-bob-iger-florida-lawsuit-46c8b436"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including some in Florida }}}\uc2 , have expressed unease over the \uc2 Disney\uc2  feud.\par \par \uc2 Billionaire Republican donor \uc2 Peter Thiel\uc2  told the Honestly podcast Wednesday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.honestlypod.com/podcast/episode/2e8ceb63/peter-thiel-says-america-has-bigger-problems-than-wokeness"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that he would support }}}\uc2  Mr. DeSantis if he is the Republican nominee but said focusing too heavily on "the woke issue" distracts from the economic issues that remain at the forefront of voter concerns.\par \par \uc2 Aides to Mr. DeSantis, who emerged as a national figure by opposing Covid restrictions, are coy about the timing of his announcement but say they are confident of his readiness.\par \par \uc2 A super PAC backing the governor has spent millions on ads boosting his profile and could soon be infused with $86 million currently sitting in a state political committee, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-ron-desantis-could-unlock-86-million-for-a-presidential-run-850b81c0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legally questionable move }}}\uc2 , according to election lawyers. The group has added staff in early primary voting states and is organizing on college campuses.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Do you think Gov. DeSantis's successes in Florida can translate to the national stage? Why or why not? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign has been eager to point out Mr. DeSantis's dropping poll numbers and the signs that some of his donors are unhappy with his agenda. Mr. Trump has been endorsed by 11 of Florida's 20 Republican U.S. House members, while Mr. DeSantis has so far gained only one. But with several months to go before primary voting begins, many other key Republican officeholders and donors remain up for grabs.\par \par \uc2 "He's clearly not as strong as he was immediately after this thumping win in November," Mr. Ayres said. "But far too many people want to jump to premature conclusions. It's ridiculous to write off his chances before he's even announced a campaign."\par \par \uc2 Write to Alex Leary at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:alex.leary@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alex.leary@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230505ej55000jq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
