\par \par \uc2 An exam room at A Woman's Choice clinic in Charlotte, N.C. PHOTO: Angela Owens/The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 North Carolina's Republican-led legislature passed a ban on most abortions after 12 weeks of pregnancy, setting the state on a path to restricting access that could ultimately reverberate across the region.\par \par \uc2 North Carolina has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/women-encounter-abortion-delays-as-clinics-draw-patients-from-out-of-state-f40e318b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 become a crucial access point }}}\uc2  for patients in the Southeast seeking abortions after the Supreme Court last year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  and many states in the region enacted near-total bans on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers passed the 12-week ban Thursday by a vote of 29-20 in the Senate and on Wednesday along party lines in the House. The bill's passage came quickly after Republicans announced Tuesday they had reached a consensus following months of negotiations within the party. Republicans crafted the legislation behind closed doors, bypassing the usual committee and amendment process.\par \par \uc2 North Carolina Gov. \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2 , a Democrat, said Wednesday he would veto the bill. A new Republican supermajority in the legislature might have the votes to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/north-carolina-lawmakers-to-vote-on-overriding-veto-of-12-week-abortion-ban-4d7d56c1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 override his veto }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bill's passage in a closely politically divided state like North Carolina shows some Republicans are willing to pursue new limits on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite some of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-shows-abortion-continues-to-sway-voters-4e47297c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blowback the party has faced }}}\uc2  on the issue over the past year. Florida lawmakers in April {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-abortion-ban-law-28c65d8c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy. In other states, such as South Carolina and Nebraska, Republican legislators failed to pass their own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans last week amid tensions over how far to go.\par \par \uc2 North Carolina Rep. Tricia Cotham {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/north-carolina-democrat-changes-parties-upending-state-politics-e8651a8e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 switched parties last month }}}\uc2  after she was elected as a Democrat in November, giving the GOP their supermajority. She voted to pass the 12-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban on Wednesday. A year ago, after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-confirms-authenticity-of-leaked-draft-opinion-overruling-roe-v-wade-11651592725"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leak of a draft Supreme Court opinion }}}\uc2  on Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization, Ms. Cotham said she would fight to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Current North Carolina law bans most abortions after 20 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The new legislation bans nearly all abortions after 12 weeks of pregnancy, a threshold Republicans called a compromise. It allows limited exceptions for rape, incest and serious fetal anomalies. There is no gestational limit on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 Eighty-eight percent of abortions in North Carolina in 2020 occurred before or at 12 weeks of pregnancy, according to data from the \uc2 North Carolina Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 . The bans implemented since then across the Southeast and elsewhere in the U.S. have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/women-encounter-abortion-delays-as-clinics-draw-patients-from-out-of-state-f40e318b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushed abortions later into pregnancy }}}\uc2  because of increased demand and delays at clinics in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal.\par \par \uc2 The new legislation also adds requirements for in-person medical visits that could make abortions more difficult to obtain for women traveling from out of state or taking off work, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups say.\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers supporting the legislation said they landed on a reasonable approach to restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  during their closed-door conversations.\par \par \uc2 "North Carolina has an opportunity to be a leader in this country for finding a way out of the acrimony and extremism that has tended to dominate our discussion of this issue," GOP Sen. Amy Galey said on the floor Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Democrats denounced the legislation and the strategies Republicans used to bring it forward with little opportunity for public comment and consideration. "This law will make many North Carolinians become healthcare refugees who must go to other states to get the care that they need\u8212\'20\'14that is if they can afford to do so," Sen. Natasha Marcus said.\par \par \uc2 Protesters supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights gathered outside of the legislature and in the chambers Wednesday and Thursday. They chanted, "Shame!" at lawmakers after they voted to pass the legislation in the House and the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Marc Hetherington, a political-science professor at the \uc2 University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill\uc2 , said that given the state's political mix, the new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions could have future consequences for Republicans running for governor and other statewide offices.\par \par \uc2 "It's a compromise within the Republican caucus. It's not a compromise really at all as it relates to the state as a whole," Mr. Hetherington said. "This is still going to put North Carolina on the relatively conservative end of the spectrum on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions."\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups say the bill strikes the right balance given the current political environment in the state. Caitlin Connors, southern regional director for SBA Pro-Life America, said North Carolinians are "rightly concerned with their state becoming an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  destination."\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What will be the political impact of North Carolina's potential 12-week ban on abortions? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 More than a dozen states banned or heavily restricted access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Supreme Court's Dobbs decision eliminated federal protections. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 patchwork of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access }}}\uc2  has prompted pregnant women and girls to travel across state lines for the procedure\u8212\'20\'14including to North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 The state saw one of the largest increases in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the Supreme Court's decision last June. On average, there were 788 more abortions each month there compared with before the ruling, according to WeCount, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -data project sponsored by the Society of Family Planning, which supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230504ej54006hd\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
