\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 President Biden Announces 2024 Re-Election Bid, Setting Up Potential Trump Rematch; Oldest-ever president cites protection of freedoms in race for second term\b0\par\par\uc2 By Catherine Lucey and Ken Thomas \par \uc2 1,670 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 April 2023\par 17:47 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14President Biden opened {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/president-biden-plans-video-re-election-bid-announcement-as-soon-as-next-week-cfcea754"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his 2024 re-election campaign }}}\uc2  by casting Republicans as a danger to democracy and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, while the GOP countered that the presidential contest would pivot on the faltering economy and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/is-biden-too-old-to-run-again-we-asked-people-born-on-his-exact-birthday-476bdff3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mr. Biden's age }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden formally launched his bid for a second term Tuesday with a video announcement, a declaration that puts him on the path to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/another-biden-trump-presidential-race-in-2024-looks-more-likely-19d88039"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a potential rematch }}}\uc2  with the man he beat in 2020\u8212\'20\'14former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . The 2024 campaign will play out in an era of political polarization, with both parties fighting over a small number of battleground states and the narrow slice of the electorate that isn't firmly in one camp or the other.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ChjibtX0UzU&t=56s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the video }}}\uc2 , Mr. Biden frames the election as a question of "whether in the years ahead we have more freedom or less freedom, more rights or fewer. I know what I want the answer to be and I think you do, too. This is not a time to be complacent. That's why I'm running for re-election." He cites \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, same-sex marriage and voting rights as examples of freedoms under threat.\par \par \uc2 The three-minute video opens with images of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/jan-6-committee-releases-final-investigative-report-on-capitol-attack-11671766032"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jan. 6, 2021, attack on the U.S. Capitol }}}\uc2 , and then references the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court's overturning of Roe vs. Wade }}}\uc2  before Mr. Biden says the word: "Freedom," pointing to the American value as the key to his first term. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , his running mate again, features prominently in the video, which warns against "MAGA extremists."\par \par \uc2 In a statement released ahead of the video, Mr. Trump attacked Mr. Biden over high inflation and his handling of the southern border, while repeating his false claims that he won the 2020 election. "There has never been a greater contrast between two successive administrations in all of American history. Ours being greatness, and theirs being failure," he said.\par \par \uc2 Already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/as-biden-turns-80-some-democrats-see-age-as-issue-for-potential-2024-bid-11668917528"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the oldest president in American history }}}\uc2  at 80 years old, Mr. Biden would be 86 at the end of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/on-bidens-second-term-agenda-unmet-goals-from-his-first-term-a9ec64de"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a second term }}}\uc2 . A majority of Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lack-of-voter-enthusiasm-poses-hurdle-for-joe-bidens-re-election-ee3cfa57"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 don't approve of his performance as president }}}\uc2 , and polls show ample public concern\u8212\'20\'14even among many Democrats\u8212\'20\'14about his age and fitness for office. Mr. Biden has answered questions about his age by saying that people should watch him do the job. Aides say his legislative record\u8212\'20\'14including securing funding for the Covid-19 pandemic and passing broad infrastructure and climate measures\u8212\'20\'14will resonate with voters.\par \par \uc2 "Every generation of Americans has faced a moment when they've had to defend democracy, stand up for our personal freedoms, stand up for our right to vote and our civil rights. And this is our moment," Mr. Biden said in the video, urging supporters to visit his campaign website. "Let's finish this job, I know we can."\par \par \uc2 In the afternoon, the president addressed the North America's Building Trades Unions in Washington, allowing him to highlight his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/infrastructure-bill-2021-what-11627515002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1 trillion bipartisan infrastructure law }}}\uc2 . Ms. Harris will speak at a rally on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights later in the day at \uc2 Howard University\uc2 , her alma mater.\par \par \uc2 "Our economic plan is working, we now have to finish the job and you're leading the way," Mr. Biden said. After he said he needed to "finish the job," the crowd interrupted him to chant "four more years."\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/whos-running-for-president-in-2024-adb754e2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The 2024 race }}}\uc2 , which will also determine the House and Senate majorities, will unfold differently than in 2020, when candidates like Mr. Biden eschewed in-person campaigning.\par \par \uc2 In the 2022 midterm elections, Democrats outperformed expectations, in part as a result of voters' concerns over preserving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and opposition to Trump-endorsed candidates. By focusing on these themes more than his legislative accomplishments, Mr. Biden is signaling that he expects these issues will motivate Democrats and independents in 2024. Mr. Biden has said he would work to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, while many Republican candidates support restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Protecting democracy at home and abroad has long been a focus for Mr. Biden, who gave {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-to-say-in-prime-time-address-democracy-is-at-stake-in-midterm-elections-11662048825"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a high-profile speech on the topic }}}\uc2  in Philadelphia ahead of the midterms.\par \par \uc2 The president faces headwinds as he enters the race. According to a new Wall Street Journal poll, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/donald-trump-tops-ron-desantis-in-test-of-gop-presidential-field-wsj-poll-finds-88c84663"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 42% of voters approve }}}\uc2  of the job Mr. Biden is doing, compared with 56% who disapprove, numbers that haven't moved much in over a year. The poll also found that 15% of voters think the country is on the right track, and it showed Mr. Biden underwater with voters on nearly all major issues, including his handling of the economy and infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have blamed Mr. Biden for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/inflation-tracker-cpi-data-prices-11657717467"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 high inflation }}}\uc2 . They also have criticized him over the chaotic withdrawal of U.S. forces from Afghanistan. \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  Chairwoman \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2  said that Mr. Biden has created "crisis after crisis."\par \par \uc2 With the first primaries still months away, Mr. Trump is leading the Republican field as he seeks to win another term after losing to Mr. Biden in 2020. The poll shows that in a direct contest with Mr. Trump, Mr. Biden gets 48% and Mr. Trump 45%. Against Florida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , a Republican who is viewed as likely to launch his campaign in May or June, Mr. Biden gets 45% and Mr. DeSantis 48%. Mr. DeSantis is pictured briefly in Mr. Biden's announcement video, standing next to Mr. Trump.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden and his advisers had considered formally launching his re-election bid toward the beginning of the year, as early as mid-February, but saw little urgency as Mr. Trump's campaign struggled and the GOP field was slow to materialize. His team started scripting his campaign video before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/ireland-marks-biden-homecoming-more-than-150-years-after-his-ancestors-fled-1a5393a3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he traveled to Ireland }}}\uc2  earlier in April and filming began when he returned to Delaware.\par \par \uc2 The president faces two long-shot primary challengers in author \uc2 Marianne Williamson\uc2  and environmental lawyer Robert F. Kennedy Jr., the son of \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy\uc2  and nephew of former President \uc2 John F. Kennedy\uc2 . Democrats' strong showing in the 2022 midterm elections, in which the party maintained control of the Senate, and a desire to avoid a divisive intraparty battle dissuaded any prominent Democrats from challenging Mr. Biden for the nomination.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday's video reveal matches the low-key, Rose Garden strategy that Mr. Biden's campaign will take for now. He is expected to keep his focus on being president, traveling and working in his official capacity, with some fundraising added to his schedule. The approach harks back to the re-election bid from former President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/SB10001424052748703712504576242274260220268"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced his campaign launch }}}\uc2  in a video in April 2011, but didn't hold his first official rally for his re-election until May 2012.\par \par \uc2 During his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/state-of-the-union-2023-president-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 State of the Union address }}}\uc2 , Mr. Biden stressed the need to "finish the job," emphasizing climate change, child care for workers and raising taxes on the wealthy.\par \par \uc2 As Election Day draws closer, Mr. Biden is expected to conduct his campaign differently than in 2020. As a result of the once-in-a-century pandemic, Mr. Biden spent weeks holed up in his home after securing the nomination, then held a limited number of in-person events and rallies. But with the pandemic waning, he would be expected to have a more robust campaign presence this time.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden began his political career in local government in Delaware and then was elected to the Senate shortly before his 30th birthday. After more than three decades in the Senate, he served two terms as vice president to Mr. \uc2 Obama\uc2 , then won the presidency in 2020. In office, he has overseen legislation to combat the Covid-19 pandemic, invest in the nation's aging infrastructure and boost domestic manufacturing.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What is your outlook for President Biden's re-election campaign? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 He has also pushed for\u8212\'20\'14but so far has been unable to deliver\u8212\'20\'14voting-rights legislation, a national paid-leave program, support for child care, changes to the immigration system and efforts to provide free community college.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden's announcement allows his re-election campaign to begin fundraising and build out a staff, which will work in close partnership with the White House. Mr. Biden will also have a built-in infrastructure from the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 , which will play a key role in organizing supporters in battleground states. The DNC currently has $28.6 million in the bank, according to their latest financial statement.\par \par \uc2 The campaign is expected to be based in the president's hometown of Wilmington, Del. Mr. Biden named Julie Chavez Rodriguez as his campaign manager Tuesday. Ms. Chavez Rodriguez is a White House senior adviser and the granddaughter of the late labor leader Cesar Chavez, whose bust is featured in Mr. Biden's Oval Office. \uc2 Quentin Fulks\uc2 , who managed Sen. Raphael Warnock's (D., Ga.) campaign, will serve as principal deputy campaign manager.\par \par \uc2 Top advisers \uc2 Jennifer O'Malley Dillon\uc2 , who managed the 2020 campaign, and Anita Dunn, who was the campaign's senior adviser, are expected to help lead the effort from the White House.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden's allies are preparing in other ways. Top donors to Mr. Biden's 2020 campaign and the DNC, including those who raised roughly $1 million or more, have been invited to meetings with Biden advisers in Washington next week. The meetings are expected to include a gathering with Mr. Biden, according to people familiar with the plans.\par \par \uc2 The DNC held a similar event earlier in the month in Scottsdale, Ariz., which included a briefing with pollster David Binder; a presentation about lessons learned in top battleground states such as Georgia, Nevada and Wisconsin; and a session on the Republican presidential field, according to a copy of the agenda viewed by the Journal.\par \par \uc2 Write to Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Ken Thomas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:ken.thomas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ken.thomas@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230425ej4p000rt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
