\par\par \uc2 Review & Outlook (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Nikki Haley Gets Real on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 ; The GOP candidate makes the pro-life case for political realism.\b0\par\par\uc2 By The Editorial Board \par \uc2 583 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 April 2023\par 22:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republicans urgently need to sort out their political argument on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the best effort we've heard so far is Nikki Haley's speech on Tuesday combining the moral case against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a politics of persuasion and humility.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Haley called \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  "a deeply personal topic for both women and men," and she treated the issue with the compassion and seriousness it demands. "I know how hard pregnancy can be" and "many women have it much harder." A friend was raped and feared an unwanted pregnancy, "an anguish I wouldn't wish on anyone."\par \par \uc2 Ms. Haley described herself as "pro-life," both "unapologetic and unhesitant about it," and cited measures she signed as South Carolina Governor. Judges in Roe v. Wade imposed a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  standard that "much of the country found deeply offensive." Roe's downfall last year was right on the legal merits and an enormous victory for the pro-life movement.\par \par \uc2 But she tempered that conviction with political realism. "The pro-life laws that have passed in strongly Republican states"\u8212\'20\'14bills that ban the procedure after a heartbeat is detected at six weeks, for instance\u8212\'20\'14"will not be approved at the federal level," she said.\par \par \uc2 She's right. A federal bill would need 60 votes to clear a Senate filibuster, and the GOP hasn't held that many seats in the upper chamber since 1910. Her candor is all the more notable because Ms. Haley spoke to an audience from Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America. "If we want to protect more moms and save more babies, we need more Americans to join with us," she added.\par \par \uc2 Compromise and incrementalism are often unpopular in movements rooted in moral conviction, but the pro-life right can't dictate the law when most voters still think \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal. Americans have grown more uneasy about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as ultrasound technology and neonatal care have improved, but a ban in the first trimester lacks majority support.\par \par \uc2 Americans can change their mind, but that will take time and persuasion. Meantime, Ms. Haley suggests federal action on "consensus" policies such as protections for doctors and nurses who decline to perform abortions. The GOP could also continue the tradition of preventing taxpayer financing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a once bipartisan policy that Democrats have abandoned.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Haley also said the GOP should tell voters what the left thinks about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Democratic position is increasingly that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be available at any time up until delivery and celebrated as a social good. The party has abandoned Bill Clinton's "safe, legal and rare" standard, but the electorate has not.\par \par \uc2 The press will call Ms. Haley's remarks a straddle, and some GOP voters will agree. But Ms. Haley deserves credit for confronting the subject head on, with a speech that wasn't sanctimonious or censorious. She told the audience about her husband, born into poverty, with an alcoholic father and a mother with a traumatic brain injury. He was eventually adopted. Ms. Haley asked: What if his biological mother had chosen "another path?" She added: "The world is better because of Michael Haley."\par \par \uc2 Democrats and the press won't let the GOP duck \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2024, and Roe blocked real debate for decades. The party could do worse than Ms. Haley's pitch for seeking discrete policy victories while building a broader cultural consensus.\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230425ej4p005xx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
