\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Trump, Other GOP 2024 Hopefuls Struggle to Define  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Message; Republican base is eager for more  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  restrictions, but polls show most voters are wary\b0\par\par\uc2 By Eliza Collins \par \uc2 1,014 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 April 2023\par 09:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 As states, Congress and the Supreme Court weigh \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, GOP presidential hopefuls are divided over how far to go on limits that are demanded by their base but unpopular with the voters who decide general elections.\par \par \uc2 Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  nominated three justices to the Supreme Court, making a conservative majority that voted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to overturn the constitutional right to an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  last year. His spokesman suggested last week that Mr. Trump opposes any national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, which some Republicans are urging.\par \par \uc2 "President Donald J. Trump believes that the Supreme Court, led by the three Justices which he supported, got it right when they ruled this is an issue that should be decided at the state level," Trump spokesman Steven Cheung said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 That brought a sharp response from SBA Pro-Life America President Marjorie Dannenfelser, who said the statement from Mr. Trump's spokesman "is a morally indefensible position for a self-proclaimed pro-life presidential candidate to hold." She said the organization will oppose any candidate who doesn't embrace a minimum 15-week national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Dannenfelser was involved in both of Mr. Trump's campaigns, and the organization along with its affiliates spent roughly $52 million during the 2020 election cycle, said spokeswoman Mary Owens.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access has been hotly debated in the U.S. since the Supreme Court's decision to overturn Roe v. Wade. Republican states continue to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights further, as some Democratic-led states work to codify rights into law. The Supreme Court on Friday allowed the widely used \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-faces-fresh-deadline-in-abortion-pill-case-6d7b9049?mod=hp_lead_pos5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mifepristone to remain on the market indefinitely }}}\uc2 , blocking the effect of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-pill-ruling-ignites-new-national-battle-a9c03329"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a lower-court order }}}\uc2  that was poised to limit access to the pill.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court's action wasn't a decision on the merits of the case; instead, the justices were deciding whether the pill could remain available during a continuing legal challenge brought by antiabortion groups.\par \par \uc2 Many prominent Republicans have been silent on that legal case and whether the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 's approval of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill should be overturned. A Wall Street Journal poll this month found 66% of voters opposed revoking approval of the drug, while 25% supported it.\par \par \uc2 Florida GOP Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who is expected to enter the race for president in the coming months, signed legislation in April that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gov-ron-desantis-signs-florida-six-week-abortion-ban-b18029cc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bans most abortions in his state after six weeks }}}\uc2  of pregnancy. The law has limited exceptions, including for rape and incest, and for certain medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 The move could boost him with the GOP base in the primary contests but might be a liability in a general election. The WSJ poll found a majority of voters opposed a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, 53% to 41%. Eight in 10 Democrats opposed the ban, as did 56% of independent voters. Meanwhile, 71% of Republicans supported the restrictions.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What impact do you think the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue will have on the GOP presidential primary? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Republicans performed worse than expected in the 2022 midterm elections, which came several months after the court's decision to overturn Roe v. Wade. While Republicans did pick up the House majority, it was by a narrower margin than most analysts predicted. Democrats picked up a Senate seat and three governor mansions compared with Republicans' one.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/why-independent-voters-broke-for-democrats-in-the-midterms-11668249002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Independent voters swung toward Democrats }}}\uc2  by wide margins in some of the most competitive Senate races in Pennsylvania, Arizona and Georgia, states that will be key to the presidential election in 2024.\par \par \uc2 "We lost a lot of seats we could have won last year, and 2024 is going to be a dogfight. If we want to win, we want to win the popular vote, this sure as hell is not going to do it," Rep. Nancy Mace (R., S.C.) said about the GOP push for more \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, including the Florida ban.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Mace said she supports restrictions after 15 weeks but believes the Republican Party also needs to back exceptions and access to birth control if they want to regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Ms. Mace, who comes from the third state in the GOP nominating contest, hasn't endorsed a candidate for president.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, South Carolina Sen. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , who endorsed Mr. Trump, pushed again Friday for the Senate to take up his legislation for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban after 15 weeks. The bill includes exceptions for rape, incest and life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 "I hope the Republican Party can muster the courage to oppose late-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  like we have done in the past," he tweeted.\par \par \uc2 Other Republican hopefuls say they oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but have been vague in how far they are willing to go.\par \par \uc2 As governor of South Carolina, Nikki Haley signed into law a ban on most abortions after 20 weeks, with no exceptions for rape or incest. The former United Nations ambassador is set to give a speech on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week in Arlington, Va.\par \par \uc2 South Carolina Sen. Tim Scott, who has an exploratory committee for president, has said he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/tim-scott-republican-president-new-hampshire-abortion-fe4edf79d4a1aa0dc77b8625e8e14135"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supports a 20-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban }}}\uc2 . But he avoided specifics when asked whether he supports a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/video/sen-tim-scott-speaks-to-nbc-news-after-launching-2024-presidential-exploratory-committee-170310725719"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 telling NBC News }}}\uc2  he would sign "the most conservative, pro-life legislation that they can get through Congress," should he become president.\par \par \uc2 Former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  has said he supports a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and wanted the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill to be taken off the market.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood Votes, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights organization that spent $45 million in the 2020 election cycle, said it was focused on increasing awareness of the GOP candidates' records, portraying them as extreme.\par \par \uc2 "They have painted themselves into a corner they cannot get out of, and we know where they stand. They are all antiabortion politicians," said Jenny Lawson, the group's executive director.\par \par \uc2 Aaron Zitner contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Eliza Collins at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:eliza.collins@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliza.collins@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230423ej4n0008l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
