\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Supreme Court Allows  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Pill Mifepristone to Stay on the Market; Justices block lower-court order that would have imposed new limits on drug\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Jess Bravin \par \uc2 1,051 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 April 2023\par 02:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14The Supreme Court on Friday allowed the widely used \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-access-case-texas-judge-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mifepristone to remain on the market }}}\uc2  indefinitely, granting emergency requests from the Biden administration and the brand-name manufacturer of the drug.\par \par \uc2 The high court blocked the effect of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-approval-suspended-by-u-s-judge-3c5c88cf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lower-court orders }}}\uc2  that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-action-expected-in-abortion-pill-case-7e0ac390"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would have limited access }}}\uc2  to the pill, which is used in more than half of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 U.S. abortions }}}\uc2 . The Supreme Court's action wasn't a decision on the merits of the case; instead, the justices were deciding whether the pill could remain available during a continuing legal challenge brought by antiabortion groups.\par \par \uc2 The court's order was unsigned and provided no reasoning, as is typical in emergency actions. But it indicated that \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved access to mifepristone would remain until litigation concludes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-battle-returns-to-the-courtroom-b163f075"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the lower courts }}}\uc2  and the Supreme Court itself has an opportunity to review those decisions\u8212\'20\'14a timeline that likely will take many months.\par \par \uc2 Two justices indicated they would have left the lower court order in place: \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a brief dissent, Justice Alito said neither the \uc2 FDA\uc2  nor the drug's maker had demonstrated they would suffer harm from limiting access to mifepristone. Besides, he said, there were "legitimate doubts" the government would obey lower-court orders restricting the drug, or that "it would choose to take enforcement actions to which it has strong objections."\par \par \uc2 Medical associations and individual doctors who oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lawsuit-filed-to-reverse-approval-access-to-abortion-pill-11668796816"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued the Food and Drug Administration }}}\uc2  in November, contesting the agency's initial approval of the pill in 2000, as well as more recent regulations that made the drug easier to obtain.\par \par \uc2 The case has moved rapidly from a courthouse in Amarillo, Texas, where a U.S. District Court judge appointed by former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  suspended the pill's approval, to the high court in a matter of weeks. In between, the New Orleans-based Fifth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals narrowed the Texas judge's injunction somewhat but ordered the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to reimpose a pre-2016 regimen for administering the drug. That included {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/appeals-court-rules-abortion-pill-mifepristone-can-remain-temporarily-available-912b03ad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 limiting its use }}}\uc2  to the earliest weeks of pregnancy, requiring three doctors' visits, precluding mailing pills to patients and reintroducing a higher dosage than what is now used.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court's order negated all of those limits. The Biden administration and Danco Laboratories LLC, which sells the pill under the brand name Mifeprex, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-faces-swift-new-abortion-test-with-mifepristone-case-b79b2a7e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed emergency appeals }}}\uc2  last week asking the court to intervene.\par \par \uc2 The Fifth Circuit is set to hear arguments in the case in mid-May and issue a more detailed ruling after that.\par \par \uc2 The case presented the Supreme Court with its first major test on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since its June ruling in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization }}}\uc2  ended federal constitutional protections for the procedure. Since then, more than a dozen states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have banned many or most abortions. }}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Pill: State Battlegrounds\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/story/states-are-next-battlegrounds-for-abortion-pill-access-8abde763"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The patchwork of state laws restricting medication \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 The mifepristone litigation has nationwide implications because a ruling against the \uc2 FDA\uc2  would reduce \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in states that have maintained protections for the procedure post-Dobbs. Providers in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal have relied on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill to help meet increased demand. Some states have been amassing stockpiles of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs, in case court decisions limit future availability.\par \par \uc2 President Biden said the Supreme Court's action would ensure access to the pill while the administration continues its battle in court. "The stakes could not be higher for women across America. I will continue to fight politically driven attacks on women's health," he said.\par \par \uc2 Danco attorney Jessica Ellsworth said, "The lower courts' reversal of longstanding \uc2 FDA\uc2  approvals has caused widespread chaos among providers, patients, and healthcare systems. Today's order provides continuity to all concerned as we litigate the underlying issues in this case."\par \par \uc2 The challengers have argued that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  improperly approved mifepristone under a pathway used to treat serious or life-threatening illnesses and failed to adequately consider potential safety concerns.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 FDA\uc2  must answer for the damage it has caused to the health of countless women and girls and the rule of law by failing to study how dangerous the chemical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug regimen is," said Erik Baptist, an attorney with the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , which represents the plaintiffs. "We look forward to a final outcome in this case that will hold the \uc2 FDA\uc2  accountable."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  said it had extensive safety data that supported the drug's approval in 2000 and later rules making the pill easier to obtain, noting that more than 5 million American women have used the pill over the past two decades. The Justice Department, representing the \uc2 FDA\uc2  in court, also argued the plaintiffs waited too long to sue and didn't have standing to challenge the drug's approval because their claims rested on speculation they might one day treat a woman experiencing complications from the drug.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How might the fight over access to mifepristone affect the national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  landscape? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 The department also has said the ruling could affect the drug's use in miscarriage management.\par \par \uc2 Voters overwhelmingly opposed overturning \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of mifepristone when asked in a Wall Street Journal poll this month. Some 66% said they didn't want approval of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill to be reversed, while 25% favored a reversal of the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval.\par \par \uc2 Democrats and independent voters in the survey opposed overturning the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval by lopsided margins, while Republicans narrowly favored a reversal of the \uc2 FDA\uc2  decision, 46% to 39%.\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone is part of a two-step regimen. Up to two days after taking the drug, women usually take misoprostol, which causes uterine contractions. The lower-court orders don't affect misoprostol, which isn't \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own but could be prescribed off-label. Researchers say women seeking a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/story/states-are-next-battlegrounds-for-abortion-pill-access-8abde763"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 medication \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  could take misoprostol alone, but it is less effective and can cause more significant side effects.\par \par \uc2 Aaron Zitner and Liz Essley Whyte contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Jess Bravin at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jess.Bravin@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jess.Bravin@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230421ej4l00131\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
