\par\par \uc2 Review & Outlook (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The Supreme Court's  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Pill Reprieve; Democrats suddenly praise a Court they otherwise claim is 'illegitimate.'\b0\par\par\uc2 By The Editorial Board \par \uc2 569 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 April 2023\par 19:18 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 America's supposed descent into "The Handmaid's Tale" was put on pause Friday after the Supreme Court stayed a lower-court order restricting access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone. Note the irony of progressives praising the same High Court they call a threat to democracy and women's rights.\par \par \uc2 FDA v. Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine arrived on the Court's emergency docket after a district court judge issued a nationwide injunction against the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 's 2000 mifepristone approval and later relaxation of safety protocols. A Fifth Circuit Court of Appeals panel let the drug stay on the market but blocked the dispensing rule changes.\par \par \uc2 While the Court didn't explain its reasoning for granting the stay, a nationwide injunction is an extraordinary remedy that lower-court judges have often been too quick to grant. The balance of legal equities and public interest also doesn't appear to favor the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  plaintiffs, and it seems unlikely they will ultimately succeed on the merits.\par \par \uc2 As we've written, the role of judges doesn't include second-guessing the FDA's judgments unless it violates procedure or the law. It's also questionable whether the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  physicians have demonstrated a sufficiently concrete injury that is traceable to the FDA's actions to have legal standing to sue.\par \par \uc2 Justices \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  dissented from the stay. While Justice Thomas didn't explain his thinking, Justice Alito made some valid points about procedural issues without expressing a view on the merits of the case. He hoisted the liberal Justices on their past criticisms of the Court's conservatives for deciding cases on the emergency docket.\par \par \uc2 "In recent cases, this Court has been lambasted for staying a District Court order 'based on the scanty review this Court gives matters on its shadow docket,'" he noted, citing a dissent by Justice \uc2 Elena Kagan\uc2 . "I did not agree with these criticisms at the time, but if they were warranted in the cases in which they were made, they are emphatically true here."\par \par \uc2 Immediate impact from the injunction might also have been minimal because the FDA would need to act to remove the drug from the market, Justice Alito points out. But "the Government has not dispelled legitimate doubts that it would even obey an unfavorable order in these cases, much less that it would choose to take enforcement actions to which it has strong objections."\par \par \uc2 Here's looking at you, \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2 . The Oregon Senator, other Democrats and South Carolina GOP Rep. Nancy Mace urged the FDA to ignore the lower-court injunction on the premise that the U.S. legal process can't be trusted. Well, apparently it can. "Tonight we breathe a collective sigh of relief," Mr. Wyden tweeted Friday. Note all three Trump-appointed Justices backed the stay.\par \par \uc2 The Fifth Circuit has fast-tracked the case and will hold oral arguments on the government's appeal next month. That means the High Court could hear the case next term with a decision coming by the summer of 2024. Democrats must be elated because this will keep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics in the news during the 2024 campaign season and put Republicans on defense. No wonder they are cheering the Supreme Court they otherwise claim is "illegitimate."\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230422ej4m001md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
