\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 GOP 2024 Hopefuls Scott, DeSantis, Pence Aim to Gain on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  by Wooing Evangelicals; Spiritual references, conservative policy show importance of the group\b0\par\par\uc2 By John McCormick and Eliza Collins \par \uc2 1,080 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par 13:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CEDAR RAPIDS, Iowa\u8212\'20\'14Sen. Tim Scott's language was heavy with spiritual references during a recent speech here in the state that will start the Republican presidential nomination balloting early next year.\par \par \uc2 Moving amid tables of GOP activists assembled in a country club ballroom, like a minister who had stepped down from the pulpit, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/republican-sen-tim-scott-prepares-for-presidential-run-cd0078f1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Carolina senator }}}\uc2  thanked "God almighty," talked of "false prophets," spoke of "redemption" and "blessings" and thanked "God almighty" again.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Scott had met privately a few hours earlier with more than 50 pastors. His team also sent a suggested prayer for his potential candidacy to followers last week when he announced an exploratory committee for president.\par \par \uc2 It was all part of an effort to court evangelical Christians, one of the most influential groups in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/republicans-worry-democrats-could-crash-iowa-gop-caucuses-5d32e8cb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iowa's caucuses }}}\uc2  and South Carolina's primary, the first and third contests in the GOP nomination process. In 2016, the last time a competitive caucus was held on the GOP side, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://graphics.wsj.com/elections/2016/iowa-caucus-entrance-polls/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 almost two-thirds of participants }}}\uc2  said in entrance polls that they considered themselves evangelical Christians.\par \par \uc2 While former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Florida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  are the early front-runners for the nomination, evangelicals could sway the 2024 primary race, if they solidify their support around a single candidate.\par \par \uc2 Candidates and potential candidates are talking about school choice, "religious liberty" and other topics that resonate with evangelicals, while also highlighting their own personal journeys with faith.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump won the hearts of many social conservatives by nominating three justices to the Supreme Court who helped {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturn the constitutional right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , but some evangelical voters question whether he is the GOP's best option to win a general election.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think they are abandoning him, but they have got an open mind," said Steve Scheffler, a \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  member and president of an Iowa group of social conservatives that is sponsoring a candidate forum Saturday.\par \par \uc2 In the 2016 Iowa caucuses, Mr. Trump won 22% support among voters who described themselves as born again or evangelical, entrance polls showed, well below the 34% scored among the group by Sen. Ted Cruz of Texas, who narrowly won the caucuses that year.\par \par \uc2 Nationally, white evangelical Christians have declined as a share of all Americans but accounted for more than 20% of voters in the 2020 elections. They supplied 37% of Mr. Trump's total votes, compared with 8% of President Biden's total, according to AP VoteCast, a large survey of the electorate that year.\par \par \uc2 This weekend's event, sponsored by the Iowa Faith and Freedom Coalition, is expected to draw more than 1,000 social conservatives as well as Mr. Scott, former Vice President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/pence-plots-2024-bid-as-jan-6-hearings-remind-voters-of-his-break-from-trump-11655471256"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Pence }}}\uc2 , former Arkansas Gov. Asa Hutchinson and other current and potential 2024 candidates. Mr. Trump is expected to address the group by video.\par \par \uc2 The Iowa gathering comes as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-ruling-draws-muted-response-from-gop-71bbdda9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the issue of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  remains dominant in the nation's political conversation. Opposing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "a waterline measurement. If a candidate does not understand that protection of life is essential, then we cannot support them," said Penny Nance, the chief executive of Concerned Women for America, an evangelical Christian organization.\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeSantis, who is expected to enter the race in May or June and isn't attending the Iowa gathering, last week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-gov-ron-desantis-signs-15-week-abortion-ban-into-law-11649961049"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed legislation }}}\uc2  that bans most abortions in his state after six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Scott has avoided specifics when asked whether he supports a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/video/sen-tim-scott-speaks-to-nbc-news-after-launching-2024-presidential-exploratory-committee-170310725719"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 telling NBC News }}}\uc2  he would sign "the most conservative, pro-life legislation that they can get through Congress" should he become president. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
