\par \par \uc2 Sen. Tim Scott arrives for a service at Seacoast Church in Mount Pleasant, S.C. PHOTO: Lauren Petracca for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Support for greater restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is high among social conservatives but could prove damaging in a general election. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters swung toward Democratic candidates in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/why-independent-voters-broke-for-democrats-in-the-midterms-11668249002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2022 midterm elections }}}\uc2  and the race for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-shows-abortion-continues-to-sway-voters-4e47297c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Wisconsin Supreme Court seat this month }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump supported \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights before he ran for president. His campaign issued a statement Tuesday saying the issue should be decided at the state level and that he supports exceptions for rape, incest and life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Pence, who like Mr. Scott hasn't formally entered the race, has met with Iowa clergy and frequently cites scripture.\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeSantis spoke last week to roughly 10,000 students at \uc2 Liberty University\uc2  in Virginia, one of the nation's largest Christian schools, but declined to highlight the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation he had signed the previous day.\par \par \uc2 While evangelical support was divided in the 2016 primary, Mr. Trump went on to enjoy broad support from the group during his presidency. Some cracks, however, have started to show.\par \par \uc2 Tony Beam, the public policy director for the South Carolina Southern Baptist Convention, said he would rather see someone other than Mr. Trump win the nomination.\par \par \uc2 "I just don't think that is the best thing for the party," he said of Mr. Trump. "I don't think it is the best thing for the country."\par \par \uc2 Still, many of Mr. Trump's supporters remain loyal. Mark Burns, a pastor from South Carolina who advises Mr. Trump, said the other candidates may say the right things, but the former president has a record of pushing policies important to evangelical voters. "You know what you're going to get with President Trump," he said.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Which current or likely GOP presidential candidate has a message that will resonate best with evangelical voters? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Scott, who grew up poor and struggled in school, has said the support of his mother and a mentor, a \uc2 Chick-fil-A\uc2  operator named John Moniz, turned his life around and taught him conservative principles and shared the importance of faith.\par \par \uc2 In an interview, Mr. Scott, the only Black Senate Republican, said his life story could resonate especially well with evangelical voters.\par \par \uc2 "My faith journey has been one that has changed my life, from being a person, as a young teenager, who was self-centered and sometimes angry and disillusioned to someone who is hope-filled, based on the teaching of Jesus," he said.\par \par \uc2 Write to John McCormick at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:mccormick.john@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mccormick.john@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Eliza Collins at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:eliza.collins@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliza.collins@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230420ej4k0020a\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
