\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Supreme Court Lets  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Pill Remain on Market for Two More Days; Justices weigh requests by Biden administration, drugmaker Danco Laboratories to preserve mifepristone access\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto, Jess Bravin and  Liz Essley Whyte \par \uc2 1,169 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 April 2023\par 21:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14The Supreme Court allowed the widely used {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-faces-fresh-deadline-in-abortion-pill-case-6d7b9049"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill mifepristone  }}}\uc2  to remain on the market through Friday, while the justices continue to weigh whether to block a lower-court order that would limit access to the drug.\par \par \uc2 The extension came in a pair of brief orders issued Wednesday by Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  , who oversees emergency matters for the courts in Texas, where a lawsuit contesting the pill's approval originated.\par \par \uc2 The justices are considering {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-faces-swift-new-abortion-test-with-mifepristone-case-b79b2a7e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 emergency appeals from the Biden administration  }}}\uc2  and Danco Laboratories LLC, the brand-name manufacturer of the pill, to keep the drug on the market during ongoing litigation over its approval more than 20 years ago by the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  . Antiabortion groups filed a lawsuit in November challenging the original approval and more recent regulations that made the pill, which is used in more than half of abortions, easier to obtain.\par \par \uc2 A U.S. District Court judge in Amarillo, Texas, issued an order earlier this month that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-approval-suspended-by-u-s-judge-3c5c88cf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspended the pill's approval  }}}\uc2 . The New Orleans-based Fifth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals last week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/appeals-court-rules-abortion-pill-mifepristone-can-remain-temporarily-available-912b03ad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 narrowed the scope of that ruling  }}}\uc2 , but reimposed restrictions that were in place before 2016, when the pill was only approved through about seven weeks of pregnancy, required three in-person doctor's visits and couldn't be sent to patients through the mail.\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs, antiabortion medical associations and individual doctors, argued that women would still have access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill under the pre-2016 framework, saying the Fifth Circuit had merely reintroduced some basic guardrails. "The only effect of the lower court's order is to restore a modicum of safety for the women and girls who use the drug, including supervision and oversight by a physician," they wrote in a filing to the Supreme Court. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw480\pich480\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal7200\pichgoal7200
