\par \par \uc2 PHOTO: kara dapena/the wall street journal\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Pill: State Battlegrounds\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/story/states-are-next-battlegrounds-for-abortion-pill-access-8abde763"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The patchwork of state laws restricting medication \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 Their lawsuit argued the \uc2 FDA\uc2  had improperly approved the drug in 2000 under a pathway used for medications that treat serious or life-threatening illnesses. Pregnancy, they argued, isn't an illness. They also said the agency had failed to take seriously potential safety concerns about the drug, particularly as it loosened certain protocols for its use over the past seven years.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  says the drug's approval was supported by a detailed safety analysis and subsequent changes were based on dozens of studies that demonstrated the pill's safety. The Justice Department also has argued that the plaintiffs waited too long to sue and don't have standing to challenge the drug's approval because their claims are based on speculation that they might one day treat a woman experiencing complications from the drug.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration and Danco said the appeals-court order usurped the authority of the \uc2 FDA\uc2  and would have serious consequences for women who need access to the drug, and for the pharmaceutical industry. Both the government and the company said they couldn't easily roll back the clock to 2016 and there was a risk the drug would be unavailable for some period of time.\par \par \uc2 The case has presented the Supreme Court with its first major test on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since its ruling last June in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended federal constitutional protections  }}}\uc2  for the procedure. Since then, more than a dozen states have banned many or most abortions. The court's conservative majority in Dobbs said it intended to return the issue to the states, but this latest legal battle has created nationwide turmoil.\par \par \uc2 The justices have three primary options. They could grant the emergency requests and leave mifepristone on the market indefinitely during litigation, which could preserve the status quo for many months. They could leave the pill in place temporarily and agree to review the case in full, even though lower courts aren't done reviewing it. Or they could deny the emergency appeals outright. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
