\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court had temporarily blocked lower court orders that would have limited access to mifepristone. PHOTO: Michael Noble Jr. for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 If the Supreme Court doesn't intervene, the Fifth Circuit order could send the \uc2 FDA\uc2  , drugmakers and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers rushing to implement new restrictions and potentially pause availability altogether.\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for Danco said the company would await guidance from the \uc2 FDA\uc2  on how to sell its drug if it needs to comply with the pre-2016 requirements, and whether it needs to tap the brake on sales while it reverts labels, packaging, doses and more to their earlier versions\u8212\'20\'14a process that could take months and prove expensive for the company.\par \par \uc2 Separately Wednesday, the maker of a generic form of the pill sued the \uc2 FDA\uc2  and others in an attempt to ensure its product can remain on the market even if court decisions threatening its approval go into effect.\par \par \uc2 GenBioPro Inc., a Nevada company that says it supplies roughly two-thirds of the mifepristone used for abortions in the U.S., argues the \uc2 FDA\uc2  doesn't have the power to remove its drug from the market immediately, without following certain legal procedures.\par \par \uc2 GenBioPro said customers canceled orders after the Biden administration represented to the Supreme Court that the recent lower-court decisions would result in mifepristone being "misbranded."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  said it doesn't comment on pending litigation.\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone also has other uses, including for miscarriage management.\par \par \uc2 If the \uc2 FDA\uc2  is required to impose new restrictions on the pill, it will likely create a patchwork of access around the country, according to attorneys and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers. In liberal-leaning states and counties, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers might be more willing to prescribe the drug off-label under relaxed conditions, but in places with more conservative legislatures and prosecutors, even where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still otherwise legal, that might be risky.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Should mifepristone remain available during ongoing litigation over the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill? Why or why not? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Adding more complexity, a federal judge in Washington state recently issued an order precluding the \uc2 FDA\uc2  from further restricting access to the drug in 17 states and the District of Columbia. Providers in those states might have to grapple with how to reconcile the different decisions.\par \par \uc2 "On the other side of this chaos are patients, people who need healthcare," said Rabia Muqaddam, a senior staff attorney at the \uc2 Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  , an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights group.\par \par \uc2 A number of states, including New York, California and Washington, said they would stockpile \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs in preparation for a court ruling taking effect that could make the pills more difficult to obtain.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\uc2 , Jess Bravin at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jess.Bravin@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jess.Bravin@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Liz Essley Whyte at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:liz.whyte@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 liz.whyte@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Liz Essley Whyte at \par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230419ej4j000p4\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
