\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  Signs Florida Six-Week  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban; Bill's signature by presidential hopeful shows Republicans aren't shying away from strict  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  limits\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Arian Campo-Flores \par \uc2 809 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2023\par 11:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Florida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  late Thursday signed into law a bill banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy, a strict measure that could earn him support from Republican primary voters if he runs for president but that also carries {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-pill-ruling-ignites-new-national-battle-a9c03329"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 political risks among the broader electorate.  }}}\uc2  late Thursday signed into law a bill banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy, a strict measure that could earn him support from Republican primary voters if he runs for president but that also carries\par \par \uc2 The legislation was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-abortion-ban-law-28c65d8c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a priority this session for the state's Republican-led legislature,  }}}\uc2  and political observers think it could boost Mr. DeSantis's prospects in a presidential primary. Antiabortion leaders said it would also help assuage concerns that Mr. DeSantis has lagged behind some other Republicans nationally in fighting for restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "There's been kind of a concern about, is he a fighter on this issue?" said \uc2 Kristan Hawkins\uc2 , president of Students for Life of America.\par \par \uc2 In a statement released after he signed the bill, Gov. DeSantis said, "We are proud to support life and family in the state of Florida."\par \par \uc2 The law has limited exceptions, including for rape and incest, and for certain medical emergencies. It isn't poised to take effect immediately but is contingent on any of several potential occurrences, most notably the state Supreme Court ruling that the state constitution contains no right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a pending case challenging the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-gov-ron-desantis-signs-15-week-abortion-ban-into-law-11649961049"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 current 15-week ban.  }}}\par \par \uc2 A strict ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Florida further unsettles the national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  landscape during a tumultuous week in which questions about the future of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/appeals-court-rules-abortion-pill-mifepristone-can-remain-temporarily-available-912b03ad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are headed for the U.S. Supreme Court.  }}}\par \par \uc2 Florida has seen one of the largest increases in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade last June  }}}\uc2 , with on average nearly 1,200 more abortions a month than before the ruling, according to WeCount, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -data project sponsored by the Society of Family Planning, which supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 A number of those women will now likely have to travel to states such as North Carolina and Illinois, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/women-encounter-abortion-delays-as-clinics-draw-patients-from-out-of-state-f40e318b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 where providers have been struggling to cope with demand.  }}}\par \par \uc2 "This is a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Florida has been serving an increased number of patients from the South since Roe v. Wade fell. It will be increasingly difficult for people to receive care," said Laura Goodhue, executive director of the Florida Alliance of Planned Parenthood Affiliates.\par \par \uc2 Unlike other cultural issues like instruction on sexual orientation in schools, on which the governor has been outspoken and assertive, he has been quieter on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . When he campaigned for re-election in November, he was vague about what specific restrictions he supported and declined, when pressed, to specify after what week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be banned.\par \par \uc2 After Mr. DeSantis won re-election and attention turned to a potential 2024 presidential run, he began to come under greater pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue.\par \par \uc2 "It's not surprising he didn't stake out a position before his re-election. Now he's not focusing on what Florida voters want in this way. He's focusing on what GOP primary voters want," said Mary Ziegler, a law professor at \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 The bill earlier Thursday passed the Florida House 70 to 40, mostly along party lines with a handful of Republicans voting against it. It passed the Senate earlier this month, also with a couple of Republican senators in more vulnerable districts voting against it.\par \par \uc2 While signing the bill might help Mr. DeSantis's chances in a potential Republican primary, heavily restricting the procedure might pose political risks for Republican legislators in Florida. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unf.edu/coas/porl/_files/polls/statewide/certified.rf.UNF-Mar-Statewide-2023.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A poll in March by the University of North Florida  }}}\uc2  found that 75% of Floridians opposed banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  starting at six weeks of pregnancy\u8212\'20\'14albeit with no exceptions for rape and incest.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups disagree that the bill will prove unpopular, pointing out that Republicans won a landslide election in November for the governorship and legislature after passing a 15-week bill.\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeSantis's signature on a bill banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy also could pose challenges for him in a national presidential election, if he gets that far, political observers said.\par \par \uc2 Since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  overturned Roe v. Wade, at least a dozen states have banned many or most abortions. But Republican leaders have at times received political blowback on the issue, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-shows-abortion-continues-to-sway-voters-4e47297c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including in the recent Wisconsin Supreme Court election  }}}\uc2  and the November midterms.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jennifer Calfas contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Arian Campo-Flores at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:arian.campo-flores@dowjones.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arian.campo-flores@dowjones.com  }}}\uc2  and Arian Campo-Flores at \par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230414ej4e001gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
