\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Florida Lawmakers Pass Six-Week  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban; Bill's swift passage shows that Republicans aren't shying away from strict  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  limits, despite recent political blowback\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto, Arian Campo-Flores and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 1,193 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 April 2023\par 21:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Florida legislators on Thursday passed a bill banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy, a strict measure that indicates Republicans aren't backing away from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/appeals-court-rules-abortion-pill-mifepristone-can-remain-temporarily-available-912b03ad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 efforts to curtail \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\uc2  even in states where such efforts may carry political risks.\par \par \uc2 The final hurdle for the bill is a signature from Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , a likely Republican presidential candidate who has said he would sign legislation limiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it crosses his desk.\par \par \uc2 If enacted, the bill would ban most abortions in the state with limited exceptions, including for rape and incest and for certain medical emergencies. That will significantly curtail \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the South, where Florida has been a major provider of abortions.\par \par \uc2 The bill passed the House by a margin of 70 to 40, mostly along party lines with a handful of Republicans voting against it. It passed the Senate earlier this month, also with a couple of Republican senators in more vulnerable districts voting against it.\par \par \uc2 "We have the opportunity to lead the national debate about the importance of protecting life," said Rep. Jenna Persons-Mulicka, a Republican, moments before lawmakers voted Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The bill isn't poised to take effect immediately but is contingent on any of several potential occurrences, most notably the state Supreme Court clearing the way for the legislation by ruling that the state constitution contains no right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in a pending case challenging the current 15-week ban.\par \par \uc2 Democrats who opposed the bill said during the debate that they believed popular opinion was on their side. "People in Florida deserve more from their elected officials," said Rep. Yvonne Hayes Hinson, a Democrat.\par \par \uc2 The legislation was a top priority this session for Florida's Republican-led legislature, and political observers think it could boost {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/down-in-polls-and-taking-flak-from-donald-trump-ron-desantis-looks-to-rebound-9bf13a27"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mr. DeSantis's prospects in a presidential primary}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As a potential presidential candidate, Mr. DeSantis "needs a strong pro-life victory. Fifteen weeks won't cut it when you compare him to other candidates," said John Stemberger, president and general counsel of Florida Family Policy Council, an antiabortion group.\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeSantis hasn't been vocal about plans to sign a six-week bill. But Florida lawmakers and party strategists say that given the governor's strong sway over state GOP lawmakers, they wouldn't have filed such a bill if he weren't supportive of it.\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeSantis's office didn't respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 The legislation's swift passage in Florida\u8212\'20\'14a longtime battleground state that has tilted toward the GOP in recent election cycles\u8212\'20\'14indicates that Republicans continue to view \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a winning issue, at least with some key voters.\par \par \uc2 "It's just a bellwether for where the rest of the GOP is going to go on this," said Mary Ziegler, a law professor at \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2 . "This is some Republicans saying this isn't popular but we're going to do it anyway. We need the primary voters."\par \par \uc2 Since the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade last June, roughly a dozen states have banned most abortions. But voters have at times pushed back on efforts to impose strict limits on the procedure, as evidenced by the recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-shows-abortion-continues-to-sway-voters-4e47297c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin Supreme Court election}}}\uc2  and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-abortion-vote-results-11659440554"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 referendum last summer in Kansas.}}}\uc2 The issue also appears to have hurt the GOP in the November midterms.\par \par \uc2 Heavily restricting the procedure may pose political risks for Republicans in Florida as well. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unf.edu/coas/porl/_files/polls/statewide/certified.rf.UNF-Mar-Statewide-2023.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A poll in March by the University of North Florida}}}\uc2  found that 75% of Floridians opposed banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  starting at six weeks of pregnancy\u8212\'20\'14albeit with no exceptions for rape and incest.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups disagree that the bill will prove unpopular, pointing to Mr. DeSantis's resounding re-election victory after he signed the 15-week bill.\par \par \uc2 For months after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade}}}\uc2 , the path to a strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban seemed far from preordained as prominent Republicans in the state seemed cautious on the issue. Senate President Kathleen Passidomo had said she supported a 12-week ban and urged lawmakers to wait until the state Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-pauses-on-more-abortion-restrictions-following-supreme-court-decision-11656591626"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled on the challenge}}}\uc2  to the 15-week ban.\par \par \uc2 When Mr. DeSantis campaigned for re-election in November, he was vague about what specific new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions he supported. During an October debate against Democrat \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2 , he declined, when pressed, to specify after what week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be banned.\par \par \uc2 After he won re-election and attention turned to a potential 2024 presidential run, Mr. DeSantis began to come under greater pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue. In a January interview with CBS News, South Dakota Gov. Kristi Noem, another potential 2024 presidential contender, said her state's near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a model for the GOP and encouraged Republican governors such as Mr. DeSantis to further restrict the procedure. Earlier that month, Ms. Noem's chief of communications, Ian Fury, accused Mr. DeSantis of "hiding behind a 15-week ban."\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion leaders also said Mr. DeSantis needs a strong record on the issue in a potential matchup against former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who can boast that he secured the strong conservative Supreme Court majority that voted to end federal constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Unlike other cultural issues, such as instruction on sexual orientation in schools, on which the governor has been outspoken and assertive, he has been quieter on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I think the clear answer is that Gov. DeSantis is running for president, and in order to compete in a primary against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , he has to be extreme on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Democratic state Rep. \uc2 Anna Eskamani\uc2 . "I think he knows it's politically unpopular, and that's why he's fidgety when he talks about it."\par \par \uc2 Florida has seen one of the largest increases in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the Supreme Court ruling last June, with on average nearly 1,200 more abortions a month than before the ruling, according to WeCount, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -data project sponsored by the Society of Family Planning, which supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 A number of those women will now likely have to travel to states such as North Carolina and Illinois, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/women-encounter-abortion-delays-as-clinics-draw-patients-from-out-of-state-f40e318b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 where providers have already been struggling to cope with demand. }}}\par \par \uc2 A Woman's Choice, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Jacksonville, Fla., added an additional day to its schedule and hired more staff to accommodate an increase in patients coming in from Alabama, Georgia, Louisiana, Mississippi and Texas, said Kelly Flynn, the clinic's president and chief executive. Ms. Flynn said clinic staff plan to refer patients to their other locations in North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 "It's so unpredictable," Ms. Flynn said. "We don't know what's going to happen from day to day if we're in the middle of clinic and suddenly a bill is signed and now we have to stop seeing patients."\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com}}}\uc2 , Arian Campo-Flores at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:arian.campo-flores@dowjones.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arian.campo-flores@dowjones.com}}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230413ej4d005pl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
