\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Justice Department to Appeal to Supreme Court on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Pill; Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  says agency disagrees with appeals-court ruling that allows pill to stay on market but with restrictions\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Liz Essley Whyte \par \uc2 1,472 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 April 2023\par 23:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-battle-returns-to-the-courtroom-b163f075"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fast-moving legal battle  }}}\uc2  over the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill is heading to the Supreme Court after a federal appeals court allowed the drug to remain on the market but imposed significant restrictions on its use.\par \par \uc2 The order issued by the New Orleans-based Fifth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals late Wednesday in effect returns restrictions on the drug, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-access-case-texas-judge-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 known as mifepristone  }}}\uc2 , to what they were before 2016, when the pill could only be used through about seven weeks of pregnancy, required three in-person doctor's visits and couldn't be sent to patients through the mail.\par \par \uc2 In the years since, women have been able to take the pill through about 10 weeks of pregnancy, and it has been much easier to acquire. Changes during the pandemic allowed patients to make telehealth appointments and receive the pills through the mail without ever seeing a physician in person. The pill, approved in 2000, is used in more than half of abortions in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  said Thursday that the Justice Department strongly disagreed with the ruling and would look to the high court. "We will be seeking emergency relief from the Supreme Court to defend the \uc2 FDA\uc2  's scientific judgment and protect Americans' access to safe and effective reproductive care," Mr. Garland said.\par \par \uc2 That appeal will place the justices back in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  spotlight months after they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overruled Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2  and sought to return the issue to the states.\par \par \uc2 The Fifth Circuit's action comes after U.S. District Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk in Amarillo, Texas, ruled last Friday that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-the-texas-courts-abortion-pill-ruling-means-for-fda-c117f015"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 U.S. Food and Drug Administration  }}}\uc2  had improperly approved the drug under a pathway used for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-approval-suspended-by-u-s-judge-3c5c88cf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 medications to treat life-threatening illnesses  }}}\uc2  and had failed to adequately assess its safety. He put his ruling on hold for a week to give the parties an opportunity to appeal.\par \par \uc2 A divided three-judge panel on the Fifth Circuit declined to block the original approval of mifepristone but said antiabortion plaintiffs had presented legitimate arguments that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  had failed to properly scrutinize more recent changes that loosened access to the drug.\par \par \uc2 The panel majority said it appeared that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  had failed to examine relevant data and possibly serious drug side effects, as it eased restrictions on the pill. "This ostrich's-head-in-the-sand approach is deeply troubling," the panel said.\par \par \uc2 The legal uncertainty over the pill comes as the nation is still adjusting to the Supreme Court's ruling last summer that overruled Roe. State-by-state rules continue to change. In Florida, lawmakers on Thursday passed a bill banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy, a measure that could significantly limit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state and throughout much of the Southeast.\par \par \uc2 Providers in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal have relied on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill to help meet increased demand. That might be significantly more difficult if the appeals-court order remains in place. Women who need to travel for abortions because it is illegal in their home state might struggle to meet the requirements for multiple doctors' visits. Some clinics said they might stop offering mifepristone altogether because the restrictions could make it too expensive or time-consuming.\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone is sold under the brand name Mifeprex by Danco Laboratories LLC. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  in 2019 approved a generic version of the drug, made by GenBioPro Inc., a move that might be jeopardized by the Fifth Circuit's order.\par \par \uc2 Judges Kurt Engelhardt and Andrew Oldham, both Trump appointees, were in the majority. Judge Catharina Haynes, a \uc2 George W. Bush\uc2  appointee, said she would have temporarily blocked a trial-court ruling that suspended approval of the drug and deferred other legal questions until the appeals court had more time to consider them.\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for Danco said the company "remains unchanged in its commitment to do all that we can to support and protect the availability of and access to Mifeprex for healthcare providers and all people in the United States."\par \par \uc2 Danco said it was also planning to appeal to the Supreme Court. GenBioPro said it "remains committed to lawfully making its evidence-based, essential medications available in the United States."\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups have long targeted pill access, arguing the drug is harmful to women and unborn children, and they have stepped up their antipill efforts since their blockbuster victory at the Supreme Court curtailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. As some states have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pills have proven particularly troubling for these groups because of the ease with which they can be distributed and moved across state lines.\par \par \uc2 Plaintiffs in the case were antiabortion medical associations and individual doctors.\par \par \uc2 "The 5th Circuit's decision is a significant victory for the doctors we represent, women's health, and every American who deserves an accountable federal government acting within the bounds of the law," said Erin Hawley, an attorney for the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  , the conservative legal group representing the plaintiffs.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates said the ruling will significantly restrict access and potentially force some patients to travel hundreds of miles to receive care. "This middle-of-the-night ruling, while keeping mifepristone on the market, rolls back years of medical progress," said Kirsten Moore, director of the Expanding Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access Project, an advocacy group.\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone is part of a two-step regimen. Up to two days after taking the drug, women usually take one or two doses of another drug called misoprostol, which causes uterine contractions. The court's ruling doesn't affect misoprostol, which isn't \uc2 FDA\uc2  -approved for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own but could be prescribed off-label.\par \par \uc2 Misoprostol-only medication abortions have been used globally for decades, but researchers say that alone it isn't as effective as the two-drug regimen and can cause more severe side effects.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers on Thursday said they were struggling to grapple with the Fifth Circuit ruling, including whether to prescribe misoprostol by itself.\par \par \uc2 "It's chaotic right now," said Paulina Briggs, executive director at WE Health Clinic in Duluth, Minn.\par \par \uc2 Obstetrician-gynecologist Katie McHugh was at the tail end of a 14-hour overnight hospital shift when she saw the news of the ruling. She said her clinic in Indiana, Women's Med, is deciding whether to continue offering mifepristone. Under the new rules, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  involving mifepristone would require four visits per patient when combined with state-mandated requirements. Some patients travel long distances to get to the clinic and four visits could discourage them from seeking care.\par \par \uc2 "It is so confusing, even to me," she said. "What can I do to make this slightly less confusing and less burdensome for patients?"\par \par \uc2 The case has captured nationwide attention over its potential to upend the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  landscape even in states where the procedure remains legal. At least a dozen states have banned most abortions since the Supreme Court eliminated constitutional protections for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Dozens of parties filed amicus briefs this week criticizing the judge's ruling, including pharmaceutical companies, some 240 members of Congress, 55 former high-ranking Justice Department officials and about two dozen states. Others registered support for the ruling, including some 20 states, 69 congressional Republicans and leading antiabortion groups.\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs had argued that even though their challenge to the drug's original 2000 approval appeared to be time-barred by the statute of limitations, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  had essentially reset the clock by making subsequent changes.\par \par \uc2 The appellate panel wasn't persuaded by this argument, at least for now. "Although a close call, we are unsure at this preliminary juncture and after truncated review that \uc2 FDA\uc2  reopened the 2000 Approval" with those subsequent changes, the court said.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in the decision, the Fifth Circuit raised concerns that an 150-year-old law called the Comstock Act might prohibit the mailing or shipping of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills.\par \par \uc2 The Fifth Circuit order, like last week's Texas ruling, appears to be in conflict with another decision last Friday by a federal judge in Washington state that could prevent the \uc2 FDA\uc2  from reimposing restrictions on the pill in 17 states and the District of Columbia that had sued the agency to preserve robust access.\par \par \uc2 The appeals court said it was unmoved. "We cannot embrace an argument that would, in effect, allow the decision of an out-of-circuit district court to impel us towards 'extraordinary' relief that would be otherwise inappropriate," the majority said.\par \par \uc2 Gareth Vipers, Sarah Toy and Dominique Mosbergen contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Liz Essley Whyte at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:liz.whyte@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 liz.whyte@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Liz Essley Whyte at \par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230413ej4d000m9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
