\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Pill Ruling Draws Muted Response From GOP; Republicans are wary of a political fight on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  after a string of electoral defeats in several states\b0\par\par\uc2 By Michelle Hackman \par \uc2 744 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2023\par 14:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers' muted reaction to a federal judge's ruling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-approval-suspended-by-u-s-judge-3c5c88cf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to suspend access to the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill  }}}\uc2  is the latest sign that the GOP's legal success in limiting access to abortions is causing the party political headaches.\par \par \uc2 Friday's ruling, issued by U.S. District Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk, suspends the Food and Drug Administration's approval of the pill, known as mifepristone, which is now used in a majority of abortions in the U.S. The judge, a Trump appointee who sits in Amarillo, Texas, delayed the impact of his decision for a week while the Biden administration appeals.\par \par \uc2 The highly anticipated ruling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-pill-ruling-ignites-new-national-battle-a9c03329"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was the most significant legal victory  }}}\uc2  for the antiabortion movement since the Supreme Court last year\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  as a federal legal right  }}}\uc2  and has the potential to have an even greater impact, as it could tighten access to abortions in blue states such as New York or California, where the procedure is still legal.\par \par \uc2 Democrats broadly condemned the ruling over the weekend. "Let's be clear, this is about the Republicans' goal of a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban," said Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (D., N.Y.).\par \par \uc2 Former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  , a likely presidential candidate, was one of a few Republicans to publicly comment on the judge's decision. "The \uc2 FDA\uc2  acted carelessly and with blatant disregard for human life and the well-being of American women, and today's ruling fixed a 20 year wrong," Mr. Pence said Friday.\par \par \uc2 Representatives for former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  , House Speaker Kevin McCarthy (R., Calif.), Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  (R., Ky.) and Florida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  , a presumed presidential aspirant {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-republicans-propose-abortion-ban-after-six-weeks-of-pregnancy-b42ef51"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who is considering a state bill  }}}\uc2  that would ban on abortions after six weeks of pregnancy, didn't respond to requests for comment on Friday's ruling.\par \par \uc2 Several top Republicans have sought to avoid a national political fight on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and have said the matter should be left to the states.\par \par \uc2 In contrast to the legal successes for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents, Republicans have faced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-shows-abortion-continues-to-sway-voters-4e47297c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a string of electoral defeats in state votes  }}}\uc2  related to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , worrying the GOP and bolstering Democrats as the issue continues to resonate with voters.\par \par \uc2 Political strategists of both parties {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-supporters-prevail-in-midterm-ballot-measures-11667986139"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 believe the issue played a pivotal role  }}}\uc2  in Democrats' better-than-expected showing in the 2022 midterms.\par \par \uc2 Regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, 72% of Americans oppose laws that make them illegal, according to PRRI, a nonpartisan polling firm.\par \par \uc2 Some Democratic lawmakers, including Sen. \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2  (D., Ore.) and Rep. \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  (D., N.Y.), called on the Biden administration to ignore the judge's ruling, arguing the \uc2 FDA\uc2  has the authority to do so.\par \par \uc2 "This ruling is an extreme abuse of power," Ms. Ocasio-Cortez said Sunday on CNN.\par \par \uc2 Health and Human Services Secretary \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2  , whose agency houses the \uc2 FDA\uc2  , said on CNN on Sunday that the judge's decision was reckless. "We want the courts to overturn this," he said.\par \par \uc2 When asked if the administration would consider lawmakers' call to ignore the ruling, Mr. Becerra declined to answer directly but said, "everything is on the table." It isn't clear what process the administration could follow to ignore a judge's ruling.\par \par \uc2 Rep. Tony Gonzales (R., Texas), also speaking on CNN, warned the administration against attempting such a move.\par \par \uc2 "It's very dangerous when you have the Biden administration coming out and saying they may not uphold a ruling," Mr. Gonzales said.\par \par \uc2 Last week, a progressive candidate won a race for a seat on Wisconsin's Supreme Court by more than 10 points by campaigning on overturning a 19th-century state law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in nearly all cases, further adding to concerns among some Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Sen. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  (R., S.C.), when asked on Fox News Sunday if Republicans' efforts on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions were out of step with voters, said: "In Wisconsin, you had an 1840 statute that banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pretty much across the board, and the Republican Party did not put an alternative on the table."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Graham introduced a bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lindsey-graham-defends-abortion-proposal-despite-gop-worries-11663524124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning abortions after 15 weeks  }}}\uc2  of pregnancy with some exceptions last year ahead of the midterms, a move that drew worries from his Republican colleagues about the proposal's impact ahead of the elections.\par \par \uc2 Write to Michelle Hackman at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:michelle.hackman@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 michelle.hackman@wsj.com  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230409ej4900231\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
