\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone is sold under the brand name Mifeprex and in a generic version. PHOTO: Michael Noble Jr. for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 A ruling by a Texas judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-approval-suspended-by-u-s-judge-3c5c88cf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspending approval of the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill }}}\uc2  sets off a new national fight over women's access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  less than a year after the Supreme Court withdrew constitutional protections for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.txnd.370067/gov.uscourts.txnd.370067.137.0_14.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 67-page ruling }}}\uc2  on Friday, U.S. District Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk, a Trump appointee who sits in Amarillo, said the \uc2 U.S. Food and Drug Administration\uc2  made a series of legal errors in approving the pill, known as mifepristone, for sale. He delayed the impact of his decision for a week while the Biden administration appeals and seeks an emergency stay.\par \par \uc2 If the ruling takes effect, it could block sales across the country of a pill that is currently the most common method for ending a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 As clinics have stopped offering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in roughly one-third of the states, access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/story/states-are-next-battlegrounds-for-abortion-pill-access-8abde763?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crucial battleground }}}\uc2 . Some states have banned prescribing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills by telemedicine and imposed other restrictions, while groups that support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have filed lawsuits arguing that federal law pre-empts those regulations.\par \par \uc2 The new ruling changes the game, however, because a national suspension of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -pill sales could dramatically tighten access even in states such as New York, California and Colorado where the procedure has remained widely available since the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overruled Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  last June.\par \par \uc2 "It's emblematic of the fight to come, which will focus on medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Rachel Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9, the dean of Temple University School of Law who studies \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  law. "We are at the center of what will define the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate in the years to come."\par \par \uc2 Judge Kacsmaryk's decision won't be the last word in the case. Additional orders from higher courts are likely in the coming days and weeks. The Justice Department and the drug's manufacturer, Danco Laboratories LLC, moved to appeal within hours of the ruling.\par \par \uc2 The case now heads to the New Orleans-based Fifth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals, one of the most conservative appellate courts in the country. A quick trip to the Supreme Court also could be on the horizon.\par \par \uc2 Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , whose emphasis on judicial nominations helped push the federal courts in a more conservative direction, made a particular mark on the Fifth Circuit, where he appointed a half-dozen new judges. Twelve of the court's 16 active judges were nominated by Republican presidents.\par \par \uc2 Court watchers said it is difficult to predict how the Fifth Circuit will handle a case that many lawyers regard as legally weak but that has become highly politicized.\par \par \uc2 Even before Roe was overruled, the Fifth Circuit had been more willing to allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions than some other courts, including in 2021 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-restrictions-can-continue-during-litigation-appeals-court-rules-11634261230?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when it left in place }}}\uc2 a novel Texas law that allowed private litigants to sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and others for damages.\par \par \uc2 "We're talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and all bets are off," said Areta Kupchyk, a former \uc2 FDA\uc2  associate chief counsel now at \uc2 Foley Hoag LLP\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Complicating the legal landscape, a different federal judge, based in Washington state, issued a contrary decision on Friday that could prevent the \uc2 FDA\uc2  from limiting the pill in the 17 states and District of Columbia that had sued the agency to preserve robust access.\par \par \uc2 The Texas and Washington cases didn't involve an identical set of legal issues, but the decisions did appear directly at odds with one another, raising questions about whether or how the \uc2 FDA\uc2  could comply with both.\par \par \uc2 Nancy Northup\uc2 , president and chief executive of the Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which represents a number of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, said attorneys there have been speaking to clinics about how to reconcile the two decisions but that they will continue providing the pill at least until the Texas decision goes into effect.\par \par \uc2 "We're really in uncharted waters with their apparently conflicting decisions," Ms. Northup said.\par \par \uc2 The potential conflict could hasten the need for the Supreme Court to intervene in a matter of weeks or even days, putting the justices back in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  spotlight for the first time since their June ruling in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization eliminated the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Democrats were quick to condemn the ruling. "Let's be clear, this is about the Republicans' goal of a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban," Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (D., N.Y.) said on Saturday.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-ruling-draws-muted-response-from-gop-71bbdda9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Many Republicans were more muted }}}\uc2  in their comments. GOP leaders have sought to avoid a national political fight on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the issue has presented challenges for the party in the months since the Dobbs ruling. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-supporters-prevail-in-midterm-ballot-measures-11667986139"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 It hurt them }}}\uc2  in some key races during the midterm elections, while voters in some states explicitly rejected measures to further restrict the procedure.\par \par \uc2 One exception was former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , a likely presidential candidate, who said on Friday, "When it approved chemical abortions on demand, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  acted carelessly and with blatant disregard for human life and the wellbeing of American women, and today's ruling fixed a 20 year wrong."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved mifepristone in 2000. It is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/little-known-abortion-pill-maker-faces-scrutiny-11656939602?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 known by the brand name Mifeprex }}}\uc2  and sold by Danco. The agency said studies had found its use safe and effective. A generic version is made by GenBioPro Inc.\par \par \uc2 The drug blocks a hormone necessary to sustain pregnancy. More than half of abortions in the U.S. now use it.\par \par \uc2 A group of antiabortion medical groups and individual physicians sued the \uc2 FDA\uc2  in November, arguing the agency overlooked the drug's risks, didn't assess its safety in girls and inappropriately approved the drug using a procedure meant only for dire conditions.\par \par \uc2 The judge said in his ruling Friday that the antiabortion challengers were likely to succeed on those arguments.\par \par \uc2 A day or two after taking mifepristone, women usually take one or two doses of another drug called misoprostol, which causes uterine contractions.\par \par \uc2 Judge Kacsmaryk's ruling doesn't affect misoprostol. Public-health experts and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups say women seeking a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  may now take misoprostol alone. Researchers have reported that taking misoprostol by itself can end a pregnancy, but not as reliably as combined with mifepristone, and with heavier side effects.\par \par \uc2 Liz Essley Whyte contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230409ej49000b9\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
