\par\par \uc2 Review & Outlook (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Democrats for Defying Court Orders; \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2  and \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  endorse law-breaking over an  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  drug.\b0\par\par\uc2 By The Editorial Board \par \uc2 514 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2023\par 20:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 One depressing sign of the political times is that partisans on the left and right are willing to trash political norms and institutions to get their way. The latest example comes from Democrats urging the Biden Administration to ignore last week's federal court order concerning the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 In an editorial nearby, we explain our doubts about Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk's ruling. His national injunction is also excessive before the merits are even considered. But the judge delayed the enforcement of his order for a week to give the Biden Administration time to appeal. The Fifth Circuit Court of Appeals will weigh in on the national injunction and the legal merits of the case.\par \par \uc2 But this regular legal process isn't enough for many Democrats, who are demanding that a federal agency ignore a legal court order they don't like.\par \par \uc2 "I believe the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  has the authority to ignore this ruling, which is why I'm again calling on President Biden and the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to do just that," said Oregon Sen. \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2  on Friday. "The \uc2 FDA\uc2 , doctors, and pharmacies can and must go about their jobs like nothing has changed and keep mifepristone accessible to women across America. If they don't, the consequences of banning the most common method of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in every single state will be devastating."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Wyden has moved ever leftward in recent years, but as Chairman of the Senate Finance Committee he has real power. New York Rep. \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  also said the \uc2 FDA\uc2  should ignore the court.\par \par \uc2 This is dangerous for the rule of law, and Democrats shouldn't think they'll be the only politicians who pick up the Wyden Nullification Doctrine. Southern Democrats called for "massive resistance" to legal orders in the 1950s after the Supreme Court's school desegregation ruling in Brown v. Board of Education. Is that now the Wyden-AOC model?\par \par \uc2 Even if Judge Kacsmaryk's ruling is upheld on appeal, that won't be the end of the matter. His ruling is procedural, and the \uc2 FDA\uc2  can re-approve the drug by closely adhering to the Administrative Procedure Act.\par \par \uc2 The other proper response is political. Mr. Wyden is one of many Democrats who predicted the end of legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Supreme Court's Dobbs decision last year. But Dobbs has proven to be an election windfall for Democrats, as they campaign against a ban while Republicans are divided and unsure how to respond. Judge Kacsmaryk's ruling is a political gift to the left that could end up aiding a more liberal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime in many states if not nationwide.\par \par \uc2 We warned about this Wyden Nullification Doctrine before, and it's encouraging that the Biden Administration is resisting so far. But there's a risk the Administration will cave under progressive pressure if the legal rulings don't go its way. If it does, the U.S. will take another giant step toward lawless politics.\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230409ej49002ut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
