\par \par \uc2 The combination of mifepristone tablets and misoprostol make up the pills prescribed in a medical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . PHOTO: Natalie Behring for the Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 A federal judge on Friday suspended approval of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, in a preliminary ruling against the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  that could limit women's access to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-an-abortion-pill-leaked-supreme-court-decision-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the most common method for ending a pregnancy  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 U.S. District Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk of Amarillo, Texas, said in a 67-page ruling that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  made a series of legal errors in approving the pill for sale in the U.S. The judge suspended approval of the drug, known as mifepristone, but delayed the impact of his decision for a week while the Biden administration appeals and seeks an emergency stay.\par \par \uc2 The judge said antiabortion challengers who sued the \uc2 FDA\uc2  were likely to succeed on arguments that the agency followed an unlawful approach when it allowed the pill on to the market using a pathway intended for drugs to treat serious illnesses. He also said the agency failed to appropriately assess the drug's safety.\par \par \uc2 "The Court does not second-guess \uc2 FDA\uc2  's decision-making lightly. But here, \uc2 FDA\uc2  acquiesced on its legitimate safety concerns\u8212\'20\'14in violation of its statutory duty\u8212\'20\'14based on plainly unsound reasoning and studies that did not support its conclusions," said Judge Kacsmaryk, a Trump appointee.\par \par \uc2 The judge's decision is the first step in what could be a series of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-approval-suspended-by-u-s-judge-3c5c88cf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fast-moving legal proceedings  }}}\uc2 . The Justice Department and the drug's manufacturer, Danco Laboratories LLC, moved to appeal within hours of the ruling. If the decision isn't put on hold by a higher court, it could stop sales of the drug even in the states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has remained legal since the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade last June.\par \par \uc2 Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  said the Justice Department strongly disagreed with the ruling. "Today's decision overturns the \uc2 FDA\uc2  's expert judgment, rendered over two decades ago, that mifepristone is safe and effective," Mr. Garland said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  , a conservative legal group that represented the plaintiffs, hailed the decision. "This is a significant victory for the doctors and medical associations we represent and more importantly, the health and safety of women and girls," it said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Complicating the legal landscape, a different federal judge, based in Washington state, issued a contrary decision on Friday that could prevent the \uc2 FDA\uc2  from limiting the pill in the 17 states and District of Columbia that had sued the agency to preserve robust access.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What impact do you think the judge's ruling will have on the access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 The litigation has been one of the most closely watched battles since the Supreme Court eliminated constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gave states wide latitude  }}}\uc2  to restrict or preserve \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they see fit.\par \par \uc2 As clinics have stopped offering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in roughly one-third of the states, access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/story/states-are-next-battlegrounds-for-abortion-pill-access-8abde763"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crucial battleground  }}}\uc2 . Some states have banned prescribing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills by telemedicine and imposed other restrictions, while groups that support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have filed lawsuits arguing that federal law pre-empts those regulations.\par \par \uc2 In 2000, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved mifepristone, which is also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/little-known-abortion-pill-maker-faces-scrutiny-11656939602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 known by the brand name Mifeprex  }}}\uc2  and sold by Danco. The agency said studies had found its use safe and effective. A generic version is made by GenBioPro Inc.\par \par \uc2 "Today's decision is wrong on the medicine and science, wrong as a matter of public health policy, wrong as a matter of \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  and wrong as a matter of law," said Danco spokeswoman Abby Long.\par \par \uc2 The drug blocks a hormone necessary to sustain pregnancy. More than half of abortions in the U.S. now use it.\par \par \uc2 Last November, a group of antiabortion medical groups and individual physicians brought the lawsuit. They argued that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  overlooked the drug's risks, didn't assess its safety in girls and inappropriately approved the drug using a procedure meant only for dire conditions.\par \par \uc2 "Today's ruling places women's welfare back at the forefront of the conversation on this issue," one of the plaintiffs, the American Association of Pro-Life Obstetricians & Gynecologists, said in a statement. "Our patients deserve excellent healthcare and fully informed consent; this decision helps ensure they receive that."\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for the federal government have said the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved the drug because it is safe and effective and that halting its distribution would upend the status quo and cause harm to patients.\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said the decision "threatens the rights of women nationwide to make decisions about their health care and the ability to access medication prescribed to them by their doctors."\par \par \uc2 A day or two after taking mifepristone, women usually take one or two doses of another drug called misoprostol, which causes uterine contractions.\par \par \uc2 Judge Kacsmaryk's ruling doesn't affect misoprostol. Public-health experts and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups say women seeking a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  may now take misoprostol alone. Researchers have reported that taking misoprostol by itself can end a pregnancy, but not as reliably as combined with mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 "This will not stop medication abortions from occurring in the U.S. It will simply force healthcare providers to rely on the misoprostol-only regimen, which, while still very safe, is somewhat less effective and causes more uncomfortable side effects," said Suzanne Bell, a professor at the \uc2 Johns Hopkins Bloomberg School of Public Health\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 It is rare for a judge to intervene in the \uc2 FDA\uc2  's decision making, particularly regarding a drug that has been on the market for many years. Plaintiffs' attorneys acknowledged at a Texas hearing in March that they couldn't point to examples where a court has intervened in a longstanding drug approval, although they did point to cases involving drugs that were newer to the market.\par \par \uc2 Judge Kacsmaryk said the \uc2 FDA\uc2  was responsible for delaying the plaintiffs' day in court until the drug had already been on the market for many years. "Had \uc2 FDA\uc2  responded to Plaintiffs' petitions within the 360 total days allotted, this case would have been in federal court decades earlier. Instead, \uc2 FDA\uc2  postponed and procrastinated for nearly 6,000 days," he wrote.\par \par \uc2 The judge previously worked at a conservative legal organization focused on religious issues before being appointed to the federal bench in 2019. In another high-profile ruling last year, he found that a federal program to provide birth control violated parents' rights because it allowed minors access to contraception without parental consent. The case is on appeal.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -pill case now heads to the New Orleans-based Fifth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals, one of the most conservative appellate courts in the country. Once that court acts on the Biden administration's stay request, the litigation could land at the Supreme Court on an emergency basis shortly thereafter.\par \par \uc2 In Washington state, U.S. District Judge Thomas Rice, an Obama appointee, sided with a group of Democratic state attorneys general who sued the \uc2 FDA\uc2  in a bid to make the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill easier to obtain.\par \par \uc2 The judge for now stopped the agency from enforcing some recent regulations on mifepristone and ordered the \uc2 FDA\uc2  not to put any further restrictions on the pill in the plaintiff states, setting up a potential conflict with the Texas ruling.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Liz Essley Whyte at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:liz.whyte@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 liz.whyte@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Liz Essley Whyte at \par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230407ej47006el\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
