\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, called mifepristone, more than two decades ago. PHOTO: Eric Lee for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-approval-suspended-by-u-s-judge-3c5c88cf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal judge's ruling  }}}\uc2  against the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  's approval of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-access-case-texas-judge-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill  }}}\uc2  could weaken the agency, opening its science-based decisions to court reviews, said lawyers specializing in the matters.\par \par \uc2 The decision, if it is appealed to the Supreme Court, could also give conservative justices an opportunity to trim the power of federal agencies generally, lawyers said.\par \par \uc2 "If the court does not defer to \uc2 FDA\uc2  , it would undermine \uc2 FDA\uc2  's authority and set a precedent for second-guessing by judges wholly unqualified to evaluate scientific data," said Areta Kupchyk, a former \uc2 FDA\uc2  associate chief counsel now at \uc2 Foley Hoag LLP\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  , which is spearheading the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lawsuit-filed-to-reverse-approval-access-to-abortion-pill-11668796816"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -pill lawsuit  }}}\uc2 , and some other conservative lawyers have argued that the case would have little impact on other drug approvals because it concerns unusually flawed decision making.\par \par \uc2 Yet the litigation could provide a springboard for tougher court scrutiny of regulatory overreach broadly, said Marc Wheat, an attorney for Advancing American Freedom, former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  's policy and advocacy nonprofit.\par \par \uc2 "This is the perfect issue of everything that has gone wrong with a federal agency and how dangerous they are when they do not adhere closely to the rule of law," he said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  declined to comment about the legal implications of the case, but it said Friday evening that the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill's "approval was based on the best available science and done in accordance with the laws that govern our work."\par \par \uc2 U.S. District Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk in Amarillo, Texas, on Friday ordered pulling the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill from the market as a preliminary measure while a lawsuit challenging the drug's approval proceeds. The order is set to go in effect after seven days.\par \par \uc2 "The Court does not second-guess \uc2 FDA\uc2  's decision-making lightly. But here, \uc2 FDA\uc2  acquiesced on its legitimate safety concerns\u8212\'20\'14in violation of its statutory duty\u8212\'20\'14based on plainly unsound reasoning and studies that did not support its conclusions," said Judge Kacsmaryk, a Trump appointee.\par \par \uc2 Just hours later, the Biden administration filed a notice of appeal. Also on Friday, a federal judge in Washington ordered the \uc2 FDA\uc2  not to place further restrictions on the drug in certain states\u8212\'20\'14setting up a legal showdown that could end at the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-an-abortion-pill-leaked-supreme-court-decision-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill, called mifepristone, in 2000  }}}\uc2 , more than four years after the application was filed. The agency said it based its approval on three studies testing the drug in nearly 2,500 women in total.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved the drug through its accelerated program to impose certain restrictions on access, such as requiring patients to have a follow-up visit before they could fill a prescription.\par \par \uc2 It is now used in more than half of all abortions in the U.S., but has emerged as one of the battlegrounds in fights over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2  last year.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups and doctors who challenged mifepristone's approval before Judge Kacsmaryk alleged the \uc2 FDA\uc2  was politically motivated, didn't follow proper procedures and ignored problems with the scientific studies supporting the action.\par \par \uc2 The federal government countered that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  based its decision on scientific evidence, followed the proper procedures and found the pill safe and effective.\par \par \uc2 Under federal law, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approves drugs that scientific studies find work safely. Typically, it requires companies to test prospective medicines in people, then reviews the data collected in the trials while deciding whether to approve and what instructions a drug's label should give.\par \par \uc2 For decades, courts have deferred to the \uc2 FDA\uc2  's scientific decision-making. Lawyers couldn't recall a case in which a court has revoked an approval for a brand-name drug so long on the market. During a recent hearing on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -pill lawsuit, lawyers for both sides acknowledged how unusual a reversal would be.\par \par \uc2 A court decision undoing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill's approval has "the potential to be game changing if the judge sort of accepts that world," said Eva Temkin, a former \uc2 FDA\uc2  associate chief counsel now at \uc2 King & Spalding LLP\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What does the decision by the Texas court mean for \uc2 FDA\uc2  drug approvals? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Temkin, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-restrictions-in-two-states-challenged-in-lawsuits-11674656653"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is representing a doctor in a lawsuit  }}}\uc2  filed in a federal court in North Carolina that seeks to roll back the state's restrictions on mifepristone access, said courts' intrusion could inject fresh uncertainty into a yearslong process, deterring drug development and financing.\par \par \uc2 ADF\uc2  lawyer Erik Baptist said the group's mifepristone lawsuit wasn't seeking a rethinking of court deference to the \uc2 FDA\uc2  , but rather overturning a particular agency decision that, he said, "egregious and flagrantly" violated the law.\par \par \uc2 "What we're asking the court to do is to hold the \uc2 FDA\uc2  accountable to follow the law. We're not asking the court to step in \uc2 FDA\uc2  's shoes and play scientific expert," he said.\par \par \uc2 If an appeal makes it to the Supreme Court, it could provide the conservative majority led by Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  a chance to dial back the authority of federal agencies, a popular goal among conservatives in recent years, lawyers on both sides said.\par \par \uc2 "I can see the path in that direction," said David Cohen, a professor at \uc2 Drexel University\uc2  's law school who studies constitutional law and gender issues. "That's been one of sort of the core missions of the Roberts court\u8212\'20\'14to push back on agency power." Mr. Cohen serves on the board of a group promoting access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last year, the Supreme Court ruled 6-3 that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-limits-environmental-protection-agencys-authority-11656598034"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency had overstepped  }}}\uc2 when it devised climate-change rules under President Obama without Congress's specific authorization.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court may use an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -pill appeal as "an opportunity to clip \uc2 FDA\uc2  's wings and say, 'You can only go so far,'" Ms. Kupchyk said. "This could be the ideal case for them to kill two birds with one stone."\par \par \uc2 Write to Liz Essley Whyte at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:liz.whyte@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 liz.whyte@wsj.com  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230408ej48001up\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
