\par\par \uc2 Election 2024\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  Prepares to Hit the Road for Biden Despite Cracks in Her Support; Vice president will seek to persuade Black voters, young people to re-elect the president\b0\par\par\uc2 By Tarini Parti \par \uc2 1,440 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 March 2023\par 12:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is preparing to campaign extensively when President Biden launches his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-appears-set-to-run-in-2024-but-many-democratic-voters-have-doubts-b71a48ad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 much-anticipated re-election bid }}}\uc2 , despite concerns in the Democratic Party that her performance in office, criticized by some as uneven, has made her a liability.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Harris plans to visit urban centers of swing states to persuade Black voters, young people and other liberal constituencies to re-elect Mr. Biden, according to people familiar with discussions about her campaign efforts. She will lead {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/bidens-budget-plan-offers-blueprint-for-2024-campaign-fights-with-gop-527c4ddb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the administration's advocacy }}}\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, tout the administration's climate investments and echo Mr. Biden's pledge to protect Medicare and Social Security.\par \par \uc2 Some top Democratic lawmakers and donors have been questioning Ms. Harris's future behind closed doors for months, saying they don't think the vice president has used her platform effectively, according to attendees at these events.\par \par \uc2 At one recent Zoom event organized by a former speechwriter for Mr. Biden, one of the Democrats aired frustrations with Ms. Harris, questioning whether she would be a liability to the 2024 ticket, according to people familiar with the call. Former California Sen. Barbara Boxer responded saying they could share concerns with Mr. Biden if they wanted. CNN earlier reported the event. The exchange during the call spurred further private discussion on the topic among some who had attended, those people said.\par \par \uc2 Missteps in high-profile interviews have also raised concerns that she doesn't perform consistently when speaking in public. Her backers said Ms. Harris, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kamala-harris-to-make-history-as-first-female-u-s-vice-president-11604769441"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the first woman }}}\uc2  to hold her position and the daughter of Indian and Jamaican immigrants, is being held to a different standard from past vice presidents, including Mr. Biden.\par \par \uc2 Jamal Simmons, a former communications director for Ms. Harris, said political rivals were criticizing the vice president to diminish her standing should she run for president years from now. "This is a conversation about 2028 dressed up as a conversation about 2024," he said.\par \par \uc2 Kirsten Allen, a spokeswoman for Ms. Harris, said the vice president "remains laser focused on delivering for the American people and ensuring they see the impacts of the Biden-Harris administration's work to lower costs, defend access to lifesaving care from extremists, and restore our reputation on the international stage."\par \par \uc2 Some of the skepticism spilled into public view when Massachusetts Democratic Sen. Elizabeth Warren was asked in a January radio interview if Ms. Harris should be on Mr. Biden's 2024 ticket. "I really want to defer to what makes Biden comfortable on his team," she said. Ms. Warren later issued a statement saying she supported the ticket and "never intended to imply otherwise."\par \par \uc2 Several Democrats said they are looking forward to when Ms. Harris hits the campaign trail to show she can effectively bring together a diverse group of voters behind Mr. Biden, 80 years old, and help persuade important constituencies to vote.\par \par \uc2 "I'm optimistic, despite what I see is the subtle voices that are out there, you know, trying to undermine her ability," said Rep. \uc2 Maxine Waters\uc2  (D., Calif.).\par \par \uc2 The vice president has hosted events at historically Black colleges and universities to energize young voters in key states in recent months. Her role in the midterms, in rallying voters around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and being one of the top fundraisers for the party, will be used as a model for the campaign to build on.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Harris's poll ratings are similar to Mr. Biden's, and her average approval rating is roughly 42%, according to FiveThirtyEight. She continues to lead polls of a hypothetical Democratic primary where Mr. Biden doesn't run with significant margins\u8212\'20\'14in large part because of her support from Black voters.\par \par \uc2 "Her position is historic, but I don't think I can definitively say that in the past two years now that she's been vice president that like, people are still excited about the fact that she holds this historic position," Shruthi Mohana Sundaram, a junior and president of College Democrats at \uc2 Georgia Institute of Technology\uc2 , where she recently attended a climate-related event held by Ms. Harris.\par \par \uc2 Cynthia Johnson, 67, a retired teacher from Laurinburg, N.C., who pointed out she attended an HBCU, like Ms. Harris, said she had been hoping for the vice president to play a bigger role in the administration. "At this point, she is kind of sidelined," Ms. Johnson said. "And I don't get it."\par \par \uc2 In her two years as vice president, Ms. Harris has made 129 domestic trips to 34 states, cast 29 tiebreaking votes in the Senate, spoken to more than 100 foreign leaders and traveled to 14 countries on 10 foreign trips, according to a White House official. Ms. Harris visited Iowa on Thursday to talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, following stops from GOP presidential contenders to the state, and is scheduled to travel to Africa at the end of the month.\par \par \uc2 Those close to the vice president frequently cite Ms. Harris herself as the biggest impediment to her political future. The former attorney general cross examines and second guesses her and her staff's smallest of decisions\u8212\'20\'14a habit those who have worked with her say she has struggled to overcome.\par \par \uc2 Some Democratic county chairs in swing states said their concern was that Ms. Harris had so far been unable to instill confidence in her political abilities as Mr. Biden faces re-election. They also said segments of Democratic voters in their area, including centrist and independent voters, seemed apathetic toward her.\par \par \uc2 Her backers are growing frustrated by the skepticism from their own party. Democrats, they say, have had expectations for her that are unreasonable for any vice president, especially one who ended her political operation, including terminating her political-action committees, as a condition for joining Mr. Biden's ticket in 2020, according to people familiar with her decisions. Like most vice presidents, she has little agency in setting the White House agenda and cannot publicly get in front of Mr. Biden on policy or be seen as outshining him, Ms. Harris's allies say.\par \par \uc2 "You don't expect the vice president to be out there tooting her horn," said former Rep. Bob Brady, chairman of the Philadelphia Democratic Party. "The president is the boss, and she complements him perfectly."\par \par \uc2 Jazheri Moore, 30, a Democrat and fashion stylist from Atlanta, Ga., who voted for the Biden-Harris ticket, said Ms. Harris's critics continue to underestimate her appeal to Black and young voters. "What more can she do? She's keeping up with appearances\u8212\'20\'14that's what vice presidents do."\par \par \uc2 Robert Dempster, chairman of Miami-Dade Democratic Party, said he sees a disconnect between the national discourse around Ms. Harris and what he sees on the ground. "Every time she comes down here, people go crazy," he said.\par \par \uc2 Allies say Ms. Harris can't publicize a big part of her job: advising Mr. Biden. She guided him on last year's Supreme Court nominee selection, advocated for a filibuster carve-out for voting rights and codifying Roe v. Wade and backed student loan forgiveness, according to people familiar with those discussions.\par \par \uc2 She has pushed for changes\u8212\'20\'14big and small\u8212\'20\'14at the White House that have rankled administration officials. Ms. Harris lobbied national security officials to change the way they described female foreign leaders in their briefings to avoid sexist language, such as "prickly," according to those people.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Where do you think Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  can make inroads with voters during the 2024 campaign? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Some close to her also acknowledge that the perception of her not doing enough or being an inconsistent politician is because she's been responsible for a hodgepodge of issues.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Harris's responsibilities include chairing a labor task force and the National Space Council; leading the White House's efforts to address migration from Central America; touting broadband-related investments; promoting the administration's efforts to preserve \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and Black maternal health; improving funding for minority-owned businesses; and preserving voting rights.\par \par \uc2 Laura Rodriguez, 58, a Miami resident who attended her \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights speech in Tallahassee earlier this year, said she would like to see Ms. Harris and other administration officials do more on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but she understands the limitations.\par \par \uc2 "You can only do so much," she said. "I think people need to sort of manage those expectations."\par \par \uc2 Natalie Andrews and Ken Thomas contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Tarini Parti at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:tarini.parti@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tarini.parti@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230320ej3k00107\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
