\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Judge Weighs Challenge to  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Pill Sales; Four-hour court argument explores antiabortion groups' challenge to \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of mifepristone\b0\par\par\uc2 By Adolfo Flores, Laura Kusisto, and Liz Essley Whyte \par \uc2 658 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 March 2023\par 21:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 AMARILLO, Texas\u8212\'20\'14A federal judge on Wednesday questioned the government about its approval of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-an-abortion-pill-leaked-supreme-court-decision-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 medication used in more than half of the abortions in the U.S }}}\uc2 , but also asked whether there was any precedent for a court blocking sales of a drug long after it had been allowed on the market.\par \par \uc2 U.S. District Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk, in the first public hearing in a case that has drawn national attention, spent four hours considering claims by antiabortion medical groups and individual physicians that the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  exceeded its authority when it approved the sale of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inducing pill known as mifepristone under a process meant for treatments of serious or life-threatening illnesses.\par \par \uc2 Judge Kacsmaryk, addressing lawyers from the Justice Department who are defending the \uc2 FDA\uc2 , said that a majority of the drugs that went through that process appeared to be for the treatment of HIV and cancer.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department said that pregnancy can be a serious or life-threatening condition for some women. Department lawyer Julie Straus Harris said mifepristone has been found to be safe and effective in various studies. An unfavorable ruling for the government, she said, would upend the use and availability of a drug that people across the U.S. have been accessing for decades.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , representing the challengers, are seeking a preliminary injunction blocking sales of the pill while litigation continues. They {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lawsuit-filed-to-reverse-approval-access-to-abortion-pill-11668796816"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed the lawsuit }}}\uc2  in November, and on Wednesday argued the medication was unsafe and posed a danger to women nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Judge Kacsmaryk, a Trump appointee, asked if they could point to an example where a court intervened after a drug had been approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  after more than two decades on the market. Lawyer Erik Baptist said he couldn't, but blamed the time lag on the agency's delay in addressing the group's previous attempts to stop the sale of mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 The judge didn't offer a timeframe for his ruling, saying he would issue a written order and opinion as soon as possible.\par \par \uc2 The case has become a critical battleground regarding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the future of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access }}}\uc2  around the country. The court allowed entry to only a limited number of members of the public and press, and some who lined up hours before the hearing were unable to get in.\par \par \uc2 Judge Kacsmaryk conferred with parties privately on Friday to make plans for the hearing, but didn't announce the proceedings right away, to minimize what he said could be disruptions and potential security issues. He said the court had already faced death threats and harassment, according to a transcript of the call. "I think less advertisement of this hearing is better," the judge said during the conference call.\par \par \uc2 There were no disruptions during Wednesday's court session.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Should a federal judge block the sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills around the country? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  first approved mifepristone for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  more than two decades ago. The drug blocks a hormone needed for childbearing and is part of a two-step regimen for ending a pregnancy, along with the drug misoprostol. Patients can take misoprostol alone, but doing so isn't as reliable.\par \par \uc2 Since the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade last summer, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become largely inaccessible in roughly one-third of the states, either because a ban is in place or because clinics have stopped offering the procedure owing to legal uncertainty. A ruling in this case has the potential to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/walgreens-abortion-pill-furor-highlights-complexity-of-access-in-post-roe-world-6ed0086c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 affect access to medication \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  even in states where the procedure is otherwise legal.\par \par \uc2 Write to Adolfo Flores at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:adolfo.flores@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 adolfo.flores@wsj.com }}}\uc2 , Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Liz Essley Whyte at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:liz.whyte@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 liz.whyte@wsj.com }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230315ej3f001gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
