\par\par \uc2 Business\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Walgreens \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Pill Furor Highlights Complexity of Access in Post-Roe World; Pharmacy chain has found itself at center of political battle over access to medication abortions\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 1,277 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 March 2023\par 02:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Pharmacies and medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are emerging as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/story/states-are-next-battlegrounds-for-abortion-pill-access-8abde763"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contentious political battlegrounds }}}\uc2  in the increasingly complex issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Walgreens Boots Alliance Inc. has found itself at the center of the fray after the pharmacy chain said it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/walgreens-wont-sell-abortion-pill-in-some-states-9d9e2131"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wouldn't dispense the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill }}}\uc2  in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is illegal and in several states where it is currently legal, including Alaska, Iowa, Kansas and Montana, given the "complexity and flux" of the laws in those places related to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as legal battles over access continue.\par \par \uc2 The move won praise from some Republican politicians but sparked backlash from several Democratic leaders. California said Wednesday it was dropping a multimillion-dollar contract with the company.\par \par \uc2 Republican state attorneys general last month sent \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  letters outlining their legal arguments against the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 's move to loosen restrictions on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill. \uc2 CVS Health Corp\uc2 . received similar letters.\par \par \uc2 California Gov. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  said Monday the state wouldn't do business with \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  "or any company that cowers to the extremists and puts women's lives at risk." He called for a review of the state's relationship with the nation's second-largest drugstore chain.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, his office said the \uc2 California Department of General Services\uc2  was withdrawing the planned renewal of its contract with \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  to provide specialty prescription drugs, mainly for the state's department of corrections. The state has paid about $54 million to \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  under the contract, Mr. Newsom's office said.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  spokesman reiterated the company's plans to dispense medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  where it is legally allowed\u8212\'20\'14including in California. The company is still in the process of seeking certification to dispense mifepristone, the drug that blocks a hormone needed to sustain pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 "We are deeply disappointed by the decision by the state of California not to renew our longstanding contract due to false and misleading information," the spokesman said in a statement Wednesday evening. "\uc2 Walgreens\uc2  is facing the same circumstances as all retail pharmacies, and no other retail pharmacies have said that they would approach this situation differently, so it's unclear where this contract would now be moved."\par \par \uc2 Illinois Gov. \uc2 J.B. Pritzker\uc2  met with leaders at the Illinois-based company and urged them to reconsider their decision. Six Democratic U.S. senators sent a letter to \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  Chief Executive \uc2 Rosalind Brewer\uc2  this week seeking to clarify the company's policies. The senators wrote that declining to dispense medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in states where it is legal "would be a betrayal of your customers."\par \par \uc2 Former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , meanwhile, praised the state attorneys general who sent the letters and \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  in a speech at a Students for Life of America gala over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 "Americans don't want their pharmacies to become \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  facilities," Mr. Pence said. "I commend \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  for yielding to the rule of law."\par \par \uc2 The political furor is the latest example of the quickly shifting landscape that has emerged since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade in June }}}\uc2 , returning the question of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 's legality to the states. In less than a year, new and newly enforced state laws have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 created a patchwork of access }}}\uc2 . About a dozen states have enacted near-total bans that restrict both surgical and medication abortions. Other states have added new protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and bolstered existing ones.\par \par \uc2 States have varying regulations on medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including some that require a person to take the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inducing medication while a physician is present, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a research group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks national and state statistics.\par \par \uc2 A lawsuit in Texas could upend nationwide access to mifepristone. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lawsuit-filed-to-reverse-approval-access-to-abortion-pill-11668796816"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  opponents sued the FDA }}}\uc2  and \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  in November in an attempt to undo the approval of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inducing pill. Two other lawsuits filed in January {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-restrictions-in-two-states-challenged-in-lawsuits-11674656653"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenge states that have restricted medication abortions }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "This is what we are in store for," said Rachel Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9, dean of \uc2 Temple University\uc2 's law school and an expert on \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-health\b0 \highlight\uc2  law. "The center of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate in this country will be over pills, in part because they are really hard to stop."\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-an-abortion-pill-leaked-supreme-court-decision-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Medication \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  made up more than half of all abortions in 2020, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  requires taking mifepristone and then misoprostol, which causes uterine contractions. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved the use of mifepristone in 2000 for up until seven weeks in pregnancy and later extended that to 10 weeks. The \uc2 FDA{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/fda-allows-women-to-get-abortion-pill-by-mail-11639698022?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 relaxed restrictions }}}\uc2  around the drug in 2021, allowing patients to get mifepristone without an in-person visit to a hospital or doctor.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  in January expanded access further, allowing bricks-and-mortar pharmacies like \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  to dispense the drug for the first time. \uc2 Walgreens\uc2 , followed by other major pharmaceutical chains like CVS, said shortly after that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/walgreens-will-sell-the-abortion-pill-pharmacy-says-11672870977"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they would seek certification to dispense mifepristone }}}\uc2  in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups and lawmakers are pushing back. Antiabortion activists have protested outside of pharmacies\u8212\'20\'14and some interrupted \uc2 Walgreens\uc2 ' annual shareholders meeting earlier this year. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
