\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  began allowing bricks-and-mortar pharmacies to dispense mifepristone in January. PHOTO: Eric Lee for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 "It's really going to be part of the standard protocol of community pro-life groups to have a regular presence outside of pharmacies as we get further and further into this," said Kristan Hawkins, president of Students for Life of America, which held protests at dozens of pharmacies over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 Kirsten Moore, director of the Expanding Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access Project, said she believes it will take time for pharmacies to get certified and for the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's new policy to sort out. Antiabortion lawmakers and groups, she said, are throwing everything at the wall to see what can slow or prevent pharmacies from dispensing medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We, as the advocates on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care side, just have to keep our heads down, don't freak out over everything and say this is the way of the future," Ms. Moore said.\par \par \uc2 The letters 20 state attorneys general sent to \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  and CVS in February {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-states-where-abortion-is-legal-some-cities-look-to-restrict-access-11671749172"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cite a 150-year-old federal law }}}\uc2  that they said prohibits the mailing of medication used to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The federal government in December said the Comstock Act doesn't prohibit the mailing of mifepristone or misoprostol, unless it's done with the intention to use it unlawfully. Nineteen of the state attorneys general sent similar letters to other pharmacy chains in late February. Kansas Attorney General Kris Kobach sent separate letters to \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  and CVS last month.\par \par \uc2 These different interpretations of the law reflect the common collision in debates over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , now with pharmaceutical companies like \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  getting caught in the middle, Dr. Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9 said. In this case, \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  is likely weighing concerns that state laws could change and erring on the side of caution, she said.\par \par \uc2 Sree Chaguturu, \uc2 CVS Health\uc2 's chief medical officer, said Monday the company will monitor the shifting legal landscape. "We're committed to providing \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved medications where legally permissible," he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/video/events/drugstores-of-the-future/17A40B96-174E-4E79-98AC-97335D626B78.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in an interview }}}\uc2  at The Wall Street Journal's Health Forum.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Rite Aid Corp\uc2 . spokeswoman said the company also was monitoring "the latest federal, state, legal and regulatory developments" related to dispensing mifepristone. "We will continue to evaluate the company's ability to dispense mifepristone in accordance with those developments," she said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230308ej38003ml\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
