\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Florida Republicans Propose  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban After Six Weeks of Pregnancy; Party leaders are building support for bill, which could further narrow  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  access in Southeast\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 635 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 March 2023\par 22:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Florida Republicans on Tuesday introduced a bill that seeks to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy, a measure that appears to have strong support from prominent state GOP leaders and would further reshape the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  landscape.\par \par \uc2 Since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 last June and cleared the way for states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Florida {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-pauses-on-more-abortion-restrictions-following-supreme-court-decision-11656591626"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been one of few outliers in the South }}}\uc2 , allowing the procedure up until 15 weeks of pregnancy. Since then, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has presented a tricky political balancing act for Republican Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , a likely presidential candidate, and Republican legislative leaders, who hold a supermajority in both chambers of the state legislature.\par \par \uc2 Florida GOP officials including Mr. DeSantis appear to be coalescing around the new bill, which is among the strictest gestational limits legislators could have proposed, short of banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  altogether. The legislation includes exceptions for rape and incest and if the mother's life or health is endangered.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, Mr. DeSantis suggested he would sign a so-called heartbeat bill if the legislature sent one to his desk. Such bills ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after embryonic cardiac activity is detectable, usually around six weeks of pregnancy. "We are for pro-life. I urge the legislature to work, produce good stuff. We will sign," he said last month. On Tuesday he said, "We welcome pro-life legislation."\par \par \uc2 Senate President Kathleen Passidomo previously said she supported a 12-week ban but also urged lawmakers to wait until the state Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-pauses-on-more-abortion-restrictions-following-supreme-court-decision-11656591626"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled on a legal challenge }}}\uc2  to the 15-week ban, a case that remains pending. On Tuesday she said she supports the six-week ban, which she said "builds on Florida's strong track record of protecting the most vulnerable, especially the unborn."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates say that if such a law passes it would leave women in the South having to travel long distances to clinics in locations such as North Carolina, which already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/women-encounter-abortion-delays-as-clinics-draw-patients-from-out-of-state-f40e318b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have been struggling }}}\uc2  with a huge increase in demand from out-of-state patients. "The impact is going to be devastating for not just Floridians but surrounding states," said Laura Goodhue, executive director of Florida Alliance of Planned Parenthood Affiliates.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Goodhue said advocates hope they can at least stall the legislation, even if they are unable to stop its passage.\par \par \uc2 Aubrey Jewett, a political-science professor at the \uc2 University of Central Florida\uc2 , said Republicans have wiggle room in the legislature to lose some moderate votes and still pass the bill. "You put that together and it suggests that there's a pretty high likelihood that Florida is going to pass a six-week ban," he said.\par \par \uc2 Medical providers in Florida performed the third-highest number of abortions in 2020 of any state, behind only Democratic-led New York and California, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a policy group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  statistics.\par \par \uc2 Florida saw an increase in abortions in the months following the Supreme Court decision, even as the number of abortions performed in most other Southern states dropped precipitously, according to WeCount, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -data project sponsored by the Society of Family Planning, which supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 In polling last year by \uc2 Florida Atlantic University\uc2 , roughly two-thirds of state respondents said they thought \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases. Antiabortion groups say they have their own polling data that indicates state residents support restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a heartbeat is detected, with exceptions for rape, incest and the life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 Arian Campo-Flores contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230307ej37005pl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
