\par \par \uc2 Medication abortions accounted for 54% of abortions in the U.S. in 2020, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 . PHOTO: Taylor Glascock for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Walgreens Boots Alliance Inc\uc2 . said it won't dispense the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill in several states, including four where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal, as the company navigates the complicated landscape created after the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The pharmacy chain said it intends to move forward with a federal certification process that will allow it to dispense mifepristone to customers from its bricks-and-mortar locations with a doctor's prescription.\par \par \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  said it won't dispense the pill in states that have banned the procedure. It is also opting against dispensing the pill in some states with legal or legislative challenges to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access\u8212\'20\'14such as Iowa, Kansas, Montana and Alaska\u8212\'20\'14given the "complexity and flux" of the laws, the company said.\par \par \uc2 "We intend to be a certified pharmacy and will distribute mifepristone only in those jurisdictions where it is legal and operationally feasible," a \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  spokesman said.\par \par \uc2 In February, around 20 Republican state attorneys general sent \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  a letter outlining their legal arguments against recent steps taken by the Biden administration to loosen restrictions on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill.\par \par \uc2 The Food and Drug Administration in early January changed its rules to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pills-to-be-available-more-widely-under-new-fda-rules-11672789765"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allow bricks-and-mortar pharmacies to carry }}}\uc2  mifepristone, a drug that blocks a hormone necessary to sustain pregnancy. Pharmacies must undergo a certification process to be part of the program.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court's ruling in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization returned the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-abortion-ruling-puts-states-in-spotlight-11656082938"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 question of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 's legality to states }}}\uc2 . About a dozen have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enacted near-total bans }}}\uc2  that restrict both procedural and medication abortions. More Republican-controlled state legislatures are expected to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/state-battles-on-abortion-access-are-ahead-in-the-new-year-11670444095"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 consider new \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  restrictions }}}\uc2  this year, even as efforts in some places have hit legal and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/state-abortion-bans-face-obstacles-as-republicans-clash-11660908536"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 political obstacles }}}\uc2 . Democrats in other states, meanwhile, are pushing to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/ohio-abortion-rights-coalition-begins-push-for-constitutional-amendment-9ab5d752"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enshrine \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights in law }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In January, as the U.S. marked the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-roe-v-wade-50th-anniversary-11674171133"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 50th anniversary of Roe }}}\uc2 , \u8203\'20\'0B\u8203\'20\'0BPresident Biden directed cabinet and administration members to identify barriers to accessing or providing medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and recommend solutions.\par \par \uc2 During the Covid-19 lockdown, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  loosened restrictions to allow patients to get the drug mifepristone without an in-person visit to a hospital or doctor. Certified online pharmacies were able to ship the pill, which the \uc2 FDA\uc2  has approved for use in the first 10 weeks of pregnancy, straight to the patient.\par \par \uc2 Some states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is restricted or illegal tried to ban the mailing of the pill, but the Justice Department has said the \uc2 U.S. Postal Service\uc2  can deliver to any state.\par \par \uc2 The Republican attorneys general who wrote to \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  challenged that assertion, alleging in their letter that federal law expressly prohibits using the mail to send or receive any drug that will "be used or applied for producing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Alaska Attorney General Treg Taylor said state law there requires licensed physicians to be the ones who perform abortions. That law was challenged by Planned Parenthood in 2019.\par \par \uc2 "While the statute is subject to a limited injunction allowing Advanced Practice Clinicians to perform medication abortions, it nevertheless operates to prohibit pharmacy sales of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs directly to patients," Mr. Taylor said.\par \par \uc2 The attorneys general's letter was sent to several other national pharmacy chains, including \uc2 CVS Health Corp\uc2 ., Mr. Taylor said.\par \par \uc2 CVS didn't respond to a request for comment Friday. The company has said it would sell mifepristone after reviewing the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's new rules. "We plan to seek certification to dispense mifepristone where legally permissible," a CVS spokeswoman said in January.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents last year sued the \uc2 FDA\uc2  and \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lawsuit-filed-to-reverse-approval-access-to-abortion-pill-11668796816"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seeking to undo }}}\uc2  federal approval of mifepristone. In January, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-restrictions-in-two-states-challenged-in-lawsuits-11674656653"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two other lawsuits }}}\uc2  challenged states that restricted medication abortions, arguing that states can't impose restrictions on the medication that are stricter than those of the federal government.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved mifepristone, in combination with misoprostol, for medication abortions in 2000. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-an-abortion-pill-leaked-supreme-court-decision-11651775689?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Medication abortions }}}\uc2  accounted for 54% of abortions in the U.S. in 2020, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a research group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks national and state statistics.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ginger Adams Otis at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Ginger.AdamsOtis@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ginger.AdamsOtis@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230303ej33007k9\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
