\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Ohio  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Rights Coalition Begins Push for Constitutional Amendment; Voters in several states approved similar constitutional protections last year\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 796 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 February 2023\par 23:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 An effort to place a constitutional amendment protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights on the ballot is brewing in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 Ohioans for Reproductive Freedom and Ohio Physicians for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  filed paperwork with the state's attorney general Tuesday in one of its first steps to try to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 The coalition aims to place the amendment on the November ballot, using a mechanism \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups have turned to after the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade last year and returned the question of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 's legality to states.\par \par \uc2 Leaders from the groups said the proposed amendment would create state-level protections for the procedure and prevent bans and narrower restrictions. The state's ban on nearly all abortions after six weeks of pregnancy is temporarily blocked in court.\par \par \uc2 "We simply cannot rely on our legislators or even ultimately on our courts to secure this freedom in the long run," said Jessie Hill, a leader with Ohioans for Reproductive Freedom and a professor at Case Western Reserve University's School of Law. "We have to do it for ourselves."\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 patchwork of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access }}}\uc2  has emerged across the U.S. following the Supreme Court's decision in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization. About a dozen states have enforced bans on nearly all abortions since June 2022, while others have moved to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access through state laws and executive orders.\par \par \uc2 Twenty Democratic governors said Tuesday they had formed a coalition focused on protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their states. "We are pledging to work together to strengthen \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  firewalls across America," the governors, representing states including California, Maine, Michigan, New Mexico, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Without federal constitutional protections, attention from groups on both sides of the issue has shifted to whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are protected {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lawsuits-to-test-whether-state-constitutions-protect-abortion-rights-11657375200"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 under state constitutions }}}\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups in Michigan found success with their citizen-led ballot initiative last year. Voters in the Midwestern state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-supporters-prevail-in-midterm-ballot-measures-11667986139"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed the referendum in November }}}\uc2 , which nullified a 1931 state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that sat largely dormant for the past 50 years. Voters in California and Vermont approved similar state constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , brought to the ballot by Democratic-led state legislatures.\par \par \uc2 Voters in Kansas and Kentucky, meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-abortion-vote-results-11659440554"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected proposed constitutional amendments }}}\uc2  last year said their state constitutions didn't include a right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ohio \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups are proposing a constitutional amendment that declares a person has the right "to make and carry out one's own reproductive decisions," including those related to contraception, fertility treatment and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The amendment would allow restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with some exceptions, after fetal viability, which is generally considered to be after around 22 to 24 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Ohioans can bring constitutional amendments to the ballot following a series of approvals and requirements. Supporters will also need to gather 413,488 signatures from at least 44 of the state's 88 counties by July 5.\par \par \uc2 Ohio Right to Life, an antiabortion group in the state, started planning its strategy to rally voters against a potential ballot initiative months ago, said Michael Gonidakis, president of the group. It kept an eye on how similar efforts played out in Michigan last year and plans to form a coalition to campaign against the initiative, tapping into faith-based communities in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 "We've known it was just a matter of time before this issue came to the battleground state of Ohio," Mr. Gonidakis said. "We're ready to go. We're ready to have this fight."\par \par \uc2 Ohio is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of several GOP-led states }}}\uc2  that had passed bans on nearly all abortions after six weeks of pregnancy before the Supreme Court's decision in June.\par \par \uc2 A county court granted a preliminary injunction blocking Ohio's six-week ban last year. In January, state Attorney General \uc2 Dave Yost\uc2  asked the Supreme Court of Ohio to take up the case after a state appeals court dismissed his appeal, citing jurisdictional issues. Mr. Yost, a Republican, said in court filings the state's constitution doesn't include the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Leaders with the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights coalition said they anticipate the constitutional amendment effort will be costly. Lauren Beene, executive director of Ohio Physicians for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said the signature collection process could cost between $2 million and $6 million, and subsequent voter-engagement campaign could cost between $20 million to $30 million.\par \par \uc2 "It's a significant amount of money," said Dr. Beene, adding the groups would likely raise funds through a combination of in-state and out-of-state donors.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230221ej2l004v1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
