\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Women Encounter  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Delays as Clinics Draw Patients From Out of State; Some providers in areas where  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  is legal report surging demand\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto | Photographs by Angela Owens /The Wall Street Journal \par \uc2 1,051 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 February 2023\par 10:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CHARLOTTE, N. C.\u8212\'20\'14Seven months after the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade, some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics say {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new state bans }}}\uc2  on the procedure are pushing abortions later into pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Since the high court's decision to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remove constitutional protections }}}\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the procedure has become largely inaccessible in nearly one-third of the states, either because a ban is in place or because clinics have shut down owing to legal uncertainty.\par \par \uc2 Clinics in states where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-states-where-abortion-is-legal-some-cities-look-to-restrict-access-11671749172"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  is still legal }}}\uc2  say they are facing strains, with a surge in demand leading to delays. While there isn't yet broad national data on post-Roe trends, a number of clinics say appointment-wait times have typically increased by weeks, for both in-state and out-of-state patients.\par \par \uc2 Chad Jackson, director of A Woman's Choice, a clinic in Charlotte, said that on average patients are arriving about two weeks later than they did before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe was overturned }}}\uc2 , primarily because of travel-related challenges. North Carolina has seen a surge in out-of-state patients because it is one of the few states in the Southeast where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still legal past the very early weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Polling shows that as a pregnancy progresses and the fetus develops, abortions are viewed by many Americans as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-americans-really-think-about-abortion-11601042639"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more ethically problematic }}}\uc2  than those that occur early on. They are also more complicated\u8212\'20\'14and expensive\u8212\'20\'14as women get further along in pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Patients can only be prescribed the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill up to about 10 weeks of pregnancy. Any time later than that typically involves a surgical procedure, which has longer wait times than pill-induced abortions at some clinics and usually requires that patients have someone to accompany them home because of sedation.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Jackson said women sometimes arrive hoping for a shorter or less invasive procedure, and when they learn they are too late, they have to return home because of employment or child-care responsibilities. "Every week just gets more stressful" for a patient, he said.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups say that the U.S. is still in the early days of the post-Roe era and that it is too soon to draw long-term conclusions. But they say anecdotal evidence shows that state bans are leading to more women carrying to term.\par \par \uc2 Pregnancy-help centers, which provide services to pregnant women and oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , are seeing an uptick in demand, suggesting that some women are choosing to continue their pregnancies because of these laws, said Jor-El Godsey, president of Heartbeat International, an association representing the centers.\par \par \uc2 Chuck Donovan\uc2 , president of the Charlotte Lozier Institute, a research group that opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said states can do more to provide support for women facing unexpected pregnancies, such as by passing laws that require fathers to provide financial support to pregnant mothers, giving tax credits to pregnant women and expanding midwifery care in places lacking healthcare.\par \par \uc2 For patients who have to travel for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it can take weeks to sort out finances, child care and time off from work. Some women are confused about the status of the law and are hesitant to seek care because of fear of potential prosecution, while others have traveled to a state with restrictions in place and are turned away, according to doctors and clinic directors.\par \par \uc2 One day in late January, Kaleatha Sykes sat in a semicircle with a handful of other women in a lavender room at A Woman's Choice, holding the pills prescribed to end her pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Sykes, a 36-year-old mother of two young boys, lives in Alabama, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now banned throughout pregnancy. She initially drove 3 1/2 hours to a clinic in Atlanta, where the staff told her she was ineligible for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Georgia under the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgia-six-week-abortion-ban-goes-into-effect-11658352186"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state's "heartbeat" law }}}\uc2 , which bars clinics from providing abortions if fetal cardiac activity is detected, usually around six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 After she drove back home in tears, her sister found the North Carolina clinic online. Ms. Sykes spent another week waiting for an appointment and coming up with money for the trip.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Sykes said the experience, her second \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was far different from her first, when there was legal access in Alabama and a clinic was 15 minutes away. "This is like I'm planning and waiting and waiting and spending money to get flights and stuff," she said. "It's overbearing."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Federation\uc2 , a membership association of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers that operates a national hotline, said on average they are seeing women from states with bans obtaining abortions one to two weeks later than they did a year ago. Researchers say it is too early for broad national data on the phenomenon, but earlier academic studies have found a correlation between legal restrictions that lead to clinic closures and significant increases in second-trimester abortions.\par \par \uc2 "The question isn't whether we're going to see delays in when people present for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," it is to what extent, said Katrina Kimport, a professor who studies \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the \uc2 University of California, San Francisco\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A Planned Parenthood clinic in southern Illinois, near the Missouri border, has seen second-trimester abortions double since the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/key-excerpts-from-supreme-courts-abortion-ruling-overturning-roe-v-wade-11656092052"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court decision }}}\uc2  in June, according to Colleen McNicholas, chief medical officer for Planned Parenthood of the St. Louis Region and Southwest Missouri. "Our volume of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  later in pregnancy has exploded," Dr. McNicholas said.\par \par \uc2 In College Park, Md., a new clinic called Partners in \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Care opened in the fall, offering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up until the 34th week of pregnancy if patients meet criteria under state law.\par \par \uc2 Diane Horvath, the clinic's co-founder and medical director, said she sometimes sees extreme examples of patients who take months to find an appointment. The clinic is scheduling patients two to three weeks out. Sometimes by the time a patient calls, the patient is approaching the legal limit in Maryland.\par \par \uc2 The clinic tries to fit in extra appointments, Dr. Horvath said, but "there are people we just have to turn away."\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230212ej2c00005\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
