\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Minnesota, With New Democratic Control, Enacts State  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights; State legislature was first to pass legislation establishing the right to an  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  since the Supreme Court overturned Roe\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 758 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 January 2023\par 21:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Minnesota Gov. \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  signed legislation enshrining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections under state law, making Minnesota the first state to enact new statutory rights following the Supreme Court's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision overturning Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Protect Reproductive Options Act declares that individuals have the right to make their own decisions about their \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including whether to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The legislation also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-states-where-abortion-is-legal-some-cities-look-to-restrict-access-11671749172"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocks local governments  }}}\uc2  from enacting narrower restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  than any established by the state.\par \par \uc2 "To Minnesotans, know that your access to \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  and your right to make your own healthcare decisions are preserved and protected," Mr. Walz, a Democrat, said before signing the bill Tuesday. "And because of this law, that won't change with the political winds or the make-up of the Supreme Court."\par \par \uc2 The Democratic-controlled state legislature is the first to pass legislation establishing the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the Supreme Court's Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization decision in June {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended federal constitutional protections  }}}\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota State Senate approved the legislation Saturday in a tight 34-33 vote along party lines. The chamber {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democrats-to-tackle-abortion-access-gun-laws-with-new-state-power-11669377187"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flipped for the state's Democratic-Farmer-Labor Party  }}}\uc2  in the 2022 midterm elections, creating a Democratic trifecta with the state House of Representatives and governor's office for the first time since the 2013-14 session.\par \par \uc2 The legislature's Reproductive Freedom Caucus called the bill "only a first step." In a 1995 decision, the Minnesota Supreme Court recognized the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under the state constitution. The new bill aimed to codify those protections in the event that a future state Supreme Court overturns the decision.\par \par \uc2 "What happened to Roe can happen to Minnesota, too," state Rep. Carlie Kotyza-Witthuhn, a Democrat who sponsored the bill, said earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 During hours of debate, Republicans in the statehouse called the bill extreme. They tried and failed to pass dozens of amendments related to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics' licensing, restrictions on abortions after a certain number of weeks of pregnancy and other regulations.\par \par \uc2 "We will become the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  magnet in the upper Midwest," state Sen. Steve Drazkowski, a Republican, said near the end of debate in the Senate. "That's the policy Minnesotans are going to get\u8212\'20\'14the most extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy our state has ever seen."\par \par \uc2 In a letter to the governor Monday, Republican legislative leaders urged Mr. Walz to veto the legislation.\par \par \uc2 Minnesota Citizens Concerned for Life, an antiabortion group, criticized the legislature's defeat of the proposed amendments.\par \par \uc2 "It is extreme, inhumane, and harmful to women and children who deserve so much better," Cathy Blaeser, co-executive director of Minnesota Citizens Concerned for Life, said in a statement Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 After the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  's decision in June, more than a dozen states enforced near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and other narrow restrictions, creating a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 patchwork of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access  }}}\uc2  across the country. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is currently unavailable in states surrounding Minnesota including North Dakota, South Dakota and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 Other states have moved to increase access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as many clinics see an uptick in patients traveling across state lines and regions. Minnesota joins more than a dozen other states and Washington, D.C., that have enacted legislation establishing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights under state law. Voters in Michigan, Vermont and California approved ballot measures that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-supporters-prevail-in-midterm-ballot-measures-11667986139"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enshrined \b  \highlight22reproductive rights\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  under their state constitutions in November 2022.\par \par \uc2 "State and local governments must continue to step up to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care for women everywhere," Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP/status/1620525329533079553"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a tweet  }}}\uc2  Tuesday after Mr. Walz signed the Minnesota law.\par \par \uc2 Minnesota \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics have seen an uptick in patients coming in from out of state, too. Planned Parenthood North Central States said it has seen a 13% increase in patients traveling from out of the region since the Dobbs decision in June, according to a spokeswoman for the group. There has also been a 40% jump in those patients seeking second-trimester abortions.\par \par \uc2 Red River Women's Clinic, once North Dakota's only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, moved across state lines to Moorehead, Minn., in August to continue its services.\par \par \uc2 "Today, for a moment, we can take a collective breath as Minnesota will be a north star for \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Ruth Richardson, president and chief executive of Planned Parenthood North Central States, said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230131ej1v0053d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
