\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade in June. PHOTO: Elizabeth Frantz for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 "The plaintiffs can make a strong argument," he said. "Basically the idea is if there's clear authority from Congress and the agency has made clear it's exercising that power, then states' law or regulations can be pre-empted by \uc2 FDA\uc2  ."\par \par \uc2 One line of defense for states, Mississippi Attorney General Lynn Fitch said, could be their powers to protect the health and safety of citizens. Ms. Fitch said courts traditionally recognize those powers as a fundamental component of state sovereignty.\par \par \uc2 Following the Supreme Court ruling last year, GenBioPro dropped a lawsuit in Mississippi arguing that the state couldn't add extra restrictions to how its drug is dispensed. The company said it was adjusting its strategy "due to the changed national landscape."\par \par \uc2 Eighteen states ban telehealth visits for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  , a nonprofit that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  statistics. A dozen states, including West Virginia, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban almost all abortions  }}}\uc2 . Most abortions in the U.S. are now performed using the pill, according to the institute.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How much oversight should states have over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs? Join the conversation below.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-orders-increase-even-in-restrictive-states-11658136602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Demand for the pills  }}}\uc2  has increased following the Supreme Court's decision, even in states that restrict access.\par \par \uc2 Activists supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights said they expect to see more lawsuits challenging state restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills.\par \par \uc2 "I'm hoping that this case and probably others will show that states are limited in how they can interfere with \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of drugs," Kirsten Moore, director of the Expanding Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access Project, said of the North Carolina case. "We've been trying to get lawyers to take this on."\par \par \uc2 Opponents of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have said the \uc2 FDA\uc2  's restrictions on mifepristone don't go far enough.\par \par \uc2 "We stand with the people of North Carolina and West Virginia against the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lobby's reckless push to mandate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand in every state," said Marjorie Dannenfelser, president of SBA Pro-Life America. "The \uc2 FDA\uc2  must do its job and safeguard Americans from this dire public health threat."\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood South Atlantic and other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics sued North Carolina in 2020 over the state's restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, saying they violated the rights of citizens. The groups dropped the case in December. A spokesman for one group said they decided they could better protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights through state legislation.\par \par \uc2 Write to Liz Essley Whyte at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:liz.whyte@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 liz.whyte@wsj.com  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230125ej1p002jp\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
