\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 States Weigh  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Regulations After Push for Legislation Stalls in Washington; About a dozen states have adopted near total bans on the procedure since the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 By Catherine Lucey and Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 1,018 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 January 2023\par 19:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14A push by the White House and Democratic lawmakers who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to renew protections for the procedure is expected to stall in Congress along with Republicans' efforts to further {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 limit \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That will leave the issue largely determined by states, as the Supreme Court intended when it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2  in June and ended the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Several Republican-controlled states are now pursuing new restrictions, while states under Democratic control, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pushes-some-suburban-women-in-west-michigan-toward-democrats-11666085403"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including Michigan  }}}\uc2 , are looking to protect access.\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  renewed the administration's call for national legislation to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, during a speech in Florida on Sunday marking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-roe-v-wade-50th-anniversary-11674171133"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 50th anniversary of the Roe v. Wade decision  }}}\uc2 . President Biden issued a memorandum directing cabinet and administration members to identify barriers to access to prescription medication for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and recommend actions to make sure doctors can legally prescribe and that pharmacies can dispense the medication.\par \par \uc2 "Republicans in Congress are now calling for a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, some even from the moment of conception," Ms. Harris said. "The right of every woman in every state in this country to make decisions about her own body is on the line."\par \par \uc2 Federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation doesn't have a path forward in Congress because Democrats, who largely support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, narrowly control the Senate, while Republicans, who mostly favor restrictions, hold a majority in the House. Around the country, about a dozen states have implemented near total bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other states are pursuing restrictions that are tied up in the courts.\par \par \uc2 Rep. Nancy Mace (R., S.C.) said that women from both parties in her district, including swing voters, were willing to find some middle ground on the issue.\par \par \uc2 "Everyone recognizes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up until birth is not something that they want," she said on NBC News on Sunday. "At the same time, banning all abortions with zero exceptions isn't something people support."\par \par \uc2 House Republicans recently passed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/house-passes-abortion-related-bills-in-show-of-gop-unity-11673477681"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two bills related to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , including one that requires medical care be given to infants born alive during an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The moves underscored the importance of the issue to many conservatives, though there are divides in the party following the end of a federal right to the procedure. Some have called for a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, while others have resisted, saying that the matter is best left to states. Democrats have unsuccessfully sought to advance a bill seeking to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 "Given the makeup of Congress, real change on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't in the cards. What we expect is action at the state level," said \uc2 Elizabeth Nash\uc2  , a state policy analyst at the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  , which supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Most state legislatures are now reconvening for the first time since Roe was overturned and Republican lawmakers are grappling with how far to push with new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions. Lawmakers in Virginia have proposed a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks of pregnancy. A Nebraska senator is proposing a law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after about six weeks of pregnancy. Republicans in states including North Carolina, Ohio and Florida are expected to push for further \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions. In Ohio lawmakers are weighing a total ban and in Florida legislators have discussed banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 12 weeks of pregnancy or around six weeks.\par \par \uc2 "Really it's year one for the pro-life movement because finally laws can be passed to save babies," said Marilyn Musgrave, vice president of government affairs at Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America, one of the country's largest antiabortion groups.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion activists marked the Roe anniversary with the annual March for Life on Friday in Washington, D.C., and other cities. The Women's March, which first began in 2017, held rallies in dozens of cities on Sunday with a focus on protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights at the state level.\par \par \uc2 Democrats in some states also are proposing legislation to protect access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including in Michigan, where the party won control of the legislature and governor's mansion and voters passed a measure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-supporters-prevail-in-midterm-ballot-measures-11667986139"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to enshrine a right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in the state's constitution.\par \par \uc2 The Food and Drug Administration\uc2  has expanded the availability of medication to terminate a pregnancy. In a recent move it allowed bricks-and-mortar pharmacies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pills-to-be-available-more-widely-under-new-fda-rules-11672789765"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to dispense the pills for the first time.  }}}\uc2  They have also ended a requirement that the pill must be prescribed in person and affirmed that mail-order pharmacies could dispense the medication if certified. Travel to other states for the procedure also appears to have filled some gaps in access.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What lies ahead for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access following the overturning of Roe v. Wade? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Those moves won't change the availability of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for many women, given that there are states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and others that require a physician to be physically present with a patient to prescribe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, effectively banning telehealth for abortions, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  , which tracks \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  statistics.\par \par \uc2 Republicans didn't perform as well as expected in the midterms, and political analysts and exit polling suggest that voter concern about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access was one reason why.\par \par \uc2 Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said on his social media platform that the issue was "poorly handled by many Republicans." He cited those that backed bans with no exceptions for cases such as rape, incest or life of the mother. President Biden has sought to draw a contrast with Republican policies. Mr. Biden has issued executive orders aimed at protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, including one that seeks to ensure patients get care during medical emergencies. The administration sued Idaho over the state's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, with a judge ruling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/idaho-must-allow-abortions-in-certain-emergencies-judge-rules-11661386919"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the state must provide abortions  }}}\uc2  in some emergency situations.\par \par \uc2 Stephanie Armour contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Laura Kusisto at \par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230122ej1m001rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
