\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Activists Chart Path Forward as They Mark Roe v. Wade's 50th Anniversary; Activists take to streets to shore up support for state-by-state fights now that the landmark 1973 ruling no longer stands\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 994 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 January 2023\par 23:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Antiabortion activists celebrated the end of Roe v. Wade with a March for Life through Washington, D.C., on Friday, while \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters gearing up for battles on the state level will hold a weekend of rallies.\par \par \uc2 This theme of this year's March for Life\u8212\'20\'14"Next Steps: Marching into a Post-Roe America"\u8212\'20\'14highlighted efforts to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the U.S. even after the seismic victory of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe's overturn }}}\uc2  in June. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates will hold many of their events on Sunday, the 50th anniversary of the landmark 1973 ruling.\par \par \uc2 D.C. marchers waved signs that read, "Post-Roe Generation," and "Love Life, Choose Life." March for Life events were also held in other cities.\par \par \uc2 "On one hand, it's a moment to symbolically raise the champagne glass and make a toast," said Jeanne Mancini, president of March for Life. "On the other hand, it's time to look ahead."\par \par \uc2 U.S. House\uc2  Majority Leader Steve Scalise (R., La.), U.S. Rep. Christopher Smith (R., N.J.) and Mississippi Attorney General Lynn Fitch, whose office argued the case that overturned Roe v. Wade, were among Friday's speakers in D.C.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Smith, who said he was at the first March for Life in 1974, praised the Supreme Court ruling that overturned Roe v. Wade for creating an "engraved invitation to protect life."\par \par \uc2 "What (it) did was to convey to lawmakers at the federal, state and local level to regulate or prohibit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the New Jersey lawmaker said.\par \par \uc2 For antiabortion and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights activists, state legislatures have been a primary focus since the Supreme Court's decision in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-1165608012"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended constitutional protections for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  and returned the issue to the states. More than a dozen states have enforced bans on most or nearly all abortions, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-supporters-prevail-in-midterm-ballot-measures-11667986139?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 others strengthened protections }}}\uc2 , creating a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 patchwork of access }}}\uc2  across the U.S.\par \par \uc2 President Biden said Friday that his administration will do all it can to restore women's rights to medical privacy in reproductive decisions.\par \par \uc2 "Never before has the Court taken away a right so fundamental to Americans. In doing so, it put the health and lives of women across this Nation at risk," Mr. Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The Women's March, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/demonstrators-gather-for-womens-march-a-day-after-trump-inauguration-1485006572?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which launched in 2017 }}}\uc2  following former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's inauguration, is holding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights marches in dozens of U.S. states this weekend under the theme "Bigger Than Roe." Organizers aim to build on momentum from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-supporters-prevail-in-midterm-ballot-measures-11667986139?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2022 midterm elections }}}\uc2 , when voters delivered victories to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates on ballot measures in a politically diverse mix of states.\par \par \uc2 Their main event will be held Sunday in Madison, Wis., where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is currently unavailable. A coming election will determine the makeup of the state Supreme Court, which could be key to the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 's legality in Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 Women's March organizers expect thousands of participants at events in nearly every state, with marches planned in cities including Washington; New York; Austin, Texas; St. Louis; Miami and Cincinnati.\par \par \uc2 "This is a new era of American politics that we're dealing with," said Rachel O'Leary Carmona, executive director of the Women's March. "We have to be nimble and shift our strategy."\par \par \uc2 A growing number of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/66-abortion-clinics-no-longer-provide-abortions-after-roe-overturned-study-says-11665090090"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have closed }}}\uc2  in states where bans are in place, with many moving to locations where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still legal. An influx of pregnant women have traveled across states and regions for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Local \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds, organizations that help cover the costs of abortions and travel logistics for patients, and crisis pregnancy centers, which are typically nonprofits that counsel women against having abortions, are both fundraising to manage increased demand.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-states-where-abortion-is-legal-some-cities-look-to-restrict-access-11671749172"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have trickled down to city councils }}}\uc2 , where some are exploring ways to restrict it within their communities.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups and antiabortion advocates are also keeping an eye on the federal government, with goals of passing national protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and restrictions on the procedure, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Marches and other demonstrations have historically been used to pull in more supporters and raise awareness, said Mary Ziegler, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law historian and professor at the University of California, Davis School of Law. The marches this year come as leaders reckon with where their work should focus now. And Roe's 50th anniversary serves as a touchstone for debate.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What lies ahead for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access following the overturning of Roe v. Wade? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 "It's harder to get out from the shadow of this being about Roe than I think anyone would like," Ms. Ziegler said. "There's still sort of uncertainty and contestation about what should come next."\par \par \uc2 In Wisconsin, the site of Sunday's main Women's March event, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-wake-of-roe-v-wade-ruling-abortion-providers-confront-new-landscape-11656268445"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confusion over \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access }}}\uc2  continues more than six months after the Dobbs decision. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers halted appointments shortly after the Supreme Court's June ruling, worried the state's pre-existing criminal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from 1849 could be enforced.\par \par \uc2 Gov. Tony Evers announced an effort Tuesday for an April ballot referendum asking voters whether the state should repeal the 1849 law. The Democrat's previous attempts to convene the GOP-led legislature to repeal the criminal ban have failed.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups and antiabortion activists are focused on the coming election for the state Supreme Court, which could shift its political leaning.\par \par \uc2 "We are one of the most important states in the post-Roe conversation because we are truly seeing what it looks like when \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned in a very large way," said Gracie Skogman, legislative director for Wisconsin Right to Life.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14Ginger Adams Otis contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230120ej1k001gv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
