\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 House Passes  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Related Bills in Show of GOP Unity; Republicans have been split on whether to pursue a federal ban or leave the matter to the states\b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalie Andrews \par \uc2 996 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 January 2023\par 22:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14House Republicans passed two bills related to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday, underscoring the importance of the issue to many conservatives while the party grapples with how to proceed following the Supreme Court's ruling last year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ending a federal right to the procedure  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The House voted 220 to 210, with one vote of present, on a bill that would require an infant born alive during an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to receive medical care and criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers who fail to provide medical care to born-alive infants. Federal law currently protects an infant "who is born alive at any stage of development." The House voted 222 to 209 to condemn attacks on antiabortion facilities. Both votes were largely along party lines.\par \par \uc2 The votes marked the first time Republicans have been able to bring up legislation related to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , having taken control of the chamber just last week. They come ahead of the March for Life, a national antiabortion protest set to take place in Washington on Jan. 20.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court's ruling prompted a debate among Republicans about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation. Many have called for a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, while others have resisted, saying the matter is best left to states, as it currently is. Amid those divides, the measures Wednesday showed the party united on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while not addressing the underlying fight.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills rarely make progress in Congress. Last year, the then-Democratic-controlled House passed a bill seeking to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access until a fetus is viable, or about 23 or 24 weeks, or later if it posed a health risk to the mother, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/senate-to-vote-on-abortion-access-law-as-supreme-court-weighs-roes-fate-11652274305"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the proposal stalled in the Senate  }}}\uc2 , where 60 votes are required to advance most legislation.\par \par \uc2 Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  of New York said Wednesday that the GOP bills won't receive votes in the Democratic-controlled chamber.\par \par \uc2 Republicans said the "born alive" bill was needed to protect children who survive failed abortions.\par \par \uc2 "Infants born alive after an attempted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are kids. They're children. All newborns deserve the same level of care," said Rep. Jim Jordan (R., Ohio), the chairman of the Judiciary Committee.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for Rep. \uc2 Ann Wagner\uc2  (R., Mo.), one of the leading sponsors of the bill, pointed to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/health_policy/mortality-records-mentioning-termination-of-pregnancy.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data from the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention  }}}\uc2 . According to that data, from 2003 to 2014, 143 infants were deemed to have been born alive after "spontaneous terminations of pregnancy and induced terminations of pregnancy." The data doesn't reveal the number of cases in which the mother chose to end the pregnancy because complications made it difficult for the infant to survive. It also doesn't indicate whether the babies born received medical care.\par \par \uc2 Democrats largely dismissed the need for a vote on the issue, citing existing federal law and noting that late-term abortions are rare and often because of health risks to the mother or infant.\par \par \uc2 "If there is a baby born alive, there is clear law that life has to be saved, there's no question about that," said Rep. Jan Schakowsky (D., Ill.). "In the real world, this doesn't happen."\par \par \uc2 The House also passed a resolution to condemn attacks on antiabortion facilities, groups and churches, which Rep. Mike Johnson (R., La.) said have been occurring with more frequency since the Supreme Court ruling.\par \par \uc2 "We have the opportunity before us today to start to push back against the mob that has targeted the groups and individuals that care for women and their unborn children," said Mr. Johnson.\par \par \uc2 Catherine Glenn Foster, the president and chief executive officer of \uc2 Americans United for Life\uc2  , said that 100 of the 2,700 antiabortion pregnancy centers in the country have been attacked in the past year.\par \par \uc2 Democrats said the bill was political messaging. The resolution "condemns violence at pro-life clinics but not at pro-choice clinics. That says it all," said Rep. \uc2 Jerrold Nadler\uc2  (D., N.Y.).\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access played a central role in the midterm elections. While Republicans narrowly captured the House, the failure of a "red wave" to materialize {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/frustrated-republicans-try-to-explain-lack-of-midterm-red-wave-11668036382"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 led to finger pointing  }}}\uc2  among Republican leaders and former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  . Earlier this month, Mr. Trump said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "poorly handled by many Republicans," whom he said pursued overly strict bans that lacked exceptions for rape, incest or the life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What do the votes by House Republicans indicate about the party's agenda this year? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 GOP Rep. Nancy Mace, who represents a swing district in South Carolina, characterized Wednesday's bills as unserious and said on MSNBC that she would like to see an effort to pursue legislation that balances "the rights of women and protecting the right to life," and a push for greater access to birth control and doctors.\par \par \uc2 Polling shows that views of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulation remain nuanced. By a margin of more than 2-to-1, voters in a December Wall Street Journal poll said they supported the idea of Congress passing a law that guarantees a woman's right to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Some 64% favored such a law, while 30% opposed it.\par \par \uc2 But nearly a quarter of people who favored the law, some 22%, said they would also support Congress passing a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 15 weeks except in cases where the mother's life or health are at risk. The finding suggests that some who back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are also willing to put limits on it that others find too restrictive.\par \par \uc2 Overall, 48% of voters in the survey said they would back an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban at 15 weeks with an exception for the life or health of the mother, essentially equal to the 47% who opposed the idea.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14Aaron Zitner contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Natalie Andrews at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:natalie.andrews@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 natalie.andrews@wsj.com  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230111ej1b006mx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
