\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 South Carolina's 6-Week  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban Ruled Unconstitutional; State Supreme Court ruling permanently blocks 2021 law\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 889 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 January 2023\par 00:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The South Carolina Supreme Court permanently blocked enforcement of the state's ban on most abortions after six weeks of pregnancy, ruling the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/south-carolina-passes-fetal-heartbeat-abortion-legislation-11613599308"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2021 law  }}}\uc2  violated the right to privacy in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 In a 3-2 decision Thursday, the court ruled state constitutional protections for a person's privacy included decisions about whether to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The decision marks the first major victory for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups in a state high court since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2 , ending federal constitutional protections for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 But a ruling by Idaho's Supreme Court later in the day upholding three state laws restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  highlighted divisions in the judiciary about whether state constitutions include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lawsuits-to-test-whether-state-constitutions-protect-abortion-rights-11657375200"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protections for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in the wake of the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  's decision.\par \par \uc2 Idaho's Supreme Court ruled 3-2 that there are no protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state constitution. South Carolina justices found the opposite.\par \par \uc2 "We hold that the decision to terminate a pregnancy rests upon the utmost personal and private considerations imaginable, and implicates a woman's right to privacy," South Carolina Supreme Court Justice Kaye Hearn wrote in the majority opinion.\par \par \uc2 The court said laws limiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access must also allow enough time for women to determine whether they are pregnant and get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , should they choose to get one.\par \par \uc2 "Six weeks is, quite simply, not a reasonable period of time for these two things to occur," the court wrote.\par \par \uc2 The dissenting justices said there is no historical basis for finding that the right to privacy in the state's constitution includes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Instead, the state's legislature should be empowered to decide the contours of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, they said.\par \par \uc2 "It is clear the framers did not intend to create a full panoply of privacy rights, much less the right to bodily autonomy or the right to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," wrote Justice George James.\par \par \uc2 The court's justices are appointed to 10-year terms by the state's legislature, which is currently controlled by Republicans.\par \par \uc2 House Speaker G. Murrell Smith, Jr. said Thursday's decision didn't respect the separation of powers and created "a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  where none exists." Republican Gov. \uc2 Henry McMaster\uc2  said he looked forward to working with state lawmakers "to correct this error."\par \par \uc2 The 2021 South Carolina law banned most abortions after around six weeks of pregnancy, mirroring similar so-called heartbeat bills {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/mississippi-bill-outlaws-abortion-when-heartbeat-of-fetus-is-detected-11553200766"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed by some state legislatures  }}}\uc2  several years ago. The law, like others, was previously blocked in federal court. But it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took effect  }}}\uc2  in June 2022 after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court's decision  }}}\uc2  in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups filed a new challenge in state court shortly after the ban took effect. The state Supreme Court temporarily blocked its enforcement in August 2022.\par \par \uc2 After the reversal of Roe v. Wade, roughly half of U.S. states were expected to ban many or most abortions. While access has been limited in more than a dozen states, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents in a number of other states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/state-battles-on-abortion-access-are-ahead-in-the-new-year-11670444095"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have hit legal and political obstacles  }}}\uc2  as they look to enforce new restrictions.\par \par \uc2 The South Carolina ruling guarantees that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will remain legal in the state up until about 22 weeks of pregnancy, putting the state in line with neighboring North Carolina and making it one of the few states in the South with access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the second trimester.\par \par \uc2 "Today's decision means that the right to make deeply personal healthcare decisions will remain protected in South Carolina\u8212\'20\'14an immense victory for South Carolinians and the entire region," said \uc2 Nancy Northup\uc2  , president and chief executive of the \uc2 Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How do you think access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will shift in states across the country? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 In Idaho, a majority of justices on the state Supreme Court upheld three separate laws, including one that bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Writing for the majority, Chief Justice G. Richard Bevan said there is no evidence that a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rooted in the state's history. Rather, he said, terminating a pregnancy was treated as a crime.\par \par \uc2 The duty of the judicial branch is to interpret the constitution "based on the plain and ordinary meaning of its text," the chief justice wrote. Otherwise, "the Idaho Constitution would no longer be the voice of the people of Idaho\u8212\'20\'14it would be effectively replaced by the voice of a select few sitting on this Court."\par \par \uc2 Idaho Supreme Court justices are elected in nonpartisan races.\par \par \uc2 The dissenting justices said the state's constitution has long included the right to life and safety, including the right of pregnant women to obtain abortions to protect their life or health.\par \par \uc2 "This Court's solemn duty is to protect the people and their rights from encroachment by the government. That duty has gone unfulfilled today, and it is the people of Idaho who will suffer for it," wrote Justice John Stegner.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/south-carolinas-6-week-abortion-ban-ruled-unconstitutional-11672940087"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Carolina's 6-Week \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ban Ruled Unconstitutional  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020230105ej15004jx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
