\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Doctors Can't Be Prosecuted for Abortions Under 1864 Law, Arizona Court Rules; After Roe v. Wade was overturned, state's attorney general requested the law be implemented\b0\par\par\uc2 By Associated Press \par \uc2 435 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 December 2022\par 02:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 An Arizona court has ruled that doctors performing abortions can't be prosecuted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/arizona-appeals-court-blocks-territorial-era-abortion-law-11665194904"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 under a pre-statehood law  }}}\uc2  that criminalizes nearly all abortions yet was barred from being enforced for decades.\par \par \uc2 But the Arizona Court of Appeals on Friday declined to repeal the 1864 law, which carries a sentence of two to five years in prison for anyone who assists in an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and provides no exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Still, the court said doctors can't be prosecuted for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/state-battles-on-abortion-access-are-ahead-in-the-new-year-11670444095"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 performing abortions  }}}\uc2  because other Arizona laws passed over the years allow them to perform the procedure, though nondoctors are still subject to be charged under the old law.\par \par \uc2 "The statutes, read together, make clear that physicians are permitted to perform abortions as regulated" by other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, the appeals court wrote.\par \par \uc2 The pre-statehood law, which allows abortions only if a patient's life is in jeopardy, had been blocked from being enforced shortly after the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  issued its 1973 Roe v. Wade decision guaranteeing women a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But after the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned the landmark decision  }}}\uc2  in June, Attorney General \uc2 Mark Brnovich\uc2  asked a state judge to allow the law to be implemented.\par \par \uc2 The Arizona Court of Appeals said it wasn't viewing the pre-statehood law in isolation of other state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, explaining that "the legislature has created a complex regulatory scheme to achieve its intent to restrict\u8212\'20\'14but not to eliminate\u8212\'20\'14elective abortions."\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Brittany Fonteno, president and chief executive of Planned Parenthood Arizona, said the decision means a state law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/arizona-legislature-passes-15-week-abortion-ban-11648156791"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 limiting abortions to 15 weeks  }}}\uc2  into a pregnancy will remain in place.\par \par \uc2 "The Arizona Court of Appeals has given us the clarity that Planned Parenthood Arizona has been seeking for months: When provided by licensed physicians in compliance with Arizona's other laws and regulations, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  through 15 weeks will remain legal," Ms. Fonteno said.\par \par \uc2 The appeals court rejected Mr. Brnovich's claim that doctors could be prosecuted under the pre-statehood law, saying the attorney general's argument ignores the legislature's intent to regulate but not eliminate abortions and violates due process by promoting arbitrary enforcement.\par \par \uc2 The attorney general's office didn't immediately respond to a request for comment on the decision, which was released late Friday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14Copyright 2022 Associated Press\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/doctors-cant-be-prosecuted-for-abortions-under-1864-law-arizona-court-rules-11672451850"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Doctors Can't Be Prosecuted for Abortions Under 1864 Law, Arizona Court Rules  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221231eicv0002t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
