\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Texas  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Law Still Faces Questions After Roe v. Wade's Demise; Allowing private parties to sue  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  providers for monetary damages upended judicial review\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 943 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 December 2022\par 13:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A novel Texas law caused a national stir in late 2021 by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-what-to-know-as-supreme-court-allows-it-to-take-effect-11630606238"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowing private citizens to sue \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  providers }}}\uc2  and others for monetary damages, essentially ending state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access months before the Supreme Court removed legal protections for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The law's practical significance faded this year when the high court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overruled Roe v. Wade in June }}}\uc2 , but it continues to complicate the legal landscape and inspire imitation laws, leaving questions for the courts heading into 2023.\par \par \uc2 The state law, known as the Texas Heartbeat Act, or SB 8, put ordinary citizens\u8212\'20\'14not any government official\u8212\'20\'14in charge of enforcing it, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/court-ruling-deals-near-final-blow-to-suit-challenging-texas-abortion-law-11647031457"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made it difficult to challenge in court }}}\uc2  even though it conflicted with legal protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that were in place at the time.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court declined to block the law and said a swath of state officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rules-abortion-clinics-can-challenge-texas-abortion-law-11639149404"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 couldn't be sued because they played no role }}}\uc2  in enforcement. The law allowed private citizens to sue anyone who performed an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or aided or abetted one, after about six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma and Idaho passed similar laws in the spring. Some Democrats were deeply critical of the approach and pledged to respond by adopting similar tactics to undercut legal protections valued by conservatives.\par \par \uc2 "It is a can of worms. You can see it threatens some things that Republicans and others on the right care about, like gun rights," said Ilya Somin, a professor at George Mason University's Antonin Scalia Law School.\par \par \uc2 SB 8 recently suffered a legal defeat when a Texas judge this month dismissed a lawsuit brought against an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, on the grounds that the Chicago man who sued had no harm or injury to claim and thus lacked standing under the Texas Constitution.\par \par \uc2 Still, the law remains on the books.\par \par \uc2 Now that the Supreme Court has eliminated federal constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , states are free to criminalize the procedure, lessening the motivation for antiabortion officials to adopt Texas-style workarounds involving private citizens.\par \par \uc2 But some antiabortion leaders and lawyers say private citizens could still play a role where liberal prosecutors won't enforce criminal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, or if such bans get blocked in state court. Some have also expressed interest in using private-enforcement laws to discourage groups from assisting women in obtaining out-of-state abortions.\par \par \uc2 "We've got district attorneys who are flagrantly saying they're not going to enforce the law in certain places," said Stephen Billy, vice president of state affairs at Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America, one of the country's largest antiabortion groups. "Where that's happening, civil enforcement provides another mechanism."\par \par \uc2 Since Texas passed SB 8, more than a dozen states mostly led by Democratic governors have passed laws attempting to shield doctors and others from being sued or facing other consequences for providing abortions to residents from states with bans, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation.\par \par \uc2 These protections remain largely untested. "I think they're a step in the right direction. It's just how protective are they? You don't know until there's a test case," said \uc2 Elizabeth Nash\uc2 , a state policy analyst at Guttmacher.\par \par \uc2 Democratic politicians also have pursued measures that could allow private citizens to sue gun manufacturers and fossil-fuel companies.\par \par \uc2 Over the summer, California {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/california-gun-measures-let-citizens-sue-to-enforce-regulations-11657640654"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a law giving private citizens a right to sue }}}\uc2  gun manufacturers for violating the state's firearm regulations. The law has a provision\u8212\'20\'14modeled on the Texas statute\u8212\'20\'14that makes plaintiffs who challenge the state's gun restrictions liable for the government's attorneys fees if they lose, but unable to recover their legal costs even if they prevail.\par \par \uc2 Gun owners and gun-rights groups {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.casd.743320/gov.uscourts.casd.743320.43.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have challenged the law }}}\uc2 , arguing that the fee-shifting provision is preventing them from exercising their legal rights. A federal judge agreed in a ruling on Dec. 19.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What lies ahead for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access after the overturning of Roe v. Wade? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 "A state law that threatens its citizens for questioning the legitimacy of its firearms regulations may be familiar to autocratic and tyrannical governments, but not American government," wrote U.S. District Judge Roger Benitez, an appointee of President \uc2 George W. Bush\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 California Gov. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , a Democrat, praised the decision even though he had signed the state's gun law.\par \par \uc2 "We have been saying all along that Texas' antiabortion law is outrageous. Judge Benitez just confirmed it is also unconstitutional," Mr. Newsom said. "The provision in California's law that he struck down is a replica of what Texas did."\par \par \uc2 More Democratic-led efforts modeled on Texas could be coming in 2023.\par \par \uc2 In New York, state Sen. Zellnor Myrie, a Democrat, has proposed a bill for the state's coming legislative session that would empower private citizens to sue fossil-fuel companies for their contributions to climate change, an attempt to position such claims squarely in state court and avoid some of the jurisdictional battles that have hampered climate-change litigation.\par \par \uc2 "I understand why some of my friends on this side of the aisle might feel this is a dangerous path to walk down," Mr. Myrie said. But the urgency of climate changes means "it is incumbent on every legislator that has the capacity and the ability to act," he added.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura.Kusisto@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-still-faces-questions-after-roe-v-wades-demise-11672405218"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Law Still Faces Questions After Roe v. Wade's Demise }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221230eicu001p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
