\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Glenn Youngkin, Floated as Potential 2024 Contender, First Faces Tests in 2023; Democrats have pledged to block his top two agenda items: 15-week  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban and tax cuts\b0\par\par\uc2 By Scott Calvert \par \uc2 1,156 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 December 2022\par 14:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Virginia Gov. Glenn Youngkin, viewed by some Republicans as a rising star in the party, will face a major test early next year when he tries to get a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and $1 billion tax cut package through a divided legislature, where Democrats narrowly control the Senate.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/youngkins-virginia-win-offers-midterm-road-map-for-gop-warning-for-democrats-11635942003"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans were elated }}}\uc2  when Mr. Youngkin, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/youngkin-aims-to-float-above-gop-infighting-in-virginia-11622725200?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a political newcomer }}}\uc2 , defeated Democrat \uc2 Terry McAuliffe\uc2  last year to become Virginia's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/virginia-governor-election-youngkin-results-11635884218"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first Republican elected governor }}}\uc2  since 2009. Party strategists praised him for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-glenn-youngkin-kept-trump-at-arms-length-but-on-his-side-11636057542"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 keeping Donald Trump supporters energized }}}\uc2  without making the former Republican president the focal point of the race.\par \par \uc2 A year into his term, Mr. Youngkin is trying another balancing act: notching legislative victories that require at least some Democratic support while keeping conservatives on his side.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill is perhaps his biggest challenge. Current Virginia law allows \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the end of the second trimester, or about 26 weeks, and thereafter only if the mother's life or health is at serious risk. After {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the fall of Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  earlier this year, many conservatives across the nation embraced restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws. Mr. Youngkin said he would back a bill to outlaw abortions after the first 15 weeks of pregnancy, with exceptions for rape, incest or to protect the mother's life.\par \par \uc2 "Virginians elected a pro-life governor," Mr. Youngkin said in an interview. But he suggested that outlawing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier than 15 weeks, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/doctors-struggle-with-navigating-abortion-bans-in-medical-emergencies-11665684225"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as has been done in states such as Tennessee }}}\uc2 , would be unattainable even if he wanted it, adding that he is "very aware of Virginia's overall state of politics." President Biden won Virginia by 10 percentage points in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Youngkin noted that he has gotten Democrats to help him pass his agenda before. "We got a lot done last year," he said, noting bipartisan support for such measures as the passage of $4 billion in tax cuts and salary increases for police and teachers. He hopes he can strike a deal on $1 billion more in tax cuts.\par \par \uc2 But this time around, Democratic state Sen. L. Louise Lucas, who serves as Senate president pro tempore and chairs the education and health committee, has pledged to block both of Mr. Youngkin's top 2023 agenda items. She called any changes to the state's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law a nonstarter and said the state can't afford his proposed tax cuts. Democrats have a 21-18 majority in the Senate, with one vacancy to be filled in a special election, while Republicans control the House.\par \par \uc2 "It's going to be a rough year for him," Ms. Lucas said of the governor.\par \par \uc2 An October poll by the Wason Center for Civic Leadership at \uc2 Christopher Newport University\uc2  found that 58% of registered voters oppose the Supreme Court's decision to overturn Roe v. Wade and that 67% prefer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be legal in most or all cases. At the same time, 51% said they supported or strongly supported a 15-week ban with exceptions for rape, incest and life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Lucas, though, said her caucus will line up against the measure. "We're going to crash and burn his bill," she said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Youngkin said it would take Democratic help in the Senate to pass the bill. "But I do believe that we have a reasonable chance," he said.\par \par \uc2 Half of Virginia voters approve of the job Mr. Youngkin is doing, according to the Wason Center poll. He fared better than President Biden, whose approval rating in the state was 39%. While 42% of voters said Virginia was going in the right direction, just 22% said the same of the U.S., the poll found.\par \par \uc2 The 2023 legislative session starts Jan. 11 and comes after Mr. Youngkin traveled extensively ahead of November's midterms campaigning for Republicans, several of whom lost. The trips fueled speculation he is laying groundwork for a potential 2024 presidential bid.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he is considering a White House run, he said he is concentrating on being governor. "We have a huge agenda, and I am laser-focused on delivering it," he said.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have pounced on his political travel. "It's amazing that you would fight so hard to get a job, and then a few months into that job, you're out campaigning for a new job," said state lawmaker Don Scott, the House minority leader.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Youngkin's rising profile elicited an attack from Mr. Trump, who has announced a 2024 presidential bid. "Young Kin (now that's an interesting take. Sounds Chinese, doesn't it?) in Virginia couldn't have won without me," Mr. Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/109325150085362681"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote last month on his social-media platform Truth Social }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Youngkin declined to comment on whether he thinks Mr. Trump remains the Republican Party leader and is the best candidate for the 2024 nomination.\par \par \uc2 Virginia Republicans have largely stuck by the governor, and some say he deserves credit for pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill, even if it fails.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Would you like to see Gov. Youngkin at the top of the GOP ticket in 2024? Why or why not? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 "I think he's demonstrated a way to govern and to campaign in states that may be borderline or purple," said Republican organizer \uc2 Ron Wright\uc2 . He added that part of Mr. Youngkin's test will be appeasing antiabortion lawmakers in Richmond, but added: "I don't see any other issue where he's separate from the party."\par \par \uc2 Bill Curtis, chairman of the Republican Party of Virginia Beach, who initially backed a different Republican for governor, said he supported Mr. Youngkin's 15-week bill but questions its chances of passing because of the Democrats. Overall, he said, the governor has exceeded his expectations and praised his pragmatic approach.\par \par \uc2 As well as pushing an additional $1 billion in tax cuts, Mr. Youngkin wants to boost spending in several areas. His budget plan includes more than $230 million to overhaul the state's behavioral health system, and $175 million for recruitment, expanded career pathways and bonuses for teachers, nurses and law-enforcement officers.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Lucas said she supports his proposals for higher pay for teachers and first responders but doesn't see how that would be possible with further tax cuts. "Where's the money supposed to come from?" she said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Youngkin, a former private-equity executive, said that while he expects a recession starting in the second quarter and lasting at least six months, his budget plan incorporates that possibility and allows for adjustments if revenues falter. "This is what business people do," he said, adding: "We plan for downsides and then we work for upsides."\par \par \uc2 Josh Jamerson contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Scott Calvert at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:scott.calvert@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scott.calvert@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221227eicr001jl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
