\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 In States Where  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Is Legal, Some Cities Look to Restrict Access; Local measures highlight complexity of  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  access in states after Supreme Court's decision to overturn Roe v. Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 1,161 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 December 2022\par 14:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Some city and county governments in states that allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are exploring ways to restrict it within their communities.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court's decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturning Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  in June returned the issue to the states. But a growing number of municipalities aim to create their own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations, potentially setting the stage for legal battles or conflicts with state officials.\par \par \uc2 The city-level efforts add to an increasingly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 complex patchwork of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access }}}\uc2  spilling across state borders. They also raise questions of what role, if any, cities play in determining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 "The reason we will see more and more of these is because the endgame is to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Rachel Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9, dean of \uc2 Temple University\uc2 's law school and an expert on \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-health\b0 \highlight\uc2  law. "Wherever there's a pressure point, that's going to be pushed."\par \par \uc2 The municipal maneuvering comes as more states ban or narrowly restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , prompting some clinics to move across state lines and pregnant women and girls to travel for abortions. Some local officials are responding to an increase in patients coming into their states from places with bans like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/doctors-struggle-with-navigating-abortion-bans-in-medical-emergencies-11665684225"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tennessee }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-nearly-century-old-abortion-ban-in-effect-for-now-states-high-court-says-11656780694"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/west-virginia-passes-near-total-abortion-ban-11663107167"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 West Virginia }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The city of Hobbs, N.M., just west of the Texas border, passed an ordinance in November that attempts to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics from operating there. The ordinance cites an old federal obscenity law that prohibits the mailing of medication or supplies used to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Other locales are considering similar ordinances. City council members in Pueblo, Colo., tabled a similar measure earlier this month, questioning the role cities played in regulating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . City council members in Bristol, Va., a southwestern Virginia town that shares a border with Bristol, Tenn., in October voted to move forward a zoning ordinance that would prohibit future \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics from operating in the city. Neighboring Washington County advanced a similar ordinance last week.\par \par \uc2 Some cities in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, meanwhile, have tried to establish resources and policies supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. The city council in Austin, Texas, approved a resolution in July that recommends law enforcement make the criminal enforcement of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws its lowest priority. Leaders in St. Louis in July approved an ordinance that creates a fund to help pay for logistics for those needing to travel across state lines for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Most abortions are now illegal in Missouri. The state attorney general filed a lawsuit against the city.\par \par \uc2 Recent antiabortion ordinances on the city-by-city level can be traced back to 2019. Antiabortion activist Mark Lee Dickson led an effort for Texas towns to pass ordinances {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/small-texas-cities-sued-over-abortion-bans-11582672644"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declaring themselves "sanctuary cities for the unborn }}}\uc2 ." He is taking a similar approach to other states, including New Mexico and Nebraska, tailoring the language of the ordinances to fit each city and offering pro bono legal services should they face lawsuits.\par \par \uc2 "If this worked in Texas, if this worked in New Mexico, then can't it work in Colorado? Absolutely," Mr. Dickson said. "I think it can work anywhere in America."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Dickson helped bring the idea to Hobbs leaders after he learned Whole Woman's Health, previously a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/as-new-texas-abortion-ban-law-takes-effect-providers-rush-to-adjust-11630521388"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prominent \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  provider in Texas }}}\uc2 , was considering the New Mexico city as an option for a new location. The all-male Hobbs City Commission passed the ordinance in November. Mr. Dickson describes it as a "de facto ban" on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; Hobbs leaders say it would still be possible for clinics to operate there should they get their equipment and pharmaceuticals within the state.\par \par \uc2 Ellie Rushforth, an attorney at the American Civil Liberties Union of New Mexico, said the ordinance is unconstitutional and "an impermissible exercise of municipal and county authority." She declined to say whether the organization may bring lawsuits.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic-led state legislature may bring forward legislation in January to establish more concrete \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights within the state, according to legislative leaders, which could affect if or how Hobbs can enforce its ordinance. Hobbs Mayor Sam Cobb said the city would amend its ordinance if it is in conflict with state law.\par \par \uc2 Amy Hagstrom Miller\uc2 , founder and chief executive of Whole Woman's Health, said the organization was originally looking at Hobbs and other towns close to the New Mexico-Texas border to decrease travel time for patients coming from Texas. They eventually settled on Albuquerque instead.\par \par \uc2 "It became a calculus of let's go to a place where we know we can be open, and we know we can be safe," Ms. Miller said.\par \par \uc2 In Bristol, Va., city leaders voiced concern over an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic moving across the border from neighboring Bristol, Tenn., after state laws took effect there barring the procedure. The Family Foundation of Virginia, an antiabortion group based in Richmond, helped craft a zoning ordinance taken up by the city council that prevents future \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics from opening in the area.\par \par \uc2 Victoria Cobb\uc2 , president of the Family Foundation, said she believes the Supreme Court's Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization decision opened the door for cities and counties to regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "No community wants to be advertised as the place to come to take a human life," she said.\par \par \uc2 While pushing for state lawmakers to pass statewide restrictions, the group is also focusing on getting city and county ordinances passed in southwestern Virginia. The area neighbors Tennessee and Kentucky, where the vast majority of abortions are no longer legal.\par \par \uc2 "For legislators from these areas, these efforts clarify the marching orders that accompany them when they go to the state Capitol," Ms. Cobb said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bristol City Council\uc2  voted to advance the ordinance to the city's planning commission in an October meeting, a required step before the council could give final approval. They also requested further legal input from the city attorney. Council member Kevin Wingard called Bristol "ground zero" for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and said the ordinance was a matter of "life or death."\par \par \uc2 It is unclear if or when the city's planning commission will take it up. Randall Eads, Bristol's city attorney and city manager, declined to disclose the advice he gave the council in November but said the ordinance raises several legal issues.\par \par \uc2 Debate over the role a city should play in regulating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  also flared up in one Colorado town, after the state earlier this year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-providers-in-illinois-colorado-and-florida-prepare-for-patient-influx-if-roe-is-overturned-11655560800"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a law }}}\uc2  protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. The Pueblo City Council took up and then tabled an ordinance designed by Mr. Dickson that was similar to the measure passed in Hobbs.\par \par \uc2 "It can only be assumed this ordinance is being used as a political ploy, as it never should've reached this point," said Pueblo City Council President Heather Graham as she motioned to table the ordinance last week.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221223eicn0020a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
