\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Record Number of Women Were Elected Governor in 2022; Some have gotten attention as possible presidential hopefuls\b0\par\par\uc2 By Catherine Lucey \par \uc2 1,401 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 November 2022\par 16:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14A record number of women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/few-state-governor-races-result-in-change-of-control-11668024031"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were elected as governors }}}\uc2  in the midterm elections, with female candidates from both parties winning executive roles that have historically been challenging for women to secure.\par \par \uc2 A total of 12 women\u8212\'20\'14eight Democrats and four Republicans\u8212\'20\'14won bids for governor in 2022. Of that group, eight already held the title and four were newcomers. The previous high-water mark of nine women serving as governor at the same time was set in 2004, according to the Center for American Women and Politics at \uc2 Rutgers University\uc2 , which researches women in politics and runs programs aimed at boosting participation.\par \par \uc2 Republican \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2  became the first woman elected governor of Arkansas. Democrat \uc2 Maura Healey\uc2  was the first woman elected as governor of Massachusetts. Democrat \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , who took office after Gov. \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  resigned last year, is the first woman elected governor of New York. Ms. Healey and Democrat \uc2 Tina Kotek\uc2  of Oregon are the nation's first openly lesbian governors.\par \par \uc2 Democratic pollster Celinda Lake said voters are now more likely to see women as leaders. "Nobody questions whether they can lead," she said.\par \par \uc2 The increase in women winning governorships follows decades of work by outside groups, as well as efforts by the political parties, to train and recruit women to run for office, said \uc2 Debbie Walsh\uc2 , director of CAWP. She said that has contributed to more women winning state-level positions that help pave the way for a bid for governor.\par \par \uc2 Most of the women who won in 2022 were already serving as governor, including Ms. Hochul, who had previously been lieutenant governor of New York. Of the four who are new to the job, Ms. Healey, Ms. Kotek and Democrat \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democrat-katie-hobbs-defeats-kari-lake-in-high-profile-arizona-governor-race-11668479658"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won in Arizona }}}\uc2 , all recently held prominent state offices. Ms. Sanders was a household name who served in former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's White House and is the daughter of former Arkansas Gov. \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 More women ran for governor in 2022 than ever before. A total of 69 women ran in the primaries as major party candidates this year, beating the previous high of 61. Of those, 25 women became their parties' nominees, above the previous high of 16.\par \par \uc2 In states like Michigan, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oregon-might-elect-a-republican-governor-for-first-time-in-four-decades-11666863003"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oregon }}}\uc2  and Arizona, both major party candidates for governor were women. The contest in Arizona pitted Ms. Hobbs against former television news anchor Kari Lake, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kari-lake-unites-many-arizona-republicans-after-partys-earlier-divisions-over-trump-11666690203"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an ally of Mr. Trump }}}\uc2  and one of the most prominent candidates falsely claiming the 2020 presidential election was stolen. She has also filed a lawsuit against Maricopa County officials related to the 2022 results.\par \par \uc2 In some states with close races, women running as Democrats likely got a boost from voters concerned about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the wake of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Supreme Court overturning Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 . Ms. Hochul focused her campaign on the topic. In Michigan, voters passed a ballot measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution and re-elected Gov. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kansas Gov. Laura Kelly narrowly won re-election after voters in her state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-abortion-vote-results-11659440554"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected a proposed amendment to the state constitution }}}\uc2  that would have ended protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She beat Republican Attorney General Derek Schmidt, who said that he opposed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but that the results of the referendum should be respected.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Lake, the pollster, said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an issue on which Democratic women are seen as strong.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Walsh of CAWP said that while the gains for women in this election were significant, there is still work to be done to advance all women in politics. She noted that the majority of the women who have been elected are white and that no Black women have ever been elected as governors.\par \par \uc2 CAWP is among the groups that have worked to get more women to run for office, running nonpartisan trainings in New Jersey and with partners around the country for decades. Organizations that recruit and support Democratic women include Emily's List, which raises money for Democratic women who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, and Emerge, which provides trainings. For Republican women, the National Federation of Republican Women offers training programs. The trainings can cover skills like fundraising, talking to the media and political strategy.\par \par \uc2 There are 147 women in the current Congress out of 535 seats, according to CAWP. Women have made gains in other fields as well. The number of women leading Fortune 500 companies hit a record high of 44 this year.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What does the election of 12 women governors mean for the political landscape? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Women who have served in top roles say that electing women often motivates others to run for office and can lead to more women appointed to key positions.\par \par \uc2 "I like to think the fact that I served, even if it was in the 1990s, it at least set a pattern that voters could look at and see that women could do the job," said Democrat Barbara Roberts, who was elected Oregon's first female governor in 1991. Ms. Kotek will be its third female governor.\par \par \uc2 Some of the women elected this year have gotten attention as possible presidential hopefuls, such as Ms. Whitmer, who won in what had been expected to be a difficult year for Democrats, and Ms. Sanders, who has a strong national profile. Both said their focus was on their current roles. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
