\par \par \uc2 Democrat \uc2 Tina Kotek\uc2  was elected governor of Oregon after a competitive race in the left-leaning state. PHOTO: Kristina Barker for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 "Governors can make great presidents," said Commerce Secretary \uc2 Gina Raimondo\uc2 , who in 2014 became the first woman elected governor of Rhode Island. She stepped down to join President Biden's administration. "Having more women with executive leadership, experience in government and business, it is a good thing." The Democrat, who has been discussed as a possible presidential candidate or Treasury secretary, said she is happy in her current role and supports Mr. Biden, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/as-biden-turns-80-some-democrats-see-age-as-issue-for-potential-2024-bid-11668917528"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said he intends to run for re-election }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While 17 former governors have been president, a governor hasn't won the White House since former President \uc2 George W. Bush\uc2 , who was first elected in 2000 after serving as governor of Texas. The only woman to be a major party nominee for president, \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , had served in the Senate, but not as governor. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  also has Senate, but not gubernatorial, experience.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Sanders said that she wanted people to vote based on her qualifications and that she connected with voters as a mother of young children. Ms. Sanders featured her children in campaign ads, including one showing her son learning that money he earned doing chores wasn't enough to cover his purchases at the grocery store due to inflation.\par \par \uc2 "Everywhere we went we had moms that came up that felt like they could connect," she said. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
