\par \par \uc2 Michigan Gov. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  won re-election. She focused on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in her campaign. PHOTO: Emily Elconin for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, Ms. Whitmer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pushes-some-suburban-women-in-west-michigan-toward-democrats-11666085403"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access a centerpiece of her campaign }}}\uc2 , talking about her experience as a victim of sexual assault and her concerns about her college-aged daughters. She also talked about being a caregiver to her daughters and her late mother.\par \par \uc2 "I believe that there was a point in time where being a mom was probably not a strength for a candidate or for an officeholder," Ms. Whitmer said. "I think that mom cred has value now."\par \par \uc2 Women from both parties said they brought their own perspective to the role.\par \par \uc2 After \uc2 Christine Todd Whitman\uc2  was elected governor of New Jersey in 1993, she was the only female governor in the country for a time. One of her early pieces of legislation required insurance companies to extend the time women could stay in the hospital after giving birth.\par \par \uc2 "White males don't have all the right answers," said Ms. Whitman, a longtime Republican who recently co-founded a centrist third party called the Forward Party.\par \par \uc2 Write to Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 Democrat \uc2 Maura Healey\uc2  was the first woman elected as governor of Massachusetts. An earlier version of this article incorrectly said Ms. Healey will be the first woman to serve as governor of Massachusetts.(Corrected on Nov. 26)\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221126eibq00107\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw25