\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Georgia's Six-Week  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban Reinstated by State Supreme Court; Court granted request for emergency order from state attorney general's office, which appealed a lower court ruling last week blocking the law\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 683 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 November 2022\par 19:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Georgia Supreme Court allowed the state's ban on most abortions after six weeks of pregnancy to once again take effect, reversing a lower court's ruling that blocked enforcement of the 2019 law last week.\par \par \uc2 The justices on Wednesday granted a request for an emergency order brought by the state's attorney general's office. The state had quickly appealed the decision of Judge Robert McBurney of the Superior Court of Fulton County that allowed clinics in the state to resume appointments after six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Judge McBurney's ruling on Nov. 15 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgias-abortion-ban-after-six-weeks-is-blocked-11668540794"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 permanently blocked enforcement  }}}\uc2  of the state's six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, finding the 2019 law was clearly unlawful at the time the state legislature passed it.\par \par \uc2 In his order, Judge McBurney said there has been a sea change in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law following the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  's ruling in June that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2  and ended federal constitutional protections for the procedure. He didn't rule on whether an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban passed in the future would violate the state's constitution, noting that the legislature could revisit the issue and pass a new law.\par \par \uc2 Georgia's ban on most abortions after six weeks of pregnancy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgia-six-week-abortion-ban-goes-into-effect-11658352186"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took effect in July  }}}\uc2 , about a month after the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  's decision in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization. The high court's ruling shifted questions about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 's legality back to the states, creating a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 patchwork of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access  }}}\uc2  across the country in the months following the decision.\par \par \uc2 The Georgia law bans most abortions after " {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgia-abortion-restrictions-spark-new-debate-over-claims-to-fetal-personhood-11661601601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a detectable human heartbeat  }}}\uc2 ," with exceptions for medical emergencies, instances of rape and incest that have been reported to law enforcement, and if the fetus isn't medically viable.\par \par \uc2 Gov. \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  , a Republican who was re-elected earlier this month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgia-governor-signs-fetal-heartbeat-abortion-law-11557266086"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed the law  }}}\uc2  in 2019. At the time, Georgia was one of several states to pass so-called heartbeat bills. It was blocked in federal court before the overturning of Roe.\par \par \uc2 Kara Richardson, a spokesperson for the \uc2 Georgia Attorney General's Office\uc2  , said the office was pleased with the court's action but couldn't comment further because of the pending appeal.\par \par \uc2 The attorney general's office, in its appeal, argued the state suffered "significant and irreparable" harm while enforcement of the law remained blocked.\par \par \uc2 "Unborn children are at risk every day that the injunction continues," it said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups and providers countered that the ban's continued enforcement would harm women who would face severe medical risks or be forced to carry a pregnancy to term without \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an option.\par \par \uc2 They also said the state couldn't claim the lower court's order caused irreparable harm, as Judge McBurney made clear the state legislature could pass a similar ban again, now that Roe is no longer in place.\par \par \uc2 "It is cruel that our patients' ability to access the \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care they need has been taken away yet again," Kwajelyn Jackson, executive director of Feminist Women's Health Center, said in a statement Wednesday. "For the second time this year, we are being forced to turn away those in need of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care beyond six weeks of pregnancy."\par \par \uc2 About a dozen states have enforced bans on nearly all abortions in the months since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  's decision. The legal battles that followed have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/doctors-struggle-with-navigating-abortion-bans-in-medical-emergencies-11665684225"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 created an uncertain  }}}\uc2  and shifting landscape for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and patients in some places, prompting some clinics to open and close their doors more than once.\par \par \uc2 State courts continue to consider whether state constitutions protect the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an argument \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups have made in their challenges to the bans. Lawmakers in a handful of states, meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/state-abortion-bans-face-obstacles-as-republicans-clash-11660908536"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are wrestling  }}}\uc2  with whether and to what to extent to regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221123eibn003ux\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 rst=wsjo AND (abortion OR "reproductive rights" OR "reproductive health") AND (atleast5(abortion) OR atleast3("reproductive rights"))\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Date\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/2021 to 06/30/2026\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbr